{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T11:23:03.912Z","ordinal":16105,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0987d0060851d607016accc30d7bf4819182f2f35d13db2c14","status":"completed","call_id":"call_fbe0b727b02e4fe0b1963911ffbc0761","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh pr create --base main --head ao/neatlogs-hack-5/release-020 --title 'Prepare tally-agents 0.2.0 and fix AO readiness checks' --body '## Summary\\n- Bump npm manifest, lockfile and CLI version together to 0.2.0; test they agree.\\n- Accept the actual healthy AO status payload (state ready, health ok, ready ready), preserving legacy running/stopped support. Live doctor now reports connected.\\n- Fix fallback-test timing flake: independent consumer checks, real AO binary resolution, unrelated prerequisites faked; unchanged timeout and temp cleanup.\\n- Add a published 0.1.0-init-shaped fixture and loop test: unchanged legacy concurrency 3 still executes sequentially, without parallelWorkers or modelAccessFallbackTier.\\n- Document Node 20 runtime separately from Vitest 5 development requirement and next-version config compatibility.\\n\\n## Verification\\n827 tests pass in two consecutive final full-suite runs; typecheck/build clean. Built CLI version 0.2.0 and seven-task dry demo run on Node 20.20.2. Healthy daemon reproduced read-only and doctor confirmed connected. No paid workers, no npm publication.\\n\\n## Release gate\\nAfter merge, pack and audit only the release branch built at the final commit; empty-cache clean-prefix installation checks still pending. Maintainer publishes with 2FA only after lane A final AO sanity run. No claim of a published 0.2.0 yet.'\",\"sandbox_permissions\":\"require_escalated\",\"justification\":\"Open the approved small version and known-defect PR for gating before final release packaging.\",\"max_output_tokens\":500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12fce-a573-76b3-a414-d175a23cff76","create_time":1791804173.4929166}}}
