{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T11:23:10.517Z","ordinal":16107,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a12fce-a573-76b3-a414-d175a23cff76","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-024fa02a-4a87-4d50-b501-3b20f5f3591b","process_id":"21549","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr create --base main --head ao/neatlogs-hack-5/release-020 --title 'Prepare tally-agents 0.2.0 and fix AO readiness checks' --body '## Summary\n- Bump npm manifest, lockfile and CLI version together to 0.2.0; test they agree.\n- Accept the actual healthy AO status payload (state ready, health ok, ready ready), preserving legacy running/stopped support. Live doctor now reports connected.\n- Fix fallback-test timing flake: independent consumer checks, real AO binary resolution, unrelated prerequisites faked; unchanged timeout and temp cleanup.\n- Add a published 0.1.0-init-shaped fixture and loop test: unchanged legacy concurrency 3 still executes sequentially, without parallelWorkers or modelAccessFallbackTier.\n- Document Node 20 runtime separately from Vitest 5 development requirement and next-version config compatibility.\n\n## Verification\n827 tests pass in two consecutive final full-suite runs; typecheck/build clean. Built CLI version 0.2.0 and seven-task dry demo run on Node 20.20.2. Healthy daemon reproduced read-only and doctor confirmed connected. No paid workers, no npm publication.\n\n## Release gate\nAfter merge, pack and audit only the release branch built at the final commit; empty-cache clean-prefix installation checks still pending. Maintainer publishes with 2FA only after lane A final AO sanity run. No claim of a published 0.2.0 yet.'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr create --base main --head ao/neatlogs-hack-5/release-020 --title 'Prepare tally-agents 0.2.0 and fix AO readiness checks' --body '## Summary\n- Bump npm manifest, lockfile and CLI version together to 0.2.0; test they agree.\n- Accept the actual healthy AO status payload (state ready, health ok, ready ready), preserving legacy running/stopped support. Live doctor now reports connected.\n- Fix fallback-test timing flake: independent consumer checks, real AO binary resolution, unrelated prerequisites faked; unchanged timeout and temp cleanup.\n- Add a published 0.1.0-init-shaped fixture and loop test: unchanged legacy concurrency 3 still executes sequentially, without parallelWorkers or modelAccessFallbackTier.\n- Document Node 20 runtime separately from Vitest 5 development requirement and next-version config compatibility.\n\n## Verification\n827 tests pass in two consecutive final full-suite runs; typecheck/build clean. Built CLI version 0.2.0 and seven-task dry demo run on Node 20.20.2. Healthy daemon reproduced read-only and doctor confirmed connected. No paid workers, no npm publication.\n\n## Release gate\nAfter merge, pack and audit only the release branch built at the final commit; empty-cache clean-prefix installation checks still pending. Maintainer publishes with 2FA only after lane A final AO sanity run. No claim of a published 0.2.0 yet.'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/147\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/147\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":824231292},"formatted_output":"https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/147\n"},"started_at_ms":1791804187693,"completed_at_ms":1791804190517}}
