u001b[0m █\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K    █  \\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▄\\u001b[0m\\u001b[48;2;226;88;34m▀\\u001b[0m\\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▀▀\\u001b[0m █   █\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K   \\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▄\\u001b[0m\\u001b[48;2;226;88;34m▀\\u001b[0m\\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▀▀\\u001b[0m █   █   █\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K \\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▀▀\\u001b[0m █   █   █   █\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K    █   █   █   █\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K    █   █   █   ▀\\r\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"88955f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.046137333,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2120,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2120)\\nTotal output lines: 66\\n\\nBudget availability\\n  Monthly remaining: $40.00 of $40.00 (tally.yaml)\\n  Run cap: $40.00 (tally.yaml)\\n  Available now: $40.00\\nT1: small (confidence 0.75) -> cheap claude-code/nova-micro ceiling $0.20\\n  No usable history exists for cheap on small, so it uses the prior; small task with 1 file touched, no dependents and tests present starts on cheap capped at $0.20, expected to cost $0.50 against $1.00 for going straight to top; top none: 0 observations, prior 95% pass rate and $1.00 average cost, uses the prior, config cap $1.00 (0 successful samples; 5 needed), model claude-opus-4.6 only (unknown-model observations excluded); cheap none: 0 observations, prior 70% pass rate and $0.20 average cost, uses the prior, config cap $0.20 (0 successful samples; 5 needed), model nova-micro only (unknown-model observations excluded); middle none: 0 observations, prior 83% pass rate and $0.50 average cost, uses the prior, config cap $0.50 (0 successful samples; 5 needed), model claude-sonnet-4.6 only (unknown-model observations excluded).\\nT1 attempt 1: worker dry-T1-1 started on cheap\\nT1 attempt 1: spend $0.00\\nT1 attempt 1: passed $0.00066\\nT2: small (confidence 0.75) -> cheap claude-code/nova-micro ceiling $0.20\\n  History has only 1 cheap attempt for small, so it uses the prior; small task with 1 file touched, no dependents and tests present starts on cheap capped at $0.20, expected to cost …1420 tokens truncated…-4.6 only (unknown-model observations excluded); cheap none: 0 observations, prior 20% pass rate and $2.00 average cost, uses the prior, config cap $2.00 (0 successful samples; 5 needed), model nova-micro only (unknown-model observations excluded); middle none: 0 observations, prior 52% pass rate and $5.00 average cost, uses the prior, config cap $5.00 (0 successful samples; 5 needed), model claude-sonnet-4.6 only (unknown-model observations excluded).\\nT7 attempt 1: worker dry-T7-1 started on top\\nT7 attempt 1: spend $0.00\\nT7 attempt 1: failed $0.4913 (The task is not solvable without scope and tax-policy inputs.)\\nwrote /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/scratch/.tally/runs/run-20261012-112832Z/run.json\\nwrote /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/scratch/.tally/runs/run-20261012-112832Z/ledger.json\\nupdated /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/scratch/.tally/runs/latest\\nfinished run-20261012-112832Z: 7 tasks, 9 attempts\\nIntegrations\\n  Integration  Status\\n  Neatlogs     off\\n  Entire       off\\n  cfo.ai       off\\n  GitHub       off\\n    Backlog loaded from file.\\n  Slack        off\\nRun summary\\n  Tasks: 6 passed, 1 failed, 0 skipped\\n  Total spend: $1.7063\\n  Run cap: $40.00\\nBudget availability\\n  Monthly remaining: $38.2937 of $40.00 (tally.yaml)\\n  Run cap: $40.00 (tally.yaml)\\n  Available now: $38.2937\\nrun folder /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/scratch/.tally/runs/run-20261012-112832Z\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"904a31\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.038761042,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":835,\"output\":\"tally: a CFO for a fleet of coding agents\\n\\nUsage: tally <command> [options]\\n\\nCommands:\\n  experiment Run baseline and Tally repeats with a shared safety budget\\n  run      Run the backlog against the budget in tally.yaml\\n  demo     Run the full loop with simulated workers on a sample backlog\\n  dashboard Start the local dashboard server\\n  init     Set up tally.yaml for the current repository\\n  uninstall List and remove the recorded Tally installation\\n  doctor   Check that each integration is connected\\n  login    Connect an integration, e.g. tally login cfoai\\n  market   Find and qualify likely pilot companies with CrustData\\n  publish  Write a static dashboard bundle (does not deploy)\\n  traces drain --run <id> Drain and read-back verify a finished run's worker traces\\n  logo     Replay the Tally logo animation\\n\\nOptions:\\n  --repeats <N>     Repeats per experiment mode (default: 2)\\n  --config <path>   Path to tally.yaml (default: tally.yaml)\\n  --dry-run         Simulate workers; spends nothing\\n  --budget <usd>    Override the budget for this run\\n  --only <task>     Run a single task\\n  --parallel <N>    Opt into up to N AO workers (default: 1; direct is sequential)\\n  --baseline        Send every task to the strongest tier\\n  --dashboard       Serve the dashboard before run/demo; keep serving until Ctrl+C\\n  --open            Also open the dashboard in the browser\\n  --port <number>   Dashboard port (default: 5177; use 0 for any free port)\\n  --plan            Size and route tasks, but do not spawn workers\\n  --live            For demo: use live read-only integrations with fake workers\\n  --yes             Approve init changes or explicitly budgeted paid experiments\\n  --test-command <cmd> For init: verification shell command\\n  --setup-command <cmd> For init: setup shell command (empty means none)\\n  --issue-label <label> For init: GitHub issue label (default: tally)\\n  --neatlogs <yes|no> --entire <yes|no> --cfoai <yes|no> Init product opt-ins\\n  --verbose         For init: include the full proposed YAML\\n  --runner <ao|direct> For init: AO workers or sequential direct workers\\n  --harness <claude-code|codex|mixed> For init: explicit coding agent choice\\n  --model-access-fallback-tier <name> For init: one budget-checked retry after explicit model denial\\n  --allow-claude     For init: explicitly consent to the printed repository allow-list\\n  --output <dir>    Output directory for tally market (default: .tally/market/latest)\\n  --limit <number>  Result limit for tally market (default: 10)\\n  --keyword <text>  Optional exact description phrase for tally market\\n  --max-credits <N> Market estimated credit cap (default: 10); refuses above cap\\n  --replay <query.json> Replay cached market snapshot; no API calls\\n  --review <json>   Apply human review labels to a cached market snapshot\\n  --jobs            Search engineering job posts for explicit coding-tool evidence\\n  --secondary <query.json> Include a cached firmographic table in the job report\\n                    market --plan checks free account pricing, without a search\\n  --out <dir>       New directory for tally publish (required)\\n  --runs <ids>      Comma-separated run folder ids (default: all real runs)\\n  --run <id>        Run id for traces drain; --output overrides its run directory\\n  -h, --help        Show this help\\n  -v, --version     Show the version\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12fdc-361d-7d60-86d2-5cd5884aa9f4","create_time":1791804513.229613}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
