own-model observations excluded); cheap none: 0 observations, prior 70% pass rate and $0.20 average cost, uses the prior, config cap $0.20 (0 successful samples; 5 needed), model nova-micro only (unknown-model observations excluded); middle none: 0 observations, prior 83% pass rate and $0.50 average cost, uses the prior, config cap $0.50 (0 successful samples; 5 needed), model claude-sonnet-4.6 only (unknown-model observations excluded).\\nT1 attempt 1: worker dry-T1-1 started on cheap\\nT1 attempt 1: spend $0.00\\nT1 attempt 1: passed $0.00066\\nT2: small (confidence 0.75) -\u003e cheap claude-code/nova-micro ceiling $0.20\\n  History has only 1 cheap attempt for small, so it uses the prior; small task with 1 file touched, no dependents and tests present starts on cheap capped at $0.20, expected to cost …1420 tokens truncated…-4.6 only (unknown-model observations excluded); cheap none: 0 observations, prior 20% pass rate and $2.00 average cost, uses the prior, config cap $2.00 (0 successful samples; 5 needed), model nova-micro only (unknown-model observations excluded); middle none: 0 observations, prior 52% pass rate and $5.00 average cost, uses the prior, config cap $5.00 (0 successful samples; 5 needed), model claude-sonnet-4.6 only (unknown-model observations excluded).\\nT7 attempt 1: worker dry-T7-1 started on top\\nT7 attempt 1: spend $0.00\\nT7 attempt 1: failed $0.4913 (The task is not solvable without scope and tax-policy inputs.)\\nwrote /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/scratch/.tally/runs/run-20261012-112832Z/run.json\\nwrote /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/scratch/.tally/runs/run-20261012-112832Z/ledger.json\\nupdated /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/scratch/.tally/runs/latest\\nfinished run-20261012-112832Z: 7 tasks, 9 attempts\\nIntegrations\\n  Integration  Status\\n  Neatlogs     off\\n  Entire       off\\n  cfo.ai       off\\n  GitHub       off\\n    Backlog loaded from file.\\n  Slack        off\\nRun summary\\n  Tasks: 6 passed, 1 failed, 0 skipped\\n  Total spend: $1.7063\\n  Run cap: $40.00\\nBudget availability\\n  Monthly remaining: $38.2937 of $40.00 (tally.yaml)\\n  Run cap: $40.00 (tally.yaml)\\n  Available now: $38.2937\\nrun folder /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/scratch/.tally/runs/run-20261012-112832Z\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"904a31\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.038761042,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":835,\"output\":\"tally: a CFO for a fleet of coding agents\\n\\nUsage: tally \u003ccommand\u003e [options]\\n\\nCommands:\\n  experiment Run baseline and Tally repeats with a shared safety budget\\n  run      Run the backlog against the budget in tally.yaml\\n  demo     Run the full loop with simulated workers on a sample backlog\\n  dashboard Start the local dashboard server\\n  init     Set up tally.yaml for the current repository\\n  uninstall List and remove the recorded Tally installation\\n  doctor   Check that each integration is connected\\n  login    Connect an integration, e.g. tally login cfoai\\n  market   Find and qualify likely pilot companies with CrustData\\n  publish  Write a static dashboard bundle (does not deploy)\\n  traces drain --run \u003cid\u003e Drain and read-back verify a finished run's worker traces\\n  logo     Replay the Tally logo animation\\n\\nOptions:\\n  --repeats \u003cN\u003e     Repeats per experiment mode (default: 2)\\n  --config \u003cpath\u003e   Path to tally.yaml (default: tally.yaml)\\n  --dry-run         Simulate workers; spends nothing\\n  --budget \u003cusd\u003e    Override the budget for this run\\n  --only \u003ctask\u003e     Run a single task\\n  --parallel \u003cN\u003e    Opt into up to N AO workers (default: 1; direct is sequential)\\n  --baseline        Send every task to the strongest tier\\n  --dashboard       Serve the dashboard before run/demo; keep serving until Ctrl+C\\n  --open            Also open the dashboard in the browser\\n  --port \u003cnumber\u003e   Dashboard port (default: 5177; use 0 for any free port)\\n  --plan            Size and route tasks, but do not spawn workers\\n  --live            For demo: use live read-only integrations with fake workers\\n  --yes             Approve init changes or explicitly budgeted paid experiments\\n  --test-command \u003ccmd\u003e For init: verification shell command\\n  --setup-command \u003ccmd\u003e For init: setup shell command (empty means none)\\n  --issue-label \u003clabel\u003e For init: GitHub issue label (default: tally)\\n  --neatlogs \u003cyes|no\u003e --entire \u003cyes|no\u003e --cfoai \u003cyes|no\u003e Init product opt-ins\\n  --verbose         For init: include the full proposed YAML\\n  --runner \u003cao|direct\u003e For init: AO workers or sequential direct workers\\n  --harness \u003cclaude-code|codex|mixed\u003e For init: explicit coding agent choice\\n  --model-access-fallback-tier \u003cname\u003e For init: one budget-checked retry after explicit model denial\\n  --allow-claude     For init: explicitly consent to the printed repository allow-list\\n  --output \u003cdir\u003e    Output directory for tally market (default: .tally/market/latest)\\n  --limit \u003cnumber\u003e  Result limit for tally market (default: 10)\\n  --keyword \u003ctext\u003e  Optional exact description phrase for tally market\\n  --max-credits \u003cN\u003e Market estimated credit cap (default: 10); refuses above cap\\n  --replay \u003cquery.json\u003e Replay cached market snapshot; no API calls\\n  --review \u003cjson\u003e   Apply human review labels to a cached market snapshot\\n  --jobs            Search engineering job posts for explicit coding-tool evidence\\n  --secondary \u003cquery.json\u003e Include a cached firmographic table in the job report\\n                    market --plan checks free account pricing, without a search\\n  --out \u003cdir\u003e       New directory for tally publish (required)\\n  --runs \u003cids\u003e      Comma-separated run folder ids (default: all real runs)\\n  --run \u003cid\u003e        Run id for traces drain; --output overrides its run directory\\n  -h, --help        Show this help\\n  -v, --version     Show the version\\n\"}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"content":null,"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0c048985e5fd68d5016accc46411c087d0abbc391ac5430bd7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12fdc-361d-7d60-86d2-5cd5884aa9f4"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_ayzRWZwxIvVHWDI5WKYSFJNw","id":"ctc_0c048985e5fd68d5016accc46e547087d091fa1d6707e680d2","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"node --input-type=module -e 'import {readFileSync,writeFileSync} from \\\"node:fs\\\";import {parse,stringify} from \\\"/private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/prefix/lib/node_modules/tally-agents/node_modules/yaml/dist/index.js\\\";const dir=\\\"/private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/scratch\\\";const cfg=parse(readFileSync(\\\"/private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/release/demo/tally.yaml\\\",\\\"utf8\\\"));cfg.runner=\\\"ao\\\";cfg.parallelWorkers=2;cfg.modelAccessFallbackTier=\\\"middle\\\";delete cfg.concurrency;writeFileSync(dir+\\\"/tally.yaml\\\",stringify(cfg));writeFileSync(dir+\\\"/sample-backlog.yaml\\\",readFileSync(\\\"/private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/release/demo/sample-backlog.yaml\\\"));console.log(\\\"Generated isolated plan config with parallelWorkers: 2 and modelAccessFallbackTier: middle.\\\");'\",\"max_output_tokens\":500}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"env HOME=/private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/home TALLY_NO_ANIMATION=1 /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/prefix/bin/tally run --plan --config tally.yaml\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/scratch\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":600}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"env HOME=/private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/home TALLY_NO_ANIMATION=1 /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/prefix/bin/tally market --replay /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/market-job-intent/query.json --output /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/market-replay\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/scratch\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":600}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"env HOME=/private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/home TALLY_NO_ANIMATION=1 /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/prefix/bin/tally doctor\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/scratch\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":700}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:81533,chars:\"\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":600}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:30880,chars:\"\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791804514.045723,"turn_id":"01a12fdc-361d-7d60-86d2-5cd5884aa9f4"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_ayzRWZwxIvVHWDI5WKYSFJNw","guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000},"id":"ctco_01a12fdf-9545-7c52-8bd6-e8704432d9c5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791804544.325473,"turn_id":"01a12fdc-361d-7d60-86d2-5cd5884aa9f4"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 6.2 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"7401f5\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.0000095,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":23,\"output\":\"Generated isolated plan config with parallelWorkers: 2 and modelAccessFallbackTier: middle.\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"91291b\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.026985042,\"exit_code\":2,\"original_token_count\":161,\"output\":\"Budget availability\\n  Monthly remaining: $40.00 of $40.00 (tally.yaml)\\n  Run cap: $40.00 (tally.yaml)\\n  Available now: $40.00\\nPlanning tasks. Enabled history reads are bounded. No workers will start.\\ntally run: tally.yaml: repo.aoProject is required for real runs so AO knows where to spawn workers; tiers[0].sessionMode is required for real runs; set sessionMode: tui after proving the harness can run unattended; tiers[1].sessionMode is required for real runs; set sessionMode: tui after proving the harness can run unattended; tiers[2].sessionMode is required for real runs; set sessionMode: tui after proving the harness can run unattended\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"b0daa0\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00000525,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":105,\"output\":\"wrote /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/market-replay/query.json\\nwrote /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/market-replay/companies.json\\nwrote /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/market-replay/companies.csv\\nwrote /private/tmp/tally-020-check.cbXeWd/market-replay/report.md\\nmarket: 20 returned prospects; 35030 API query matches (not adoption or market size)\\ncredits: 0.75 originally; cached replay made no API calls\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"d234dd\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.146598208,\"exit_code\":1,\"original_token_count\":381,\"output\":\"AO daemon: broken\\n  AO status did not report a running or stopped state\\n  Next: check the AO installation and run ao status --json\\nAO worker auto mode: missing\\n  repo.aoProject is required before Tally can check worker permissions\\n  Next: add repo.aoProject to tally.yaml\\nAO setup post-create: missing\\n  repo.aoProject is required before Tally can check setup post-create\\n  Next: add repo.aoProject to tally.yaml\\nClaude Code: broken\\n  claude is signed out or its sign-in status could not be verified\\n  Next: claude auth login\\nConfigured model access: unverified\\n  Model access is unverified. Harness sign-in does not prove these models are available. Tally does not send a model request before a run. Configured tiers: cheap (claude-code: nova-micro), middle (claude-code: claude-sonnet-4.6), top (claude-code: claude-opus-4.6).\\n  Next: Check model access with the configured accounts. Update tiers[].model in tally.yaml for any model they reject.\\nClaude Code allow-list consent: missing\\n  Claude Code worker allow-list has not been approved for these test/setup commands.\\n  Next: tally init\\nGitHub CLI: broken\\n  gh command failed (1); check the command in your terminal before retrying.\\n  Next: gh auth login\\nEntire CLI: off\\n  Disabled in tally.yaml. This integration is not required.\\nEntire graph plugin: off\\n  Disabled in tally.yaml. This integration is not required.\\nNeatlogs key: off\\n  Disabled in tally.yaml. This integration is not required.\\ncfo.ai: off\\n  Disabled in tally.yaml. This integration is not required.\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"196118\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005792,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3176,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3176)\\nTotal output lines: 92\\n\\n\\u001b[10A\\r\\u001b[2K    ▄   █       ▄\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K    █   █   █   █\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K    █   █ ▀ █ ▀ █  \\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▄\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K    █   █   █  \\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▄\\u001b[0m\\u001b[48;2;226;88;34m▀\\u001b[0m\\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▀▀\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K    █   █  \\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▄\\u001b[0m\\u001b[48;2;226;88;34m▀\\u001b[0m\\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▀▀\\u001b[0m █\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K    █  \\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▄\\u001b[0m\\u001b[48;2;226;88;34m▀\\u001b[0m\\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▀▀\\u001b[0m █   █\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K   \\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▄\\u001b[0m\\u001b[48;2;226;88;34m▀\\u001b[0m\\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▀▀\\u001b[0m █   █   █\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K \\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▀▀\\u001b[0m █   █   █   █\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K    █   █   █   █\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K    █   █   █   ▀\\r\\n\\u001b[10A\\r\\u001b[2K    ▄   █       ▄         \\u001b[2;3mMeet\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K    █   █   █   █         \\u001b[2;1m█████████\\u001b[0m         \\u001b[2;1m▀██\\u001b[0m  \\u001b[2;1m▀██\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\\r\\u001b[2K    █   █ ▀ █ ▀ █  \\u001b[38;2;226;88;34m▄\\u001b[0m   