{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T12:21:08.247Z","ordinal":16422,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a1300c-41d0-7252-878d-fac3cabd2b16","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e1231269-445a-4580-aa91-b4f81ba0e407","process_id":"80292","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'consent|PR|publish|evidence|Mirror this' onboarding/entire.ts engine/init.ts docs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'consent|PR|publish|evidence|Mirror this' onboarding/entire.ts engine/init.ts docs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md","query":"consent|PR|publish|evidence|Mirror this","path":"entire.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"onboarding/entire.ts:117:        if (files.some(file => !SETTINGS_FILES.includes(file))) return off('Entire generated unexpected files. Review them before publishing. Nothing was committed or pushed.');\nonboarding/entire.ts:119:          context.ui.print('Generated settings to publish:');\nonboarding/entire.ts:127:          if (local !== remote) return off('Default branch has unpublished commits. Entire setup will not publish unrelated work.');\nonboarding/entire.ts:128:          context.ui.print('Entire Git hooks may also publish checkpoint and session evidence.');\nonboarding/entire.ts:143:      if (pending) return off('Capture settings are still uncommitted. Entire remains off until they are published on the default branch.');\nonboarding/entire.ts:144:      const published = json(await this.run('git', ['show', 'refs/remotes/origin/HEAD:.entire/settings.json']));\nonboarding/entire.ts:145:      if (published.enabled !== true) return off('Entire capture is not enabled on the remote default branch yet.');\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:11:The integration table is a selection summary, not proof that each integration is fully ready. The following steps have their own consent:\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:13:- **Neatlogs project key:** `NEATLOGS_API_KEY` authorizes decision-trace export. A consented SDK probe sends synthetic probe spans. Tally stores credentials outside the repository. This key does not grant Public API history reads.\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:17:- **Entire repository capture:** before enabling capture, review the proposed repository files and local Git hooks. A second confirmation is required before Tally commits only the listed settings and pushes them to the repository's default branch. That push is a GitHub write and can enable checkpoint/session evidence for future workers. Declining publication leaves capture unavailable to worker worktrees until you publish the settings through your normal review process.\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:18:- **Entire Codex hooks:** after repository capture is published, open Codex in that repository, run `/hooks`, inspect the Entire hooks, and trust them yourself. If you decline or have not trusted them, init keeps Entire disabled. Tally cannot approve hooks on your behalf. See the [Codex Hooks documentation](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks).\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:24:- `tally doctor` checks configured connections. It does not start workers, trust hooks, create tables, or publish repository settings.\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:26:- `tally run --plan` reads the selected GitHub backlog, local repository signals, Neatlogs history when enabled, and CFO.ai budget/spend when enabled. It starts no coding agent, writes no CFO.ai spend, and creates no PR. Neatlogs history reads have a 15-second total deadline; if that read fails or times out, Tally reports the fallback and uses local history.\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:29:- **`tally run` is the approval to perform real work.** It starts the configured coding agent, uses the model account, edits a worker worktree, runs the configured verification command, and can publish a PR after verification. With cfo.ai enabled, real usage is written to the selected spend tables; if a write fails, Tally keeps a local CSV fallback. Review the task list and effective available budget before starting.\nengine/init.ts:270:async function consentClaude(config: TallyConfig, options: InitOptions, readLine: PromptReader, print: (line: string) => void): Promise<void> {\nengine/init.ts:275:  print('Script tokens are portable content-bound consent. Tally replaces them with exact paths outside the worker worktree at startup.');\nengine/init.ts:278:  print('Test and setup commands execute repository code and may install dependencies. Tally installs these consented script rules locally before Claude starts. Never bypass-permissions.');\nengine/init.ts:280:  if (options.dryRun) { print('Preview only: Claude permission consent has not been granted.'); return; }\nengine/init.ts:359:    await consentClaude(config, options, readLine, print);\nengine/init.ts:380:  print(`Preserve all other settings. ${plan.beforeRecord === null ? 'No installation ownership record will be created' : 'Installation ownership and consented harness modes will be updated'}. AO project, setup hooks and worker permissions will not change.`);\nengine/init.ts:484:  await consentClaude(config, options, readLine, print);\nengine/init.ts:526:    print('Before each AO spawn Tally selects the consented tier harness mode under one in-process project lock: Codex auto, Claude Code default with local dontAsk.');\nengine/init.ts:527:    if (hasClaude) print('Worker allow-list: consented Claude rules are installed before launch in .claude/settings.local.json. Script files stay outside the worktree. Local settings and instructions are excluded from Git.');\nengine/init.ts:533:    print('- Tally publishes changes. Workers must not git push or create PRs. Approved setup may install dependencies.');\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"onboarding/entire.ts:117:        if (files.some(file => !SETTINGS_FILES.includes(file))) return off('Entire generated unexpected files. Review them before publishing. Nothing was committed or pushed.');\nonboarding/entire.ts:119:          context.ui.print('Generated settings to publish:');\nonboarding/entire.ts:127:          if (local !== remote) return off('Default branch has unpublished commits. Entire setup will not publish unrelated work.');\nonboarding/entire.ts:128:          context.ui.print('Entire Git hooks may also publish checkpoint and session evidence.');\nonboarding/entire.ts:143:      if (pending) return off('Capture settings are still uncommitted. Entire remains off until they are published on the default branch.');\nonboarding/entire.ts:144:      const published = json(await this.run('git', ['show', 'refs/remotes/origin/HEAD:.entire/settings.json']));\nonboarding/entire.ts:145:      if (published.enabled !== true) return off('Entire capture is not enabled on the remote default branch yet.');\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:11:The integration table is a selection summary, not proof that each integration is fully ready. The following steps have their own consent:\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:13:- **Neatlogs project key:** `NEATLOGS_API_KEY` authorizes decision-trace export. A consented SDK probe sends synthetic probe spans. Tally stores credentials outside the repository. This key does not grant Public API history reads.\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:17:- **Entire repository capture:** before enabling capture, review the proposed repository files and local Git hooks. A second confirmation is required before Tally commits only the listed settings and pushes them to the repository's default branch. That push is a GitHub write and can enable checkpoint/session evidence for future workers. Declining publication leaves capture unavailable to worker worktrees until you publish the settings through your normal review process.\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:18:- **Entire Codex hooks:** after repository capture is published, open Codex in that repository, run `/hooks`, inspect the Entire hooks, and trust them yourself. If you decline or have not trusted them, init keeps Entire disabled. Tally cannot approve hooks on your behalf. See the [Codex Hooks documentation](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks).\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:24:- `tally doctor` checks configured connections. It does not start workers, trust hooks, create tables, or publish repository settings.\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:26:- `tally run --plan` reads the selected GitHub backlog, local repository signals, Neatlogs history when enabled, and CFO.ai budget/spend when enabled. It starts no coding agent, writes no CFO.ai spend, and creates no PR. Neatlogs history reads have a 15-second total deadline; if that read fails or times out, Tally reports the fallback and uses local history.\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:29:- **`tally run` is the approval to perform real work.** It starts the configured coding agent, uses the model account, edits a worker worktree, runs the configured verification command, and can publish a PR after verification. With cfo.ai enabled, real usage is written to the selected spend tables; if a write fails, Tally keeps a local CSV fallback. Review the task list and effective available budget before starting.\nengine/init.ts:270:async function consentClaude(config: TallyConfig, options: InitOptions, readLine: PromptReader, print: (line: string) => void): Promise<void> {\nengine/init.ts:275:  print('Script tokens are portable content-bound consent. Tally replaces them with exact paths outside the worker worktree at startup.');\nengine/init.ts:278:  print('Test and setup commands execute repository code and may install dependencies. Tally installs these consented script rules locally before Claude starts. Never bypass-permissions.');\nengine/init.ts:280:  if (options.dryRun) { print('Preview only: Claude permission consent has not been granted.'); return; }\nengine/init.ts:359:    await consentClaude(config, options, readLine, print);\nengine/init.ts:380:  print(`Preserve all other settings. ${plan.beforeRecord === null ? 'No installation ownership record will be created' : 'Installation ownership and consented harness modes will be updated'}. AO project, setup hooks and worker permissions will not change.`);\nengine/init.ts:484:  await consentClaude(config, options, readLine, print);\nengine/init.ts:526:    print('Before each AO spawn Tally selects the consented tier harness mode under one in-process project lock: Codex auto, Claude Code default with local dontAsk.');\nengine/init.ts:527:    if (hasClaude) print('Worker allow-list: consented Claude rules are installed before launch in .claude/settings.local.json. Script files stay outside the worktree. Local settings and instructions are excluded from Git.');\nengine/init.ts:533:    print('- Tally publishes changes. Workers must not git push or create PRs. Approved setup may install dependencies.');\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":4292},"formatted_output":"onboarding/entire.ts:117:        if (files.some(file => !SETTINGS_FILES.includes(file))) return off('Entire generated unexpected files. Review them before publishing. Nothing was committed or pushed.');\nonboarding/entire.ts:119:          context.ui.print('Generated settings to publish:');\nonboarding/entire.ts:127:          if (local !== remote) return off('Default branch has unpublished commits. Entire setup will not publish unrelated work.');\nonboarding/entire.ts:128:          context.ui.print('Entire Git hooks may also publish checkpoint and session evidence.');\nonboarding/entire.ts:143:      if (pending) return off('Capture settings are still uncommitted. Entire remains off until they are published on the default branch.');\nonboarding/entire.ts:144:      const published = json(await this.run('git', ['show', 'refs/remotes/origin/HEAD:.entire/settings.json']));\nonboarding/entire.ts:145:      if (published.enabled !== true) return off('Entire capture is not enabled on the remote default branch yet.');\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:11:The integration table is a selection summary, not proof that each integration is fully ready. The following steps have their own consent:\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:13:- **Neatlogs project key:** `NEATLOGS_API_KEY` authorizes decision-trace export. A consented SDK probe sends synthetic probe spans. Tally stores credentials outside the repository. This key does not grant Public API history reads.\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:17:- **Entire repository capture:** before enabling capture, review the proposed repository files and local Git hooks. A second confirmation is required before Tally commits only the listed settings and pushes them to the repository's default branch. That push is a GitHub write and can enable checkpoint/session evidence for future workers. Declining publication leaves capture unavailable to worker worktrees until you publish the settings through your normal review process.\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:18:- **Entire Codex hooks:** after repository capture is published, open Codex in that repository, run `/hooks`, inspect the Entire hooks, and trust them yourself. If you decline or have not trusted them, init keeps Entire disabled. Tally cannot approve hooks on your behalf. See the [Codex Hooks documentation](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks).\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:24:- `tally doctor` checks configured connections. It does not start workers, trust hooks, create tables, or publish repository settings.\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:26:- `tally run --plan` reads the selected GitHub backlog, local repository signals, Neatlogs history when enabled, and CFO.ai budget/spend when enabled. It starts no coding agent, writes no CFO.ai spend, and creates no PR. Neatlogs history reads have a 15-second total deadline; if that read fails or times out, Tally reports the fallback and uses local history.\ndocs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md:29:- **`tally run` is the approval to perform real work.** It starts the configured coding agent, uses the model account, edits a worker worktree, runs the configured verification command, and can publish a PR after verification. With cfo.ai enabled, real usage is written to the selected spend tables; if a write fails, Tally keeps a local CSV fallback. Review the task list and effective available budget before starting.\nengine/init.ts:270:async function consentClaude(config: TallyConfig, options: InitOptions, readLine: PromptReader, print: (line: string) => void): Promise<void> {\nengine/init.ts:275:  print('Script tokens are portable content-bound consent. Tally replaces them with exact paths outside the worker worktree at startup.');\nengine/init.ts:278:  print('Test and setup commands execute repository code and may install dependencies. Tally installs these consented script rules locally before Claude starts. Never bypass-permissions.');\nengine/init.ts:280:  if (options.dryRun) { print('Preview only: Claude permission consent has not been granted.'); return; }\nengine/init.ts:359:    await consentClaude(config, options, readLine, print);\nengine/init.ts:380:  print(`Preserve all other settings. ${plan.beforeRecord === null ? 'No installation ownership record will be created' : 'Installation ownership and consented harness modes will be updated'}. AO project, setup hooks and worker permissions will not change.`);\nengine/init.ts:484:  await consentClaude(config, options, readLine, print);\nengine/init.ts:526:    print('Before each AO spawn Tally selects the consented tier harness mode under one in-process project lock: Codex auto, Claude Code default with local dontAsk.');\nengine/init.ts:527:    if (hasClaude) print('Worker allow-list: consented Claude rules are installed before launch in .claude/settings.local.json. Script files stay outside the worktree. Local settings and instructions are excluded from Git.');\nengine/init.ts:533:    print('- Tally publishes changes. Workers must not git push or create PRs. Approved setup may install dependencies.');\n"},"started_at_ms":1791807668247,"completed_at_ms":1791807668247}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T12:21:08.381Z","ordinal":16423,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a1300c-41d0-7252-878d-fac3cabd2b16","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e971c805-f3b2-4f61-9f2c-12a80105ee99","process_id":"67797","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/skills/using-ao/SKILL.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/skills/using-ao/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/skills/using-ao/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\nname: using-ao\ndescription: \"Catalog of the AO (Agent Orchestrator) `ao` CLI: spawning workers, managing sessions and projects, creating reusable Cues, sending messages, controlling the shared browser, previewing pages, and daemon control. Use when using the ao CLI, creating Cues, spawning workers, or managing AO sessions in an AO workspace.\"\ntrigger: \"Using the ao CLI in an AO workspace: creating Cues, spawning workers, managing sessions/projects, sending messages, controlling or previewing pages.\"\n---\n\n# AO CLI Catalog\n\n`ao` is a thin CLI over the local AO daemon. Every command is `ao <command> --help` for the authoritative flag list.\n\n| Command | What it does | When to use | Details |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `spawn` | Spawn a project worker, orchestrator, or projectless standalone worker | Starting a new task or issue | [commands/spawn.md](commands/spawn.md) |\n| `session` | Manage agent sessions (list, kill, rename, restore, etc.) | Inspecting or controlling running/terminated sessions | [commands/session.md](commands/session.md) |\n| `agent` | Inspect installed harnesses and launch readiness | Choosing or diagnosing an agent harness | `ao agent ls --refresh` |\n| `pr` | Merge a PR or resolve its review threads | Completing a reviewed change | `ao pr merge` / `ao pr resolve-comments` |\n| `project` | Register, inspect, configure, or remove projects | Setting up or managing repos AO knows about | [commands/project.md](commands/project.md) |\n| `automation` | Manage durable recurring session automations | Creating, editing, disabling, deleting, and inspecting scheduled runs | [commands/automation.md](commands/automation.md) |\n| `cue` | Create or list reusable project Cues | Saving a repetitive command or agent task at the user's request | [commands/cue.md](commands/cue.md) |\n| `orchestrator` | List orchestrator sessions | Viewing which sessions are orchestrators | [commands/orchestrator.md](commands/orchestrator.md) |\n| `review` | Start, list, cancel, or submit AO's native reviewer for a worker's PR (default: this session) | Getting an adversarial review of an AO session's PR; never spawn a worker to review | [commands/review.md](commands/review.md) |\n| `send` | Send a message to a running agent session | Correcting or directing a live agent | [commands/send.md](commands/send.md) |\n| `report` | Persist a meaningful worker report | Checkpoints, blockers, decisions, outputs, and completion | [commands/report.md](commands/report.md) |\n| `preview` | Start a session-owned app or open an exact URL/file | Running and showing the worker's relevant app, Markdown, HTML, PDF, or image | [commands/preview.md](commands/preview.md) |\n| `render` | Show a self-contained HTML page inline in a chat thread | Answering with a chart, table, diagram, or mockup | [commands/render.md](commands/render.md) |\n| `browser` | Inspect and control the session's shared live browser | Verifying a web app through snapshots, interactions, waits, screenshots, console, and errors | [commands/browser.md](commands/browser.md) |\n| `start` | Fetch (if needed) and open the AO desktop app | Launching the app | [commands/start.md](commands/start.md) |\n| `stop` | Stop the AO daemon | Shutting down AO | [commands/stop.md](commands/stop.md) |\n| `status` | Show daemon status | Verifying the daemon is up and healthy | [commands/status.md](commands/status.md) |\n| `doctor` | Run local health checks | Diagnosing AO setup problems | [commands/doctor.md](commands/doctor.md) |\n| `import` | Import projects from a legacy AO install | Migrating from the old flat-file store | [commands/import.md](commands/import.md) |\n| `version` | Print version information | Checking installed version | - |\n| `completion` | Generate shell completion scripts | Setting up tab completion | - |\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Most read commands accept `--json` for machine-readable output.\n- `-p / --project` scopes session subcommand lookups to one project.\n- Session and project ids are shown by `ao session ls` and `ao project ls`.\n- To refer to a session in AO Chat or the AO terminal, use the canonical in-app\n  link `ao://sessions/{project-id}/{session-id}`. Read\n  [commands/session.md](commands/session.md) for identity, encoding, and safety\n  rules before constructing one.\n- When the user asks to save a repeatable task as a Cue, use `ao cue list --json` to check existing definitions, then `ao cue create`. An agent Cue stores a reusable instruction; a command Cue stores an exact shell command. This agent-facing command can create and read Cues, but cannot edit or delete them. Direct the user to project settings for changes to existing Cues.\n- `--agent` is an alias for `--harness` on `ao spawn`.\n- Every command accepts `-h / --help` for the full flag list.\n- For frontend launch, preview selection, or artifact handoff, read\n  [commands/preview.md](commands/preview.md) before acting. Its static-file,\n  project-runtime, and automatic-handoff rules are load-bearing.\n- For page inspection, interaction, or request diagnosis, read\n  [commands/browser.md](commands/browser.md). It defines shared-tab behavior\n  and the opt-in network policy.\n\nUse [references.md](references.md) only when a natural-language request does\nnot map clearly to a command above.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: using-ao\ndescription: \"Catalog of the AO (Agent Orchestrator) `ao` CLI: spawning workers, managing sessions and projects, creating reusable Cues, sending messages, controlling the shared browser, previewing pages, and daemon control. Use when using the ao CLI, creating Cues, spawning workers, or managing AO sessions in an AO workspace.\"\ntrigger: \"Using the ao CLI in an AO workspace: creating Cues, spawning workers, managing sessions/projects, sending messages, controlling or previewing pages.\"\n---\n\n# AO CLI Catalog\n\n`ao` is a thin CLI over the local AO daemon. Every command is `ao <command> --help` for the authoritative flag list.\n\n| Command | What it does | When to use | Details |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `spawn` | Spawn a project worker, orchestrator, or projectless standalone worker | Starting a new task or issue | [commands/spawn.md](commands/spawn.md) |\n| `session` | Manage agent sessions (list, kill, rename, restore, etc.) | Inspecting or controlling running/terminated sessions | [commands/session.md](commands/session.md) |\n| `agent` | Inspect installed harnesses and launch readiness | Choosing or diagnosing an agent harness | `ao agent ls --refresh` |\n| `pr` | Merge a PR or resolve its review threads | Completing a reviewed change | `ao pr merge` / `ao pr resolve-comments` |\n| `project` | Register, inspect, configure, or remove projects | Setting up or managing repos AO knows about | [commands/project.md](commands/project.md) |\n| `automation` | Manage durable recurring session automations | Creating, editing, disabling, deleting, and inspecting scheduled runs | [commands/automation.md](commands/automation.md) |\n| `cue` | Create or list reusable project Cues | Saving a repetitive command or agent task at the user's request | [commands/cue.md](commands/cue.md) |\n| `orchestrator` | List orchestrator sessions | Viewing which sessions are orchestrators | [commands/orchestrator.md](com