× 60% × 80% |\n| Tally's share | 20% | assumption |\n| **Revenue per customer per month** | **$480** | $2,400 × 20% |\n| Customer keeps | $1,920 | the rest of the saving |\n\n## 4. Funnel (first 6 months)\n\n| Stage | Number | Basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| Qualified leads | to come from the CrustData sample | lane B is checking 10 companies by hand; the earlier \"2,085\" was a raw search count, not qualified leads, and is not used here |\n| Leads contacted | 200 | assumption |\n| Pilots started (5%) | 10 | assumption |\n| Pilots that convert to paying (40%) | 4 | assumption |\n| Monthly revenue at month 6 | $1,920 | 4 × $480 |\n\n## 5. Costs\n\n| Line | Monthly | Basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| Tally's own model spend | $0 | the customer runs the agents on their own accounts; Tally makes no model calls of its own |\n| CrustData | small | 0.03 credits per search result; today's qualification work is capped at 10 credits |\n| neatlogs, Entire, cfo.ai | plan prices | not checked; fill in from your plans |\n| Hosting | none yet | the CLI runs on the customer's machine; the project page is static |\n\n## 6. What would make this plan real\n\n1. Run the baseline comparison so the saving per task is measured, not assumed.\n2. Replace the lead numbers with the CrustData sample once it is reviewed.\n3. Decide how the baseline is agreed with a customer (their last month's bill, or the same tasks priced at their top model's list price).\n\n## Proposed cfo.ai page\n\nA new page \"Tally business plan\" in the \"Main Scenario\", beside the existing \"Tally\" page that holds the agent budget and spend. Three tables: unit economics (section 3), funnel (section 4), costs (section 5), with the assumptions as editable inputs so the plan recalculates when you change them, and a note linking the measured rows in section 2 to the ledger. The agent's real budget and spend cells are not touched.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":9167},"formatted_output":"# Tally business plan: draft for t