an assumption.\n\n## 3. Unit economics (one customer)\n\n| Line | Value | Basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| Engineers using coding agents | 25 | assumption |\n| Agent spend per engineer per month, all on the top model | $200 | assumption |\n| Baseline monthly agent spend | $5,000 | 25 × $200 |\n| Share of tasks a cheaper tier can finish | 60% | assumption; every small task in our real runs passed on the cheap tier, but that is 6 tasks |\n| Saving on those tasks | 80% | assumption, deliberately below the 95% price gap to allow for escalations and retries |\n| Monthly saving | $2,400 | $5,000 × 60% × 80% |\n| Tally's share | 20% | assumption |\n| **Revenue per customer per month** | **$480** | $2,400 × 20% |\n| Customer keeps | $1,920 | the rest of the saving |\n\n## 4. Funnel (first 6 months)\n\n| Stage | Number | Basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| Qualified leads | to come from the CrustData sample | lane B is checking 10 companies by hand; the earlier \"2,085\" was a raw search count, not qualified leads, and is not used here |\n| Leads contacted | 200 | assumption |\n| Pilots started (5%) | 10 | assumption |\n| Pilots that convert to paying (40%) | 4 | assumption |\n| Monthly revenue at month 6 | $1,920 | 4 × $480 |\n\n## 5. Costs\n\n| Line | Monthly | Basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| Tally's own model spend | $0 | the customer runs the agents on their own accounts; Tally makes no model calls of its own |\n| CrustData | small | 0.03 credits per search result; today's qualification work is capped at 10 credits |\n| neatlogs, Entire, cfo.ai | plan prices | not checked; fill in from your plans |\n| Hosting | none yet | the CLI runs on the customer's machine; the project page is static |\n\n## 6. What would make this plan real\n\n1. Run the baseline comparison so the saving per task is measured, not assumed.\n2. Replace the lead numbers with the CrustData sample once it is reviewed.\n3. Decide how the baseline is agreed with a customer (their last month's bill, or the same tasks priced at their top model's list price).\n\n## Proposed cfo.ai page\n\nA new page \"Tally business plan\" in the \"Main Scenario\", beside the existing \"Tally\" page that holds the agent budget and spend. Three tables: unit economics (section 3), funnel (section 4), costs (section 5), with the assumptions as editable inputs so the plan recalculates when you change them, and a note linking the measured rows in section 2 to the ledger. The agent's real budget and spend cells are not touched.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791810437944,"completed_at_ms":1791810437944}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T13:07:18.232Z","ordinal":16455,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a13039-52ed-7140-86e2-0302da789af2","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-84e1d37d-d680-4842-b891-f501814ff2a1","process_id":"81134","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'business.plan|business plan|approved|finalized' /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8 --glob '*.md'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'business.plan|business plan|approved|finalized' /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8 --glob '*.md'","query":"business.plan|business plan|approved|finalized","path":"neatlogs-hack-8"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-remaining.md:52:- [ ] cfo.ai: the business plan (share-of-savings pricing); the correct page address for the dashboard link.\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-remaining.md:55:- [ ] CrustData: validate the query; put it in the business plan as leads, not market size.\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-video-kit.md:147:- \"Plan a business around the agent\" is part of the 25%. The cfo.ai side today is the agent budget and spend, not a business plan. A pricing or revenue page in cfo.ai (share-of-savings pricing, with the CrustData lead list) would cover it and is not built yet.\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-demo-guide.md:107:- The baseline comparison, hosted dashboard and business plan belong to the Final milestone.\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-business-plan-draft.md:1:# Tally business plan: draft for the cfo.ai page\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-business-plan-draft.md:65:A new page \"Tally business plan\" in the \"Main Scenario\", beside the existing \"Tally\" page that holds the agent budget and spend. Three tables: unit economics (section 3), funnel (section 4), costs (section 5), with the assumptions as editable inputs so the plan recalculates when you change them, and a note linking the measured rows in section 2 to the ledger. The agent's real budget and spend cells are not touched.\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/site-brief.md:38:Code cannot paint airbrush illustration. The orchestrator is generating the painted images (hero object, crimson-sky desert scene, mascots together, contact-card figure) and will drop them into the reference folder as they are approved. Build every section so it looks finished with CSS/SVG alone (gradients, glints, grain, type), with a clearly named image slot per section that upgrades it when the file exists. Do not block on artwork and do not generate images yourself.\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/site-brief-v2.md:21:Use the mark he approved: `site-reference-v2/tally-mark-approved.png`. It is the terminal rendering from `cli/logo.ts`: four white block strokes of uneven height, two small square eyes, one orange stepped slash, \"Meet\" in italic mono, \"Tally\" in block letters, \"the CFO for your agent fleet\", on dark slate. That pixel/terminal mark **is** the logo and the mascot. Render it crisply (SVG rects or a canvas from the real frames), animate it with the same draw-in the CLI uses, and use it at small size for the nav and favicon. No chrome, no gradients on the mark, no hand-drawn variant, no painted version.\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/site-brief-v2.md:49:   Fill each with real evidence only. Verified facts you may use: four runner paths each proven by a real pull request on `Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup` (Codex via AO PR #10 $0.0121; Claude Code via AO PR #13 $0.0871; Claude Code direct PR #14 $0.0765; Codex direct PR #18 $0.0109; costs are estimates at list price); stop at the ceiling and escalate proven once (fly-doom-jev PR #14); cfo.ai spend matched the ledger to the cent on each run; decision and worker traces read back from neatlogs; `tally-agents` 0.1.0 on npm; run `npm test` for the current test count. Where evidence does not exist yet (video, public posts, a business plan in cfo.ai, a measured baseline saving), leave a clearly marked empty slot rather than inventing anything. Do not state a savings percentage.\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-final-plan.md:43:| Usefulness and originality | 10% | \"They cap people, we cap tasks\", backed by the experiment and a business plan in cfo.ai. |\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-final-plan.md:108:| D3 | Market size into the cfo.ai business plan (C5). | The plan's market row cites the CrustData list. |\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-final-plan.md:211:| Your pricing assumptions for the business plan | C5 | C5 |\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-remaining.md:52:- [ ] cfo.ai: the business plan (share-of-savings pricing); the correct page address for the dashboard link.\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-remaining.md:55:- [ ] CrustData: validate the query; put it in the business plan as leads, not market size.\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-video-kit.md:147:- \"Plan a business around the agent\" is part of the 25%. The cfo.ai side today is the agent budget and spend, not a business plan. A pricing or revenue page in cfo.ai (share-of-savings pricing, with the CrustData lead list) would cover it and is not built yet.\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-demo-guide.md:107:- The baseline comparison, hosted dashboard and business plan belong to the Final milestone.\n/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-business-plan-draft.md:1:# Tally business plan: draft for the cfo.ai page\n/Users/vaibhaav/