{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T13:31:21.048Z","ordinal":16576,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a1304c-6bc6-74e2-abf0-d7073703152e","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_004274e0102b2ff9016acce127085081919cd461c8e4a37102","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Both runtime installs passed the command checks and ran the unchanged 0.1.0 config sequentially. The tarball contains 285 files; the remaining review concern is that #149 posts configured cfo.ai table links to task PRs without a specific init disclosure.\n"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1791811879214,"completed_at_ms":1791811881048}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T13:31:21.052Z","ordinal":16577,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_004274e0102b2ff9016acce127085081919cd461c8e4a37102","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Both runtime installs passed the command checks and ran the unchanged 0.1.0 config sequentially. The tarball contains 285 files; the remaining review concern is that #149 posts configured cfo.ai table links to task PRs without a specific init disclosure.\n"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1304c-6bc6-74e2-abf0-d7073703152e","create_time":1791811879.0359092,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_004274e0102b2ff9016acce127085081919cd461c8e4a37102","turn_id":"01a1304c-6bc6-74e2-abf0-d7073703152e","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a1304f-885c-7852-8003-5b63720c4f3a","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":1659}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T13:31:53.326Z","ordinal":16578,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_004274e0102b2ff9016acce129040081919bf35152c791af78","status":"completed","call_id":"call_afc5b3b0111d4ac2ae12b47fc6cba10b","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:73859,chars:\"\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:350}));\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/release-020b/report.md\\n+# Tally 0.2.0 Candidate B Pre-Release Check\\n+\\n+Source commit: `afbd3769aac4b5be24489591a7da19d1e1f917b0`.\\n+Built release commit: `78885aada7f9769b632c419567de77803216d72f`.\\n+Its release-source.json matches the source exactly. Packed from an extracted\\n+built release, not a source checkout. Nothing was published. The earlier\\n+release-020/ fallback was not modified or deleted.\\n+\\n+## Tarball\\n+\\n+- Path: `/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/release-020b/tally-agents-0.2.0.tgz`\\n+- Files: 285; compressed size: 476,251 bytes; unpacked size: 1,708,726 bytes.\\n+- SHA-256: `d47dd7bd63689d2678f436b75d68e676042b8afee51144324dabb792d5d44799`\\n+- Full file inventory and npm integrity metadata: `inventory.json` alongside this report.\\n+\\n+The bin, dist, dashboard, JSON schemas, README, LICENSE and release-source\\n+manifest are present. No tests, testing helpers, site/, unnecessary scripts,\\n+.env, .tally, .claude, .codex or node_modules are packed. Known configured\\n+credential values were compared against packed content without printing them;\\n+none matched. No development dependencies or lifecycle scripts in the release\\n+manifest. No new dependencies from #149.\\n+\\n+## Clean Install Results\\n+\\n+Separate fresh prefixes and empty caches were used for Node 26.8.2 and Node\\n+20.20.2. Neither replaced the user's global installation. Vitest is absent\\n+from both installed runtime packages.\\n+\\n+| Check | Both Runtimes |\\n+| --- | --- |\\n+| tally --version | 0.2.0, exit 0 |\\n+| tally logo, non-TTY | Plain static mark, exit 0 |\\n+| tally logo, TTY | Animation completes, reset and cursor-show emitted, exit 0 |\\n+| tally demo | 7 tasks, 9 attempts, 6 passed and 1 intentional failure, $1.7063 simulated |\\n+| tally doctor, empty HOME and scratch repository | Expected exit 1: GitHub sign-in missing; optional integrations off |\\n+| tally doctor, complete existing AO configuration | Exit 0 |\\n+| tally init --help | Exit 0; no setup performed |\\n+| tally run --plan | Exit 0 with parallelWorkers: 2 and modelAccessFallbackTier: middle |\\n+| tally market --replay | Exit 0; cached 20-company report; no CrustData API calls |\\n+| Unchanged published 0.1.0-style init config | Loads and runs two passing tasks sequentially despite legacy concurrency: 3 |\\n+\\n+The upgrade check runs through the installed real loop with fake worker,\\n+intake, sizing and usage ports. It asserts start/end/start/end ordering and\\n+that the legacy config has no parallelWorkers or modelAccessFallbackTier.\\n+Plan and configured doctor read the existing fly-doom-jev AO configuration and\\n+repository only; no workers, PR edits, commits, project changes or cfo.ai writes.\\n+\\n+npm warned that two protobufjs dependency postinstall scripts were not\\n+approved. That policy was not overridden; all installed runtime checks passed.\\n+The orchestrator separately gated this source at 839 tests twice, typecheck,\\n+build and dry runs; this audit did not repeat the full source suite.\\n+\\n+## Five-Line Read of #149\\n+\\n+1. Adds two compiled runtime modules (evidence-links and pr-evidence), updated docs and no dependencies.\\n+2. Adds Entire mirror-readiness queries and gh pr view/edit; #151 bounds each GitHub evidence call to 15 seconds.\\n+3. Adds no cfo.ai data writes, but enabling it automatically posts configured budget/spend URLs to task PRs without a dedicated init sharing disclosure or opt-in.\\n+4. HUMAN_APPROVALS.md's new mirror consent is real: init explains repository upload and asks separately before mirror creation; existing ready mirrors are only read.\\n+5. Neatlogs URLs are formed from trace IDs without requiring successful read-back; mirror readiness is checked for derived Entire session links, but readiness alone does not verify browser access.\\n+\\n+## Maintainer Publish Command\\n+\\n+Only Vaibhaav should run this, with his own fresh 2FA code, after the\\n+orchestrator confirms the final candidate is approved:\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+npm publish /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/release-020b/tally-agents-0.2.0.tgz --access public --tag latest --registry https://registry.npmjs.org --otp '<2FA_CODE>'\\n+```\\n+\\n+No publish, login, Git tag or GitHub release was attempted.\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1304c-6bc6-74e2-abf0-d7073703152e","create_time":1791811881.0187688}}}
