{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T15:45:15.480Z","ordinal":16617,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a130c9-841c-7440-b5e7-c596eae592f9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7143325a-c2b5-49fb-9a57-c005870e2984","process_id":"71113","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,150p' /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/report.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,150p' /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/report.md","name":"report.md","path":"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/report.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Routing evidence\n\nGenerated 2026-10-12T11:32:54.147Z. 24 closed real runs; 35 task outcomes (including skipped).\n\n## Three-Pass Comparison\n\n### What This Comparison Proves\n\nThree tasks (BENCH-2, BENCH-4, BENCH-5), one run each per pass. All three\npassed in A, B and C; each pass had three model attempts plus three separately\nreported zero-token startup retries. BENCH-1 and BENCH-3 were not run.\n\nTotal estimated costs: A $1.21693600, B $0.30932564, C $0.42632384.\nMean cost per task: A $0.40564533, B $0.10310855, C $0.14210795.\nC cost more than B in this single comparison; this is not evidence that\ntrace-history routing reduced cost compared with prior-only routing.\n\nB routed on priors. In C only the large task used observed neatlogs statistics:\nthe top-tier cost estimate changed from $1.50 to about $0.303 from two samples.\nNo selected tier or configured cap changed between B and C. The other two C\ntasks had only one observation per size/model and still used priors. No learned\nP90 cap was available (five successful samples are required).\n\nThis is evidence of history being read and used in an expectation, not of a\nhistory-driven model/cap change or a repeatable improvement. Task runtime,\ncaching and model variability can explain cost differences; one run per task\nprovides no statistical spread. Costs are Tally's token-price estimates, not\nprovider invoices. The trace-readback cache predates these comparison passes;\nthe decision's saved provenance is not a new worker-trace readback.\n\nPlan measured 2026-10-12T09:30:21.074Z, pinned base 565e6ccd757ff794ead643dac7359efe67ec9db2. Signals source: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-2/mentor-comparison-plan-signals.json.\n\n| Pass | Covered tasks | Task outcomes | Mean cost/task USD | Pass rate | Model attempts | Startup retries |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| A: top-tier baseline | 3/5 | 3 | 0.40565 | 100.0% | 3 | 3 |\n| B: Tally v1 (priors) | 3/5 | 3 | 0.10311 | 100.0% | 3 | 3 |\n| C: Tally v2 (trace history) | 3/5 | 3 | 0.14211 | 100.0% | 3 | 3 |\n\nStartup retries are zero-token error rows with an explicit linked :startup-retry row, not model failures or model attempts-to-success; all recorded costs remain included. Zero-token errors without that link remain operational errors.\n\n| Task | Size | Targets | Dependents | Graph nodes | Text chars | Named paths | A: cost/verdict/attempts | B: cost/verdict/attempts | C: cost/verdict/attempts |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---|\n| BENCH-1 | small | 1 | unmeasured | unmeasured | 634 | 3 | pending | pending | pending |\n| BENCH-2 | small | 2 | 26 | 12 | 746 | 2 | $0.45790 / passed / 1 model attempts + 1 startup retries (run-20261012T104159Z-comparison-A) | $0.01523 / passed / 1 model attempts + 1 startup retries (run-20261012T105538Z-comparison-B) | $0.01167 / passed / 1 model attempts + 1 startup retries (run-20261012T111142Z-comparison-C) |\n| BENCH-3 | medium | 4 | 70 | 23 | 869 | 3 | pending | pending | pending |\n| BENCH-4 | medium | 3 | 35 | 21 | 803 | 3 | $0.41609 / passed / 1 model attempts + 1 startup retries (run-20261012T104159Z-comparison-A) | $0.03039 / passed / 1 model attempts + 1 startup retries (run-20261012T105538Z-comparison-B) | $0.01976 / passed / 1 model attempts + 1 startup retries (run-20261012T111142Z-comparison-C) |\n| BENCH-5 | large | 3 | 91 | 21 | 1110 | 4 | $0.34294 / passed / 1 model attempts + 1 startup retries (run-20261012T104159Z-comparison-A) | $0.26370 / passed / 1 model attempts + 1 startup retries (run-20261012T105538Z-comparison-B) | $0.39489 / passed / 1 model attempts + 1 startup retries (run-20261012T111142Z-comparison-C) |\n\n![Cost per comparison task](cost-by-routing.svg)\n\n![Pass rate per comparison pass](success-by-routing.svg)\n\nPass labels are explicit experiment assignments, not proof that history affected every route in C. Actual routing provenance remains in tasks.csv. Costs only come from matching real ledgers; plan signals never supply spend. Missing passes/tasks stay pending; partial coverage is not a completed comparison. No savings claim before all three passes cover the same tasks. A single repeat establishes no statistical spread.\n\nComparison join exclusions: 0 (base/text/pass-label mismatches retained in results.json).\n\n## Historical Audit (Not the Matched Comparison)\n\n| Routing evidence | Task outcomes | Passed | Operational errors | Skipped | Mean cost (USD) | Pass rate |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| prior-only | 15 | 11 | 4 | 0 | 0.06801 | 73.3% |\n| trace-driven | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0.39489 | 100.0% |\n| local-history | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | not measured | not measured |\n| unattributed | 16 | 10 | 4 | 0 | 0.04686 | 62.5% |\n| baseline | 3 | 3 | 0 | 0 | 0.40565 | 100.0% |\n\nPrior-only requires an explicit prior statement for the chosen tier. Trace-driven requires explicit neatlogs provenance and observed statistics for the chosen tier; this can affect routing before five successful cost samples exist for a learned P90 cap. A configured cap is not a learned cap. Old ambiguous decisions are unattributed, not silently assigned to either group.\n\nNo v1/v2 savings claim or baseline comparison is valid until both have measured, matched tasks. Missing cohorts mean not measured, never zero cost or 0% success. Closed interrupted runs and skipped tasks stay in the denominator; zero spend on an unstarted task is not savings. Repeated issues across runs are not independent experiments.\n\n## Does sizing predict cost?\n\n| Signal | Paired successful tasks | Pearson r | Spearman rho | Interpretation |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| Entire graph nodes | 9 | 0.213 | 0.274 | No clear linear signal in this sample. |\n| Predicted target files | 9 | 0.213 | 0.274 | No clear linear signal in this sample. |\n| Issue-text characters | 9 | 0.443 | 0.316 | Positive association in this sample, not a causal or out-of-sample prediction. |\n| Path-like file mentions | 9 | 0.383 | 0.316 | Positive association in this sample, not a causal or out-of-sample prediction. |\n\n| Pass | Signal | Successful pairs | Pearson r | Spearman rho |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| A | Entire graph nodes | 3 | -0.778 | -0.866 |\n| A | Predicted target files | 3 | -0.778 | -0.866 |\n| A | Issue-text characters | 3 | -0.976 | -1.000 |\n| A | Path-like file mentions | 3 | -0.988 | -1.000 |\n| B | Entire graph nodes | 3 | 0.546 | 0.866 |\n| B | Predicted target files | 3 | 0.546 | 0.866 |\n| B | Issue-text characters | 3 | 0.996 | 1.000 |\n| B | Path-like file mentions | 3 | 0.892 | 1.000 |\n| C | Entire graph nodes | 3 | 0.516 | 0.866 |\n| C | Predicted target files | 3 | 0.516 | 0.866 |\n| C | Issue-text characters | 3 | 0.992 | 1.000 |\n| C | Path-like file mentions | 3 | 0.875 | 1.000 |\n\nThe size chart uses only comparison outcomes at the pinned base with measured plan signals, not unrelated historical tasks. Pooled correlations mix model prices; per-pass coefficients are also reported. Repeated tasks across passes are not independent observations. New target files and named context can make graph targets differ from literal file mentions.\n\n![Sizing signals against estimated cost](size-cost.svg)\n\nGraph nodes and target-file counts come only from saved impact totals; missing historical graphs are not reconstructed or replaced with actual edited files. Current issue bodies are labelled current-issue, not run-start snapshots. Most historical successful tasks are small documentation changes; the planned five-task comparison broadens scope but remains a tiny single-repository sample. Model price, caching, setup and repository differences confound these correlations; do not use them to train or claim a general cost predictor.\n\n## Trace readback\n\nReadback date: 2026-10-12T10:31:01.706Z. 6/48 attempt costs/outcomes match a neatlogs history record by run, size, tier, result and integer cost.\n12/19 stored worker trace IDs verified by correlated metadata plus readable spans. Window truncated: true.\nCosts here are normalized list-price/AO estimates from the real ledger, not invoices. History trace names repeat those recorded estimates. Public worker traces can report zero cost/tokens when hooks export tool activity only; that does not mean the worker was free.\n\n## Cap and Escalation Evidence\n\n| Run/task | Stopped spend and cap | Failure class/source | Next attempt | Stopped checkpoint | Worker trace id |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| run-20261010-201255Z / FDJ-3 | cheap: $0.01531 / cap $0.01500 | classification not recorded | middle: passed / $0.08152 | 01M4KQ6FY5C33GHZ4EHGM4QTME | 49bac43affb72d3ae8fcf05bbd336152 |\n| run-20261010-195412Z / FDJ-5 | cheap: $0.01010 / cap $0.01000 | classification not recorded | middle: failed / $0.00000 | none | unverified |\n| run-20261012-091013Z / #15 | cheap: $0.01837 / cap $0.01800 | classification not recorded | middle: error / $0.17067 | 01M4QP510W3QV39MSX9DGQ40JS | unverified |\n| run-20261012-100856Z / #15 | cheap: $0.01956 / cap $0.01800 | ceiling / ledger | middle: passed / $0.16958 | 01M4QSHQT5EVWM8MB1BJW6SDHT | 961d841ba3223b7d1bb3e81932369507 |\n\nMetering/polling lag can overshoot a cap. A stored worker trace id is not fresh read-back verification; see the readback section. Ledger-derived ceiling classifications remain ledger-derived even after trace delivery recovers.\n\n## Replay and limits\n\nThe audited input paths are in sources.json; task-level data is in tasks.csv and results.json. trace-readback.json caches actual read results. Re-running without --live-traces makes no API call. No paid workers, cfo.ai writes, or fabricated baseline runs were used.\nSchema/exclusion count: 0. Read errors: 0.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Routing evidence\n\nGenerated 2026-10-12T11:32:54.147Z. 24 closed real runs; 35 task outcomes (including skipped).\n\n## Three-Pass Comparison\n\n### What This Comparison Proves\n\nThree tasks (BENCH-2, BENCH-4, BENCH-5), one run each per pass. All three\npassed in A, B and C; each pass had three model attempts plus three separately\nreported zero-token startup retries. BENCH-1 and BENCH-3 were not run.\n\nTotal estimated costs: A $1.21693600, B $0.30932564, C $0.42632384.\nMean cost per task: A $0.40564533, B $0.10310855, C $0.14210795.\nC cost more than B in this single comparison; this is not evidence that\ntrace-history routing reduced cost compared with prior-only routing.\n\nB routed on priors. In C only the large task used observed neatlogs statistics:\nthe top-tier cost estimate changed from $1.50 to about $0.303 from two samples.\nNo selected tier or configured cap changed between B and C. The other two C\ntasks had only one observation per size/model and still used priors. No learned\nP90 cap was available (five successful samples are required).\n\nThis is evidence of history being read and used in an expectation, not of a\nhistory-driven model/cap change or a repeatable improvement. Task runtime,\ncaching and model variability can explain cost differences; one run per task\nprovides no statistical spread. Costs are Tally's token-price estimates, not\nprovider invoices. The trace-readback cach