sal 154ms\nfatal: ambiguous argument 'origin/main..HEAD': unknown revision or path not in the working tree.\nUse '--' to separate paths from revisions, like this:\n'git <command> [<revision>...] -- [<file>...]'\n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯ Failed Tests 1 ⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯\n\n FAIL  cli/dashboard-server.test.ts > dashboard server > serves dashboard files and run data without directory listing or traversal\nError: listen EPERM: operation not permitted 127.0.0.1\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯[1/1]⎯\n\n\n Test Files  1 failed | 69 passed (70)\n      Tests  1 failed | 873 passed (874)\n   Start at  21:15:04\n   Duration  25.04s (tests 69%, import 20%, transform 6%, setup 4%, worker 1%)\n\n    Isolate  70 workers spawned · ~397ms startup each (spawn + environment, per file)\n             at least ~2.69s faster with isolate: false — reuses workers across files instead of one per file\n\n"},"started_at_ms":1791819903770,"completed_at_ms":1791819930052}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T15:45:30.421Z","ordinal":16626,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a130c9-841c-7440-b5e7-c596eae592f9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-86d2bae2-df24-40b5-a874-1bab628546d3","process_id":"79627","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","git rev-parse HEAD"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git rev-parse HEAD"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"8a6ce511adffab41f6d9b6b05251ea64c1025db7\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"8a6ce511adffab41f6d9b6b05251ea64c1025db7\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":15000},"formatted_output":"8a6ce511adffab41f6d9b6b05251ea64c1025db7\n"},"started_at_ms":1791819930421,"completed_at_ms":1791819930421}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T15:45:30.828Z","ordinal":16627,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a130c9-841c-7440-b5e7-c596eae592f9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7b949323-b805-42f1-8f96-32e0049392a5","process_id":"66642","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '418,455p' README.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '418,455p' README.md","name":"README.md","path":"README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"## Routing Evidence\n\nFrom a source checkout, build and analyze an audited list of real run directories:\n\n```sh\nnpm run build\nnode scripts/routing-evidence.mjs --manifest runs.json --out /tmp/routing-evidence\n```\n\n`runs.json` is a JSON array of paths containing `run.json` and `ledger.json`.\nThe script writes a Markdown report, task CSV, JSON provenance and three SVG\ncharts. It excludes simulations and active runs, keeps skipped/interrupted\noutcomes in the denominator, and labels missing historical signals as missing.\nUnattributed historical decisions are not silently assigned to prior or\ntrace-driven cohorts. Correlations are descriptive, not cost predictions.\n\nAdd `--live-traces` for bounded read-only neatlogs verification using Tally's\nread token and project id. Without that flag it only replays the output folder's\ncached `trace-readback.json`, making no API call. Optional `--issues issues.json`\naccepts a URL-keyed map of current issue titles/bodies for historical runs;\nthese are labelled current text, not run-start snapshots. No paid workers or\ncfo.ai writes are performed. Before/after savings require matched measured\ntasks; missing baseline or v2 cohorts are reported as **not measured**.\n\nFor the matched three-pass experiment, add `--comparison-dir <folder>`.\nThe folder contains `mentor-comparison-plan-signals.json` and, when results\narrive, `comparison-passes.json`: an object mapping `A`, `B`, `C` to arrays of\nreal run-directory paths (absolute or relative to that folder). A is top-tier\nbaseline, B is Tally v1/priors, C is Tally v2/trace history. Missing passes stay\npending. The report joins signals only at the exact pinned base SHA and task\ntext, reports cost/verdict/attempts per task and per pass, and charts sizing\nagainst real costs with per-pass correlations. A pass C label does not itself\nprove that history influenced every route or that any cap was learned.\nUse `--comparison-passes <json>` to keep the labelled path manifest elsewhere\nwithout changing the measured signals folder.\n\n## Layout\n\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"## Routing Evidence\n\nFrom a source checkout, build and analyze an audited list of real run directories:\n\n```sh\nnpm run build\nnode scripts/routing-evidence.mjs --manifest runs.json --out /tmp/routing-evidence\n```\n\n`runs.json` is a JSON array of paths containing `run.json` and `ledger.json`.\nThe script writes a Markdown report, task CSV, JSON provenance and three SVG\ncharts. It excludes simulations and active runs, keeps skipped/interrupted\noutcomes in the denominator, and labels missing historical signals as missing.\nUnattributed historical decisions are not silently assigned to prior or\ntrace-driven cohorts. Correlations are descriptive, not cost predictions.\n\nAdd `--live-traces` for bounded read-only neatlogs verification using Tally's\nread token and project id. Without that flag it only replays the output folder's\ncached `trace-readback.json`, making no API call. Optional `--issues issues.json`\naccepts a URL-keyed map of current issue titles/bodies for historical runs;\nthese are labelled current text, not run-start snapshots. No paid workers or\ncfo.ai writes are performed. Before/after savings require matched measured\ntasks; missing baseline or v2 cohorts are reported as **not measured**.\n\nFor the matched three-pass experiment, add `--comparison-dir <folder>`.\nThe folder contains `mentor-comparison-plan-signals.json` and, when results\narrive, `comparison-passes.json`: an object mapping `A`, `B`, `C` to arrays of\nreal run-directory paths (absolute or relative to that folder). A is top-tier\nbaseline, B is Tally v1/priors, C is Tally v2/trace history. Missing passes stay\npending. The report joins signals only at the exact pinned base SHA and task\ntext, reports cost/verdict/attempts per task and per pass, and charts sizing\nagainst real costs with per-pass correlations. A pass C label does not itself\nprove that history influenced every route or that any cap was learned.\nUse `--comparison-passes <json>` to keep the labelled path manifest elsewhere\nwithout changing the measured signals folder.\n\n## Layout\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":17209},"formatted_output":"## Routing Evidence\n\nFrom a source checkout, build and analyze an audited list of real run directories:\n\n```sh\nnpm run build\nnode scripts/routing-evidence.mjs --manifest runs.json --out /tmp/routing-evidence\n```\n\n`runs.json` is a JSON array of paths containing `run.json` and `ledger.json`.\nThe script writes a Markdown report, task CSV, JSON provenance and three SVG\ncharts. It excludes simulations and active runs, keeps skipped/interrupted\noutcomes in the denominator, and labels missing historical signals as missing.\nUnattributed historical decisions are not silently assigned to prior or\ntrace-driven cohorts. Correlations are descriptive, not cost predictions.\n\nAdd `--live-traces` for bounded read-only neatlogs verification using Tally's\nread token and project id. Without that flag it only replays the output folder's\ncached `trace-readback.json`, making no API call. Optional `--issues issues.json`\naccepts a URL-keyed map of current issue titles/bodies for historical runs;\nthese are labelled current text, not run-start snapshots. No paid workers or\ncfo.ai writes are performed. Before/after savings require matched measured\ntasks; missing baseline or v2 cohorts are reported as **not measured**.\n\nFor the matched three-pass experiment, add `--comparison-dir <folder>`.\nThe folder contains `mentor-comparison-plan-signals.json` and, when results\narrive, `comparison-passes.json`: an object mapping `A`, `B`, `C` to arrays of\nreal run-directory paths (absolute or relative to that folder). A is top-tier\nbaseline, B is Tally v1/priors, C is Tally v2/trace history. Missing passes stay\npending. The report joins signals only at the exact pinned base SHA and task\ntext, reports cost/verdict/attempts per task and per pass, and charts sizing\nagainst real costs with per-pass correlations. A pass C label does not itself\nprove that history influenced every route or that any cap was learned.\nUse `--comparison-passes <json>` to keep the labelled path manifest elsewhere\nwithout changing the measured signals folder.\n\n## Layout\n\n"},"started_at_ms":1791819930828,"completed_at_ms":1791819930828}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T15:45:31.004Z","ordinal":16628,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a130ca-5d7b-7e11-9590-2cb23fe1e9fb","call_id":"call_j41z6xWOaOUUyRNAqWP2y13U","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"ae975e\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.371666667,\"exit_code\":1,\"original_token_count\":228,\"output\":\"fatal: ambiguous argument 'origin/main..HEAD': unknown revision or path not in the working tree.\\nUse '--' to separate paths from revisions, like this:\\n'git <command> [<revision>...] -- [<file>...]'\\n\\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯ Failed Tests 1 ⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯\\n\\n FAIL  cli/dashboard-server.test.ts > dashboard server > serves dashboard files and run data without directory listing or traversal\\nError: listen EPERM: operation not permitted 127.0.0.1\\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯[1/1]⎯\\n\\n\\n Test Files  1 failed | 69 passed (70)\\n      Tests  1 failed | 873 passed (874)\\n   Start at  21:15:04\\n   Duration  25.04s (tests 69%, import 20%, transform 6%, setup 4%, worker 1%)\\n\\n    Isolate  70 workers spawned · ~397ms startup each (spawn + environment, per file)\\n             at least ~2.69s faster with isolate: false — reuses workers across files instead of one per file\\n\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"3ce4f3\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000015,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":11,\"output\":\"8a6ce511adffab41f6d9b6b05251ea64c1025db7\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"891a52\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000017209,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":509,\"output\":\"## Routing Evidence\\n\\nFrom a source checkout, build and analyze an audited list of real run directories:\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm run build\\nnode scripts/routing-evidence.mjs --manifest runs.json --out /tmp/routing-evidence\\n```\\n\\n`runs.json` is a JSON array of paths containing `run.json` and `ledger.json`.\\nThe script writes a Markdown report, task CSV, JSON provenance and three SVG\\ncharts. It excludes simulations and active runs, keeps skipped/interrupted\\noutcomes in the denominator, and labels missing historical signals as missing.\\nUnattributed historical decisions are not silently assigned to prior or\\ntrace-driven cohorts. Correlations are descriptive, not cost predictions.\\n\\nAdd `--live-traces` for bounded read-only neatlogs verification using Tally's\\nread token and project id. Without that flag it only replays the output folder's\\ncached `trace-readback.json`, making no API call. Optional `--issues issues.json`\\naccepts a URL-keyed map of current issue titles/bodies for historical runs;\\nthese are labelled current text, not run-start snapshots. No paid workers or\\ncfo.ai writes are performed. Before/after savings require matched measured\\ntasks; missing baseline or v2 cohorts are reported as **not measured**.\\n\\nFor the matched three-pass experiment, add `--comparison-dir <folder>`.\\nThe folder contains `mentor-comparison-plan-signals.json` and, when results\\narrive, `comparison-passes.json`: an object mapping `A`, `B`, `C` to arrays of\\nreal run-directory paths (absolute or relative to that folder). A is top-tier\\nbaseline, B is Tally v1/priors, C is Tally v2/trace history. Missing passes stay\\npending. The report joins signals only at the exact pinned base SHA and task\\ntext, reports cost/verdict/attempts per task and per pass, and charts sizing\\nagainst real costs with per-pass correlations. A pass C label does not itself\\nprove that history influenced every route or that any cap was learned.\\nUse `--comparison-passes <json>` to keep the labelled path manifest elsewhere\\nwithout changing the measured signals folder.\\n\\n## Layout\\n\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a130c9-841c-7440-b5e7-c596eae592f9","create_time":1791819931.003896}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
