{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T15:45:44.158Z","ordinal":16636,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a130c9-841c-7440-b5e7-c596eae592f9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0064f215-853e-404a-9d0e-718d601738bf","process_id":"37546","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '124,173p' README.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '124,173p' README.md","name":"README.md","path":"README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"### Real-Run Evidence\n\nAll four runner/harness paths have completed real runs on chip-design-groundup:\n\n| Path | Real-run PR evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Codex via AO | [#10](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/10) |\n| Claude Code via AO | [#13](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/13), [#16](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/16) |\n| Claude Code direct | [#14](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/14) |\n| Codex direct | [#18](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/18) |\n\nThese runs do not prove every workflow. The following remain unproven live:\n\n- Mixed AO spawning a real Codex worker after a Claude Code worker. The mixed\n  setup proof completed on Claude Code without escalating to Codex.\n- Parallel workers.\n- Escalation on the direct runner.\n- The no-account onboarding path.\n\nThe simulated demo is not evidence of any real worker path.\n\nThree ways in:\n\n1. **npm (primary):** `npm install -g tally-agents`.\n2. **GitHub (alternative, available now):** `npm install -g github:Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack#release`.\n   The `release` branch includes the compiled CLI and records its source commit\n   in `release-source.json`; no TypeScript or manual build is needed. The main\n   branch is source-only and is not the global-install target.\n3. **Source checkout:** `git clone https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack`,\n   enter `neatlogs-hack`, and run `npm install` followed by `npm run build`.\n   Then use `node bin/tally.js` in place of `tally` in the commands below.\n   After editing TypeScript sources, run `npm run build` again. Generated\n   `dist/` files are not committed to main.\n\nThe npm package is named `tally-agents`; the installed command is still\n`tally`.\n\nMaintainers can build a release tree with\n`npm run release:branch -- --source origin/main --out /tmp/tally-release`.\nAdd `--push` to update the dedicated `release` branch (never publishes to npm).\nThe main-push workflow builds and smoke-checks that tree before updating it.\nFor npm publication, pack the built `release` tree, not the source-only main\ncheckout. Check that `release-source.json` identifies the intended main commit,\nthen inspect and smoke-test the tarball before publishing that exact artifact.\nThe built package includes `dist/` and has no build or install lifecycle scripts.\n`npm run test:git-install` checks the GitHub `#release` URL with an empty cache\nand temporary global prefix, then checks version, help, demo and dashboard\noutside the checkout. Pass another Git URL after `--` to check a candidate.\n\n## Quickstart\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"### Real-Run Evidence\n\nAll four runner/harness paths have completed real runs on chip-design-groundup:\n\n| Path | Real-run PR evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Codex via AO | [#10](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/10) |\n| Claude Code via AO | [#13](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/13), [#16](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/16) |\n| Claude Code direct | [#14](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/14) |\n| Codex direct | [#18](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/18) |\n\nThese runs do not prove every workflow. The following remain unproven live:\n\n- Mixed AO spawning a real Codex worker after a Claude Code worker. The mixed\n  setup proof completed on Claude Code without escalating to Codex.\n- Parallel workers.\n- Escalation on the direct runner.\n- The no-account onboarding path.\n\nThe simulated demo is not evidence of any real worker path.\n\nThree ways in:\n\n1. **npm (primary):** `npm install -g tally-agents`.\n2. **GitHub (alternative, available now):** `npm install -g github:Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack#release`.\n   The `release` branch includes the compiled CLI and records its source commit\n   in `release-source.json`; no TypeScript or manual build is needed. The main\n   branch is source-only and is not the global-install target.\n3. **Source checkout:** `git clone https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack`,\n   enter `neatlogs-hack`, and run `npm install` followed by `npm run build`.\n   Then use `node bin/tally.js` in place of `tally` in the commands below.\n   After editing TypeScript sources, run `npm run build` again. Generated\n   `dist/` files are not committed to main.\n\nThe npm package is named `tally-agents`; the installed command is still\n`tally`.\n\nMaintainers can build a release tree with\n`npm run release:branch -- --source origin/main --out /tmp/tally-release`.\nAdd `--push` to update the dedicated `release` branch (never publishes to npm).\nThe main-push workflow builds and smoke-checks that tree before updating it.\nFor npm publication, pack the built `release` tree, not the source-only main\ncheckout. Check that `release-source.json` identifies the intended main commit,\nthen inspect and smoke-test the tarball before publishing that exact artifact.\nThe built package includes `dist/` and has no build or install lifecycle scripts.\n`npm run test:git-install` checks the GitHub `#release` URL with an empty cache\nand temporary global prefix, then checks version, help, demo and dashboard\noutside the checkout. Pass another Git URL after `--` to check a candidate.\n\n## Quickstart\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":53083},"formatted_output":"### Real-Run Evidence\n\nAll four runner/harness paths have completed real runs on chip-design-groundup:\n\n| Path | Real-run PR evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Codex via AO | [#10](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/10) |\n| Claude Code via AO | [#13](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/13), [#16](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/16) |\n| Claude Code direct | [#14](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/14) |\n| Codex direct | [#18](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/18) |\n\nThese runs do not prove every workflow. The following remain unproven live:\n\n- Mixed AO spawning a real Codex worker after a Claude Code worker. The mixed\n  setup proof completed on Claude Code without escalating to Codex.\n- Parallel workers.\n- Escalation on the direct runner.\n- The no-account onboarding path.\n\nThe simulated demo is not evidence of any real worker path.\n\nThree ways in:\n\n1. **npm (primary):** `npm install -g tally-agents`.\n2. **GitHub (alternative, available now):** `npm install -g github:Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack#release`.\n   The `release` branch includes the compiled CLI and records its source commit\n   in `release-source.json`; no TypeScript or manual build is needed. The main\n   branch is source-only and is not the global-install target.\n3. **Source checkout:** `git clone https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack`,\n   enter `neatlogs-hack`, and run `npm install` followed by `npm run build`.\n   Then use `node bin/tally.js` in place of `tally` in the commands below.\n   After editing TypeScript sources, run `npm run build` again. Generated\n   `dist/` files are not committed to main.\n\nThe npm package is named `tally-agents`; the installed command is still\n`tally`.\n\nMaintainers can build a release tree with\n`npm run release:branch -- --source origin/main --out /tmp/tally-release`.\nAdd `--push` to update the dedicated `release` branch (never publishes to npm).\nThe main-push workflow builds and smoke-checks that tree before updating it.\nFor npm publication, pack the built `release` tree, not the source-only main\ncheckout. Check that `release-source.json` identifies the intended main commit,\nthen inspect and smoke-test the tarball before publishing that exact artifact.\nThe built package includes `dist/` and has no build or install lifecycle scripts.\n`npm run test:git-install` checks the GitHub `#release` URL with an empty cache\nand temporary global prefix, then checks version, help, demo and dashboard\noutside the checkout. Pass another Git URL after `--` to check a candidate.\n\n## Quickstart\n"},"started_at_ms":1791819944157,"completed_at_ms":1791819944158}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T15:45:44.477Z","ordinal":16637,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a130ca-921d-7023-8fc0-eee6bf6c817d","call_id":"call_ed5eTqqQPOdgbBEKtSYPEftE","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"24baa9\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.003409792,\"session_id\":61186,\"original_token_count\":31,\"output\":\"\\n> tally-agents@0.2.0 test\\n> vitest run\\n\\n\\n RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5\\n\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"a429d8\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000053083,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":660,\"output\":\"### Real-Run Evidence\\n\\nAll four runner/harness paths have completed real runs on chip-design-groundup:\\n\\n| Path | Real-run PR evidence |\\n|---|---|\\n| Codex via AO | [#10](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/10) |\\n| Claude Code via AO | [#13](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/13), [#16](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/16) |\\n| Claude Code direct | [#14](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/14) |\\n| Codex direct | [#18](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/18) |\\n\\nThese runs do not prove every workflow. The following remain unproven live:\\n\\n- Mixed AO spawning a real Codex worker after a Claude Code worker. The mixed\\n  setup proof completed on Claude Code without escalating to Codex.\\n- Parallel workers.\\n- Escalation on the direct runner.\\n- The no-account onboarding path.\\n\\nThe simulated demo is not evidence of any real worker path.\\n\\nThree ways in:\\n\\n1. **npm (primary):** `npm install -g tally-agents`.\\n2. **GitHub (alternative, available now):** `npm install -g github:Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack#release`.\\n   The `release` branch includes the compiled CLI and records its source commit\\n   in `release-source.json`; no TypeScript or manual build is needed. The main\\n   branch is source-only and is not the global-install target.\\n3. **Source checkout:** `git clone https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack`,\\n   enter `neatlogs-hack`, and run `npm install` followed by `npm run build`.\\n   Then use `node bin/tally.js` in place of `tally` in the commands below.\\n   After editing TypeScript sources, run `npm run build` again. Generated\\n   `dist/` files are not committed to main.\\n\\nThe npm package is named `tally-agents`; the installed command is still\\n`tally`.\\n\\nMaintainers can build a release tree with\\n`npm run release:branch -- --source origin/main --out /tmp/tally-release`.\\nAdd `--push` to update the dedicated `release` branch (never publishes to npm).\\nThe main-push workflow builds and smoke-checks that tree before updating it.\\nFor npm publication, pack the built `release` tree, not the source-only main\\ncheckout. Check that `release-source.json` identifies the intended main commit,\\nthen inspect and smoke-test the tarball before publishing that exact artifact.\\nThe built package includes `dist/` and has no build or install lifecycle scripts.\\n`npm run test:git-install` checks the GitHub `#release` URL with an empty cache\\nand temporary global prefix, then checks version, help, demo and dashboard\\noutside the checkout. Pass another Git URL after `--` to check a candidate.\\n\\n## Quickstart\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a130c9-841c-7440-b5e7-c596eae592f9","create_time":1791819944.477482}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
