{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T15:55:17.516Z","ordinal":16742,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_004274e0102b2ff9016acd02dd62308191a7163bf64d8ba72c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_442c54051a4e4ebe80cdaf0e6e250b0c","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh pr create --base main --head ao/neatlogs-hack-5/business-plan --title 'Finalize evidence-backed Tally business plan' --body '## Summary\\n- Add docs/BUSINESS_PLAN.md and link it from README; docs only.\\n- Separate the three-task measured comparison from commercial assumptions, report history limitations, runner/parallel/cap proofs, and the 20 hiring-intent lead signal without market-size claims.\\n- Explain share-of-savings pricing, agreed baselines, cfo.ai usage and the concurrency/link-sharing gaps.\\n\\n## Validation\\n- Base 8a6ce51: full suite 874 tests passed with localhost access. Initial sandbox-only run failed solely on dashboard listen EPERM.\\n- git diff --check clean; savings percentages and $480 scenario arithmetic checked.\\n\\n## Important Clarifications\\n- The proposed 80% routable saving is ABOVE the measured aggregate 65-75%, not below it. It is below an earlier roughly 95% same-token price gap, which was not measured task savings. The document explicitly labels this assumption as unvalidated.\\n- Existing cfo.ai page is linked; this PR does not synchronize or write to that page.\\n- No runtime changes, paid runs or customer claims.'\",\"sandbox_permissions\":\"require_escalated\",\"justification\":\"Open the expressly requested small docs-only business-plan PR against main.\",\"max_output_tokens\":1000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a130c9-841c-7440-b5e7-c596eae592f9","create_time":1791820509.4311924}}}
