{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:25:18.575Z","ordinal":16885,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a13190-4b5d-74c2-9db6-6b4f1c0c4022","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_004274e0102b2ff9016acd34187ab481919fe57fa85af7942e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"[PR #166](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/166) is open: version-only bump, including the matching CLI constant. Version test and typecheck pass. Awaiting the merged commit for packaging; no publish.\n\n1. Fresh init explicitly asks for “budget, spend and Ari context”; re-init only asks to enable cfo.ai, leaving an upgrade-consent gap.\n2. Init adds/updates only the Tally-marked guide block and enables `publishRunContext`.\n3. Real-attempt reports send task/title/IDs, repository, issue URL, sizing, model/prices/tokens/cost, outcome/decision, budget snapshots and evidence links to organization-scoped memory.\n4. Reports exclude issue bodies, code/diffs, prompts/transcripts and raw traces; dry runs send none. Free-text redaction cannot guarantee all sensitive data is removed.\n5. #152 adds subprocess-scoped GitHub credentials and one push retry, not new financial writes; automatic cfo.ai URL sharing in PRs remains without a dedicated question."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1791833112531,"completed_at_ms":1791833118575}}
