{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:36:30.523Z","ordinal":17080,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_05aac4860f45c66e016acd3697b3c88191bc68900e5c900c5e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_7cc7fe5775dd47bc8c44f77e91e2c91c","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/release-021/report.md\\n+# Tally 0.2.1 Pre-Release Audit\\n+\\n+Source: `ceddd6a23e7d57dd69f5ba240aa34218647a47c2`.\\n+Built release: `8bd995664a27faf8dc647dab3673f6186a45f482`.\\n+release-source.json matches exactly. Remote main was checked before packing,\\n+before each runtime's checks and after completion; it remained at this source.\\n+No publish, login, tag, GitHub release or paid worker was attempted.\\n+\\n+## Package\\n+\\n+- Tarball: `/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/release-021/tally-agents-0.2.1.tgz`\\n+- 294 files; 503,883 compressed bytes; 1,829,399 unpacked bytes.\\n+- SHA256: `84a18ecbbabb3611a147699c2e66c8b2fdcb9cd62d09b54d185ac6e03e0a5aed`\\n+- Full file list and npm integrity metadata: `inventory.json` alongside this report.\\n+\\n+Packed from the built release, not a source checkout. Includes bin/tally.js,\\n+dist, dashboard, schemas, README, LICENSE, business-plan documentation and\\n+release-source.json. No tests/test helpers, external-services guard or real-runs\\n+guard, site/, unnecessary scripts, .env, .tally, .claude, .codex or node_modules.\\n+Known configured credential values were checked against packed content without\\n+printing any values; none matched. The release manifest has no lifecycle\\n+scripts or development dependencies; installed runtime packages contain no Vitest.\\n+\\n+## Clean Install Checks\\n+\\n+Independent new prefixes and initially empty caches were used for the default\\n+Node 26.8.2 runtime and Node 20.20.2. Both passed:\\n+\\n+| Check | Result |\\n+| --- | --- |\\n+| tally --version | 0.2.1, exit 0 |\\n+| tally logo, non-TTY | Static uncoloured mark, exit 0 |\\n+| tally logo, TTY | Animation completes, final ANSI reset/cursor-show, exit 0 |\\n+| tally demo | 7 tasks, 9 attempts, 6 passed and 1 intentional failure; simulated spend $1.7063 |\\n+| tally doctor in scratch repo, empty HOME | Expected exit 1: missing GitHub authentication, optional integrations off |\\n+| tally doctor with valid existing project config | Exit 0 |\\n+| tally init --help | Exit 0; no onboarding writes performed |\\n+| tally run --plan | Exit 0; parallelWorkers: 2 and modelAccessFallbackTier: middle accepted |\\n+| tally market --replay | Exit 0; cached job-intent report, no CrustData call |\\n+| Unchanged 0.1.0-style config | Two tasks pass sequentially despite legacy concurrency: 3 |\\n+| Unchanged 0.2.0 audit config | New parallel/fallback fields retained; two tasks pass |\\n+\\n+Upgrade checks execute the installed real loop with fake intake/worker/usage/\\n+sizing ports; no real worker starts. 0.1.0 asserts start/end/start/end ordering.\\n+0.2.0 uses the exact config retained from the previous release audit.\\n+\\n+The first plan attempt correctly failed because the former fly-doom-jev AO\\n+project had been removed. The completed audit instead used a separate scratch\\n+plan config reading the registered chip-design-groundup project and repository,\\n+without changing its settings. Integrations were off, the backlog was a local\\n+sample, and plan/doctor did not spawn workers or write PRs/cfo.ai data.\\n+\\n+npm warned about unapproved protobufjs dependency postinstall scripts; no\\n+allow-scripts override was used. Runtime checks passed without those scripts.\\n+Source-suite validation was separately gated by the orchestrator: 882 tests\\n+twice, typecheck, build and three dry runs. These package checks do not replace\\n+lane A's paid sanity run and do not re-prove live integration delivery.\\n+\\n+## Five-Line Consent Review of #150 and #152\\n+\\n+1. Fresh interactive init asks \\\"Use cfo.ai for budget, spend and Ari context?\\\"; this covers the combined feature, not an independent reports-only choice.\\n+2. Re-init asks only \\\"Enable cfo.ai integration?\\\" and can add the guide/enable reporting for an existing user without the fresh-init Ari wording; --yes/dry-run do not run external re-onboarding.\\n+3. Init writes only the Tally-marked scenario-page guide; real attempts, with publishRunContext enabled, send organization-memory documents via edit_memory with repository/run/task title and IDs/issue URL, size/confidence/graph counts, model/provider/prices/tokens/cost, ceiling/outcome/decision/result note/timestamps/commit, budget snapshots and evidence URLs.\\n+4. The payload excludes issue bodies, code/diffs, prompts/transcripts and raw spans; dry runs send no reports. Free-text fields are sanitized but cannot guarantee all sensitive content is excluded. Reports are shared with workspace members.\\n+5. #152 adds GitHub credentials only in push subprocesses and one retry, not new finance data types; finance-table URL posting to task PRs still has no dedicated init disclosure/opt-in.\\n+\\n+## Publish Command for the Maintainer\\n+\\n+Run only after the orchestrator approves and lane A's final sanity run passes:\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+npm publish /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/release-021/tally-agents-0.2.1.tgz --access public --tag latest --registry https://registry.npmjs.org --otp '<2FA_CODE>'\\n+```\\n+\\n+This command was not run. Earlier release-020/ and release-020b/ artifacts are untouched.\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"ao report --done --note \\\"0.2.1 package audit complete; no publish/paid runs. Source ceddd6a23e7d57dd69f5ba240aa34218647a47c2, built release 8bd995664a27faf8dc647dab3673f6186a45f482. Main stayed pinned across checks. release-021/tally-agents-0.2.1.tgz: 294 files, 503883 bytes, SHA256 84a18ecbbabb3611a147699c2e66c8b2fdcb9cd62d09b54d185ac6e03e0a5aed. Empty-cache fresh prefixes default Node26 and Node20 pass version, TTY/nonTTY logo, demo, doctor (empty-HOME expected missing auth; configured exit0), init help, plan with new fields, replay, unchanged 0.1 sequential and 0.2 configs. No guards/tests/settings/site/known credentials packed. Old removed flydoom project initially blocked plan; final check reads registered chip project only, changes nothing. Consent concerns preserved in report: fresh init asks combined Ari context; re-init generic question can enable reports; PR finance URLs still lack dedicated disclosure. OTP command in attached report; awaiting lane A sanity gate.\\\" --artifact /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/release-021/report.md\",\"sandbox_permissions\":\"require_escalated\",\"justification\":\"Deliver the completed authorized 0.2.1 package audit, consent findings and maintainer publish command without publishing.\",\"max_output_tokens\":500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a13198-29de-7b21-baeb-0750d37549c2","create_time":1791833751.7053127}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:36:31.189Z","ordinal":17081,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a13198-29de-7b21-baeb-0750d37549c2","session_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","root_turn_id":"01a13198-29de-7b21-baeb-0750d37549c2","response_id":"resp_05aac4860f45c66e016acd3694b0cc819186e04f6fbfb1fcc8","usage":{"input_tokens":168394,"cached_input_tokens":166656,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1747,"reasoning_output_tokens":14,"total_tokens":170141},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":4346171,"cached_input_tokens":4323456,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6613,"reasoning_output_tokens":786,"total_tokens":4352784},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":270398148,"cached_input_tokens":262849024,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":941782,"reasoning_output_tokens":206216,"total_tokens":271339930}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:36:37.544Z","ordinal":17082,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a13198-29de-7b21-baeb-0750d37549c2","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-655798a7-bd86-4841-bad3-bf0f8d1886fd","changes":{"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/release-021/report.md":{"type":"add","content":"# Tally 0.2.1 Pre-Release Audit\n\nSource: `ceddd6a23e7d57dd69f5ba240aa34218647a47c2`.\nBuilt release: `8bd995664a27faf8dc647dab3673f6186a45f482`.\nrelease-source.json matches exactly. Remote main was checked before packing,\nbefore each runtime's checks and after completion; it remained at this source.\nNo publish, login, tag, GitHub release or paid worker was attempted.\n\n## Package\n\n- Tarball: `/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/release-021/tally-agents-0.2.1.tgz`\n- 294 files; 503,883 compressed bytes; 1,829,399 unpacked bytes.\n- SHA256: `84a18ecbbabb3611a147699c2e66c8b2fdcb9cd62d09b54d185ac6e03e0a5aed`\n- Full file list and npm integrity metadata: `inventory.json` alongside this report.\n\nPacked from the built release, not a source checkout. Includes bin/tally.js,\ndist, dashboard, schemas, README, LICENSE, business-plan documentation and\nrelease-source.json. No tests/test helpers, external-services guard or real-runs\nguard, site/, unnecessary scripts, .env, .tally, .claude, .codex or node_modules.\nKnown configured credential values were checked against packed content without\nprinting any values; none matched. The release manifest has no lifecycle\nscripts or development dependencies; installed runtime packages contain no Vitest.\n\n## Clean Install Checks\n\nIndependent new prefixes and initially empty caches were used for the default\nNode 26.8.2 runtime and Node 20.20.2. Both passed:\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| tally --version | 0.2.1, exit 0 |\n| tally logo, non-TTY | Static uncoloured mark, exit 0 |\n| tally logo, TTY | Animation completes, final ANSI reset/cursor-show, exit 0 |\n| tally demo | 7 tasks, 9 attempts, 6 passed and 1 intentional failure; simulated spend $1.7063 |\n| tally doctor in scratch repo, empty HOME | Expected exit 1: missing GitHub authentication, optional integrations off |\n| tally doctor with valid existing project config | Exit 0 |\n| tally init --help | Exit 0; no onboarding writes performed |\n| tally run --plan | Exit 0; parallelWorkers: 2 and modelAccessFallbackTier: middle accepted |\n| tally market --replay | Exit 0; cached job-intent report, no CrustData call |\n| Unchanged 0.1.0-style config | Two tasks pass sequentially despite legacy concurrency: 3 |\n| Unchanged 0.2.0 audit config | New parallel/fallback fields retained; two tasks pass |\n\nUpgrade checks execute the installed real loop with fake intake/worker/usage/\nsizing ports; no real worker starts. 0.1.0 asserts start/end/start/end ordering.\n0.2.0 uses the exact config retained from the previous release audit.\n\nThe first plan attempt correctly failed because the former fly-doom-jev AO\nproject had been removed. The completed audit instead used a separate scratch\nplan config reading the registered chip-design-groundup project and repository,\nwithout changing its settings. Integrations were off, the backlog was a local\nsample, and plan/doctor did not spawn workers or write PRs/cfo.ai data.\n\nnpm warned about unapproved protobufjs dependency postinstall scripts; no\nallow-scripts override was used. Runtime checks passed without those scripts.\nSource-suite validation was separately gated by the orchestrator: 882 tests\ntwice, typecheck, build and three dry runs. These package checks do not replace\nlane A's paid sanity run and do not re-prove live integration delivery.\n\n## Five-Line Consent Review of #150 and #152\n\n1. Fresh interactive init asks \"Use cfo.ai for budget, spend and Ari context?\"; this covers the combined feature, not an independent reports-only choice.\n2. Re-init asks only \"Enable cfo.ai integration?\" and can add the guide/enable reporting for an existing user without the fresh-init Ari wording; --yes/dry-run do not run external re-onboarding.\n3. Init writes only the Tally-marked scenario-page guide; real attempts, with publishRunContext enabled, send organization-memory documents via edit_memory with repository/run/task title and IDs/issue URL, size/confidence/graph counts, model/provider/prices/tokens/cost, ceiling/outcome/decision/result note/timestamps/commit, budget snapshots and evidence URLs.\n4. The payload excludes issue bodies, code/diffs, prompts/transcripts and raw spans; dry runs send no reports. Free-text fields are sanitized but cannot guarantee all sensitive content is excluded. Reports are shared with workspace members.\n5. #152 adds GitHub credentials only in push subprocesses and one retry, not new finance data types; finance-table URL posting to task PRs still has no dedicated init disclosure/opt-in.\n\n## Publish Command for the Maintainer\n\nRun only after the orchestrator approves and lane A's final sanity run passes:\n\n```sh\nnpm publish /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/release-021/tally-agents-0.2.1.tgz --access public --tag latest --registry https://registry.npmjs.org --otp '<2FA_CODE>'\n```\n\nThis command was not run. Earlier release-020/ and release-020b/ artifacts are untouched.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/release-021/report.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1791833794554,"completed_at_ms":1791833797544}}
