{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:50:23.854Z","ordinal":17095,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a131aa-8f6e-7c02-97fe-3685cf735a3c","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"[from neatlogs-hack-8] New task from Vaibhaav: redo the README and add an agent-readable guide. One PR from main ceddd6a (docs and package 'files' only; no behaviour change). \n\n(1) README.md, rewritten for a first-time reader, in this order: the banner image at the very top; one sentence on what Tally is; install (npm install -g tally-agents); a 60-second quick start (tally init, tally run --plan, tally run --budget N --dashboard) with a short real output excerpt; what Tally does (route, cap, escalate, verify, open a pull request; never merges); the two runners and the two agents (Agent Orchestrator for parallel, direct for one at a time; Claude Code and Codex); what neatlogs, Entire and cfo.ai each add, and what happens when each is off; evidence, with real numbers and their limits (the three-pass comparison: 1.22 USD on the top tier against 0.31 and 0.43 through Tally, 3 of 3 passing each time, three tasks, one run each, list-price estimates; cap-and-escalate fly-doom-jev PR #17; parallel run; a learned ceiling from neatlogs history); what Tally asks your consent for and what it sends where (the Claude allow-list, the Entire settings commit to the default branch, cfo.ai spend write-back, the per-attempt reports to the cfo.ai workspace, evidence links on PRs), stated plainly; known limits; links to docs/GETTING_STARTED.md, docs/BUSINESS_PLAN.md, the site https://tally-agents-pi.vercel.app and npm; licence. Keep it accurate to the code on main: check 'npm view tally-agents version' when you write it and name the version that is actually published. Cut the long historical proof logs from the README into docs/EVIDENCE.md and link it; lose nothing true.\n\n(2) The banner: the file is /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-readme-banner.png (the pixel Tally mark, 'Meet Tally, the CFO for your agent fleet', dark slate). Commit it as docs/assets/tally-banner.png and reference it in the README with the absolute raw GitHub URL on main so it also renders on the npm page; give it alt text; do NOT add docs/assets to the npm package 'files'.\n\n(3) The agent-readable guide: a single self-contained file an AI coding agent can read when a person says 'use Tally on this repo' and then drive Tally correctly without other context. Put it at docs/AGENT_GUIDE.md, add it to the package 'files' so it ships with npm, link it from the README under a heading agents will find ('For AI agents'), and add a root llms.txt that points to it and to the getting-started guide. Write it as instructions to an agent: preconditions to check and the exact commands to check them (node version, gh auth status, which agents are signed in, ao status if present, tally --version); the decision points it must put to the human rather than decide itself, each named (budget and caps, runner, agents and tiers, each integration, the Claude allow-list, the Entire commit to the default branch, cfo.ai reports); the non-interactive forms of each command with their flags, from 'tally init --help' and 'tally run --help' on main, not from memory; how to read tally run --plan and what to tell the human before spending; how to start a run, where run.json and ledger.json are and how to read status, cost, result and failureAssessment from them; what each failure looks like and the correct response (reservation does not fit, AO project not found, signed-out agent, missing consent, ceiling stop, verify failed, integration errors); hard rules: never merge Tally's pull requests, never push to a default branch, never use bypass or danger flags, never edit tally.yaml to skip a consent, never run two tally runs against one cfo.ai page at once, never paste keys; and how to report back to the human at the end (PR links, cost, what failed and why). Verify every command in it by running it (plan and dry-run only, no paid runs). Tell me the PR number."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","create_time":1791834623.854549,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a131aa-8f6e-7c02-97fe-3685cf735a3c","turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","role":"user"},"revision":"retained_01a131aa-8f6e-7c02-97fe-36a521457910","complete":false},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":1685,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"complete","sources":[{"server_name":"node_repl","tool_name":"js","first_turn_id":"01a12a97-e4ab-7890-8387-c5ab0eeee751"},{"server_name":"ao","tool_name":"html_preview","first_turn_id":"01a12f92-ff72-7412-8b38-fb74800a991a"},{"server_name":"ao","tool_name":"html_render","first_turn_id":"01a12fc0-e6ed-70d3-9280-cf68527cb68a"}]}}}
