n(2) The banner: the file is /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-8/tally-readme-banner.png (the pixel Tally mark, 'Meet Tally, the CFO for your agent fleet', dark slate). Commit it as docs/assets/tally-banner.png and reference it in the README with the absolute raw GitHub URL on main so it also renders on the npm page; give it alt text; do NOT add docs/assets to the npm package 'files'.\n\n(3) The agent-readable guide: a single self-contained file an AI coding agent can read when a person says 'use Tally on this repo' and then drive Tally correctly without other context. Put it at docs/AGENT_GUIDE.md, add it to the package 'files' so it ships with npm, link it from the README under a heading agents will find ('For AI agents'), and add a root llms.txt that points to it and to the getting-started guide. Write it as instructions to an agent: preconditions to check and the exact commands to check them (node version, gh auth status, which agents are signed in, ao status if present, tally --version); the decision points it must put to the human rather than decide itself, each named (budget and caps, runner, agents and tiers, each integration, the Claude allow-list, the Entire commit to the default branch, cfo.ai reports); the non-interactive forms of each command with their flags, from 'tally init --help' and 'tally run --help' on main, not from memory; how to read tally run --plan and what to tell the human before spending; how to start a run, where run.json and ledger.json are and how to read status, cost, result and failureAssessment from them; what each failure looks like and the correct response (reservation does not fit, AO project not found, signed-out agent, missing consent, ceiling stop, verify failed, integration errors); hard rules: never merge Tally's pull requests, never push to a default branch, never use bypass or danger flags, never edit tally.yaml to skip a consent, never run two tally runs against one cfo.ai page at once, never paste keys; and how to report back to the human at the end (PR links, cost, what failed and why). Verify every command in it by running it (plan and dry-run only, no paid runs). Tell me the PR number.","text_elements":[]}]},"started_at_ms":1791834623855,"completed_at_ms":1791834623855}}
