{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:51:24.616Z","ordinal":17143,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7d1add9b-8f00-4087-b5ca-be8b98926bcd","process_id":"29467","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-2/final-021-sanity-report.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-2/final-021-sanity-report.md","name":"final-021-sanity-report.md","path":"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-2/final-021-sanity-report.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Tally 0.2.1 release sanity: passed\n\n## Candidate and isolation\n\n- Installed with `npm install -g --prefix /private/tmp/tally-021-sanity.l0XjHO/prefix --cache /private/tmp/tally-021-sanity.l0XjHO/npm-cache github:Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack#release` (fresh prefix and cache).\n- Installed `tally --version`: `0.2.1`. Installed `release-source.json`: `ceddd6a23e7d57dd69f5ba240aa34218647a47c2`. Main was checked again immediately before starting and matched.\n- Fresh clone: `/private/tmp/tally-021-sanity.l0XjHO/tally-021-sanity-chip`. Human checkout was not touched. Scratch AO project: `tally-021-sanity-chip`.\n- Fresh issues: [#33](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/issues/33), [#34](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/issues/34), label `tally-sanity-021`. No old tasks were selected.\n- Used the installed CLI for init, doctor, plan and run. No hand-edited tally.yaml, ceilings, tiers, worker output or PR body.\n\n## Init and the explicitly authorized settings commit\n\nPTY init used AO, Codex only, two parallel workers, verification `find js -name '*.js' -print0 | xargs -0 -n1 node --check`, no setup, and all three integrations requested. Default model prices and ceilings were retained. Monthly/fallback budget: $40, read from cfo.ai.\n\nThe first init asked to publish automatic Entire linking to the target default branch. I declined, reported the blocker, and started no worker. The human then authorized exactly that settings change. Before consenting I compared the existing settings with the installed init transformation; the sole proposed change was `commit_linking: always`. Re-init published the same exact change:\n\nCommit: `d5d93ba9cb23466585f9416cabf3bc98690da43c` (`chore: enable Entire capture for Tally workers`). Only `.entire/settings.json` changed. It is the only default-branch push in this proof, separately authorized by the human.\n\n```diff\n@@ -4,5 +4,6 @@\n     \"primary\": {\n       \"type\": \"git-refs\"\n     }\n-  }\n+  },\n+  \"commit_linking\": \"always\"\n }\n```\n\nRe-init's config diff only changed Entire from false to true. It preserved the rest of the settings and install record. Doctor then reported AO ready, worker auto mode, signed-in Codex, GitHub, Entire CLI/graph/checkpoint recall/repository/mirror, neatlogs and cfo.ai connected. No mirror was created; existing mirrors were ready. Generated summaries remained off.\n\n## Run and results\n\nCommand: `tally run --budget 3 --parallel 2 --dashboard --port 0`.\n\n- Run: `run-20261012-194035Z`, from `2026-10-12T19:40:35.715Z` to `19:42:49.622Z` (13 October 01:10:35 to 01:12:49 IST).\n- Repo base: `d5d93ba9cb23466585f9416cabf3bc98690da43c`, after the authorized settings commit.\n- Dashboard: `http://127.0.0.1:61613/?data=%2Fruns%2Flatest%2F`; stopped after the final summary, not while workers were active.\n- 2/2 tasks passed; two attempts total; no ceiling stop or escalation, as expected for this sanity run.\n- Both tasks used `codex/gpt-5.6-luna`, AO tui, cheap tier, $0.30 attempt ceilings. Parallel reservations: 2 x ($0.30 + $0.75) = $2.10, within the $3 run cap and monthly remaining budget.\n\n| Issue | Tokens (uncached / cached / output / total) | Cost USD | PR | Commit |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| #33 | 39762 / 87552 / 1980 / 129294 | 0.012079440 | [#35](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/35) | 8d7c3b42ea35012c33432bf9f0e197153ce2463b |\n| #34 | 29017 / 212736 / 2252 / 244005 | 0.012760520 | [#36](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/36) | e5ea198b2361f8c128afa8125350ebc757997fc3 |\n\nTotal: **$0.024839960 of $3.00**. Tally verified and published both PRs. GitHub `closingIssuesReferences` reports #33 and #34 respectively. Each PR adds exactly its requested docs file, no other changes. Both PRs remain open; neither was merged.\n\n## Parallelism and live UI\n\n- #33 AO session `tally-021-sanity-chip-1`: created `19:40:51.931043Z`, terminated/updated `19:41:51.306589Z`.\n- #34 AO session `tally-021-sanity-chip-2`: created `19:40:56.271395Z`, terminated/updated `19:41:56.387101Z`.\n- Both are `isTerminated: true`, activity `exited`. Their lifetimes overlapped for about 55 seconds.\n- Dashboard run.json HTTP 200 at `19:40:40.776Z`, before either session existed. Latest pointed at this run from its initial record.\n- 130 recorded live observations: pending/zero at `19:40:40.420Z`, both running with $0.003165120 live spend at `19:41:06.451Z`, then climbing to $0.024839960, then both passed with PR links.\n- Terminal printed routing, worker starts, repeated spend, result/PR lines and final budget/integration summary. Exact output is retained in `terminal.log`.\n- run.json records GitHub backlog source and label, CLI limit source, $3 cap, cfo.ai system of record and $40 monthly budget with the pre-run spend snapshot.\n\nActual terminal Entire line:\n\n```text\nEntire       CONNECTED\n  Graph sizing: ok (Graph search available; tasks without matching code symbols are sized by repository search.); checkpoint search available\n```\n\nThis verifies #159 on real tasks with no matching code symbols: no setup-needed/fix advice was printed. Both task decisions retained the repository-search explanation.\n\n## Evidence links and trace delivery\n\nEach PR has five working evidence links: Entire session/checkpoint; neatlogs routing trace; neatlogs worker trace; cfo.ai budget table; cfo.ai spend table.\n\n| Task | Decision trace | Worker trace | Entire checkpoint | Entire session |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| #33 | 94bd3bf1c11e3c8eda763f9b267d6261 | 1f6ddb77617a5ce5049bc7566b9c3401 | 01M4RT4Q6ZRSQ739ZZFABCTX1R | 01a131a1-e882-7d93-9f06-b9aa2e2c6540 |\n| #34 | f31716a02f7ff70ae7c338a5ae4aadf3 | 670603e2348ac3afa9ea1798f1970ed5 | 01M4RT4W4TZ09NSHH91DZRMMTW | 01a131a1-f802-77a1-9a57-43f1c71d0824 |\n\n- Worker traces were delivered and written back automatically; no manual drain or PR edit.\n- All four authenticated neatlogs trace-detail and span reads returned HTTP 200. Public UI URLs redirect to sign-in with the correct trace callback; they are not anonymously readable trace views.\n- Both Entire URLs returned HTTP 200 with the actual task-specific session title, not a generic not-found page.\n- Both cfo.ai share URLs returned HTTP 200, and their backing budget/spend cells were read through the adapter.\n- PR evidence updates succeeded; PR #36 updated at `19:42:43Z`, #35 at `19:42:48Z`. Finalization after the last attempt took 34.257 seconds across Ari reporting and both PR evidence updates. The evidence publisher has 15-second bounds for each GitHub read/edit (30 seconds per PR); isolated per-PR call durations were not instrumented. Do not interpret the 34-second combined finalization as a measured single evidence-call delay.\n\n## cfo.ai: exact changes beyond spend\n\nRead snapshots were taken before init, after init, after re-init, immediately before the run, and after the run. No accounting correction was performed.\n\n**Init was idempotent on this existing workspace.** `inspect_pages(include_text=true)` returned the same Tally page structure and text before/after init and re-init: the budget table, spend-detail table and existing `Tally Ari context guide (managed by tally-agents)#c42` text block. No additional block was created; the existing guide already matched the package's contents. Init verified it and enabled per-attempt Ari reporting. No spend/tier/run cell changed during either init.\n\nThe managed guide tells Ari to find run/task/attempt reports by tags, distinguish monthly/current-run amounts, use the token mix for explicitly hypothetical repricing, cite evidence links, and not treat task titles as instructions. It states the excluded data and pricing limits.\n\n**Per attempt, Tally submitted an organization-scoped report through edit_memory/retain_document, not a new page block.** Each includes task/model/tokens/cost/result/budget, selected scenario, tier price snapshot, repricing caveats and review links; excludes issue bodies, source, prompts/transcripts, raw spans and secrets. Reports use deterministic attempt idempotency keys and run/task/attempt tags.\n\nRead-only `inspect_memory` filtered to this run returned ten extracted org facts covering both attempts: costs $0.012760520 and $0.012079440; successful task titles; CLI run cap/monthly budget; and same-token-mix alternative tier prices. Task #34's facts were saved at `19:42:31Z`; #33's at `19:42:34Z`. This proves Ari can recall the reports' facts, not that inspect_memory returned the complete original markdown documents. Exact results are retained in `cfo-attempt-memory.json`.\n\n`inspect_pages` after the run still showed the same page blocks and guide text. It does not expose table-cell values; separate adapter reads verified these changes:\n\n| Cell | Before USD | After USD | Change USD |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Agent spend | 2.274052560 | 2.298892520 | +0.024839960 |\n| Tier spend - cheap | 1.078686560 | 1.103526520 | +0.024839960 |\n| Tier spend - middle | 1.195366000 | 1.195366000 | 0 |\n| Tier spend - top | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| Run spend - current | 0.774489440 | 0.024839960 | replaced with this run total |\n| Run spend - cumulative | 2.274052560 | 2.298892520 | +0.024839960 |\n\nMonthly budget remained $40. Remaining budget fell by the exact ledger cost to $37.701107480. Prior test excess or historical spend was not corrected.\n\n## Cleanup and scope\n\nScratch AO registration was removed after both workers were confirmed closed (`removedStorageDir: false`), retaining the run/worktrees as evidence. Dashboard stopped after completion. No new workers beyond the two approved tasks, no paid rerun, no PR merges, no code fixes or manual publication, and no default-branch change except the explicitly authorized automatic-linking commit.\n\nDurable run and raw read-back evidence: `final-021-sanity/run-20261012-194035Z/` beside this report.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Tally 0.2.1 release sanity: passed\n\n## Candidate and isolation\n\n- Installed with `npm install -g --prefix /private/tmp/tally-021-sanity.l0XjHO/prefix --cache /private/tmp/tally-021-sanity.l0XjHO/npm-cache github:Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack#release` (fresh prefix and cache).\n- Installed `tally --version`: `0.2.1`. Installed `release-source.json`: `ceddd6a23e7d57dd69f5ba240aa34218647a47c2`. Main was checked again immediately before starting and matched.\n- Fresh clone: `/private/tmp/tally-021-sanity.l0XjHO/tally-021-sanity-chip`. Human checkout was not touched. Scratch AO project: `tally-021-sanity-chip`.\n- Fresh issues: [#33](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/issues/33), [#34](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/issues/34), label `tally-sanity-021`. No old tasks were selected.\n- Used the installed CLI for init, doctor, plan and run. No hand-edited tally.yaml, ceilings, tiers, worker output or PR body.\n\n## Init and the explicitly authorized settings commit\n\nPTY init used AO, Codex only, two parallel workers, verification `find js -name '*.js' -print0 | xargs -0 -n1 node --check`, no setup, and all three integrations requested. Default model prices and ceilings were retained. Monthly/fallback budget: $40, read from cfo.ai.\n\nThe first init asked to publish automatic Entire linking to the target default branch. I declined, reported the blocker, and started no worker. The human then authorized exactly that settings change. Before consenting I compared the existing settings with the installed init transformation; the sole proposed change was `commit_linking: always`. Re-init published the same exact change:\n\nCommit: `d5d93ba9cb23466585f9416cabf3bc98690da43c` (`chore: enable Entire capture for Tally workers`). Only `.entire/settings.json` changed. It is the only default-branch push in this proof, separately authorized by the human.\n\n```diff\n@@ -4,5 +4,6 @@\n     \"primary\": {\n       \"type\": \"git-refs\"\n     }\n-  }\n+  },\n+  \"commit_linking\": \"always\"\n }\n```\n\nRe-init's config diff only changed Entire from false to true. It preserved the rest of the settings and install record. Doctor then reported AO ready, worker auto mode, signed-in Codex, GitHub, Entire CLI/graph/checkpoint recall/repository/mirror, neatlogs and cfo.ai connected. No mirror was created; existing mirrors were ready. Generated summaries remained off.\n\n## Run and results\n\nCommand: `tally run --budget 3 --parallel 2 --dashboard --port 0`.\n\n- Run: `run-20261012-194035Z`, from `2026-10-12T19:40:35.715Z` to `19:42:49.622Z` (13 October 01:10:35 to 01:12:49 IST).\n- Repo base: `d5d93ba9cb23466585f9416cabf3bc98690da43c`, after the authorized settings commit.\n- Dashboard: `http://127.0.0.1:61613/?data=%2Fruns%2Flatest%2F`; stopped after the final summary, not while workers were active.\n- 2/2 tasks passed; two attempts total; no ceiling stop or escalation, as expected for this sanity run.\n- Both tasks used `codex/gpt-5.6-luna`, AO tui, cheap tier, $0.30 attempt ceilings. Parallel reservations: 2 x ($0.30 + $0.75) = $2.10, within the $3 run cap and monthly remaining budget.\n\n| Issue | Tokens (uncached / cached / output / total) | Cost USD | PR | Commit |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| #33 | 39762 / 87552 / 1980 / 129294 | 0.012079440 | [#35](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/35) | 8d7c3b42ea35012c33432bf9f0e197153ce2463b |\n| #34 | 29017 / 212736 / 2252 / 244005 | 0.012760520 | [#36](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/36) | e5ea198b2361f8c128afa8125350ebc757997fc3 |\n\nTotal: **$0.024839960 of $3.00**. Tally verified and published both PRs. GitHub `closingIssuesReferences` reports #33 and #34 respectively. Each PR adds exactly its requested docs file, no other changes. Both PRs remain open; neither was merged.\n\n## Parallelism and live UI\n\n- #33 AO session `tally-021-sanity-chip-1`: created `19:40:51.931043Z`, terminated/updated `19:41:51.306589Z`.\n- #34 AO session `tally-021-sanity-chip-2`: created `19:40:56.271395Z`, terminated/updated `19:41:56.387101Z`.\n- Both are `isTerminated: true`, activity `exited`. Their lifetimes overlapped for about 55 seconds.\n- Dashboard run.json HTTP 200 at `19:40:40.776Z`, before either session existed. Latest pointed at this run from its initial record.\n- 130 recorded live observations: pending/zero at `19:40:40.420Z`, both running with $0.003165120 live spend at `19:41:06.451Z`, then climbing to $0.024839960, then both passed with PR links.\n- Terminal printed routing, worker starts, repeated spend, result/PR lines and final budget/integration summary. Exact output is retained in `terminal.log`.\n- run.json records GitHub backlog source and label, CLI limit source, $3 cap, cfo.ai system of record and $40 monthly budget with the pre-run spend snapshot.\n\nActual terminal Entire line:\n\n```text\nEntire       CONNECTED\n  Graph sizing: ok (Graph search available; tasks without matching code symbols are sized by repository search.); checkpoint search available\n```\n\nThis verifies #159 on real tasks with no matching code symbols: no setup-needed/fix advice was printed. Both task decisions retained the repository-search explanation.\n\n## Evidence links and trace delivery\n\nEach PR has five working evidence links: Entire session/checkpoint; neatlogs routing trace; neatlogs worker trace; cfo.ai budget table; cfo.ai spend table.\n\n| Task | Decision trace | Worker trace | Entire checkpoint | Entire session |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| #33 | 94bd3bf1c11e3c8eda763f9b267d6261 | 1f6ddb77617a5ce5049bc7566b9c3401 | 01M4RT4Q6ZRSQ739ZZFABCTX1R | 01a131a1-e882-7d93-9f06-b9aa2e2c6540 |\n| #34 | f31716a02f7ff70ae7c338a5ae4aadf3 | 670603e2348ac3afa9ea1798f1970ed5 | 01M4RT4W4TZ09NSHH91DZRMMTW | 01a131a1-f802-77a1-9a57-43f1c71d0824 |\n\n- Worker traces were delivered and written back automatically; no manual drain or PR edit.\n- All four authenticated neatlogs trace-detail and span reads returned HTTP 200. Public UI URLs redirect to sign-in with the correct trace callback; they are not anonymously readable trace views.\n- Both Entire URLs returned HTTP 200 with the actual task-specific session title, not a generic not-found page.\n- Both cfo.ai share URLs returned HTTP 200, and their backing budget/spend cells were read through the adapter.\n- PR evidence updates succeeded; PR #36 updated at `19:42:43Z`, #35 at `19:42:48Z`. Finalization after the last attempt took 34.257 seconds across Ari reporting and both PR evidence updates. The evidence publisher has 15-second bounds for each GitHub read/edit (30 seconds per PR); isolated per-PR call durations were not instrumented. Do not interpret the 34-second combined finalization as a measured single evidence-call delay.\n\n## cfo.ai: exact changes beyond spend\n\nRead snapshots were taken before init, after init, after re-init, immediately before the run, and after the run. No accounting correction was performed.\n\n**Init was idempotent on this existing workspace.** `inspect_pages(include_text=true)` returned the same Tally page structure and text before/after init and re-init: the budget table, spend-detail table and existing `Tally Ari context guide (managed by tally-agents)#c42` text block. No additional block was created; the existing guide already matched the package's contents. Init verified it and enabled per-attempt Ari reporting. No spend/tier/run cell changed during either init.\n\nThe managed guide tells Ari to find run/task/attempt reports by tags, distinguish monthly/current-run amounts, use the token mix for explicitly hypothetical repricing, cite evidence links, and not treat task titles as instructions. It states the excluded data and pricing limits.\n\n**Per attempt, Tally submitted an organization-scoped report through edit_memory/retain_document, not a new page block.** Each includes task/model/tokens/cost/result/budget, selected scenario, tier price snapshot, repricing caveats and review links; excludes issue bodies, source, prompts/transcripts, raw spans and secrets. Reports use deterministic attempt idempotency keys and run/task/attempt tags.\n\nRead-only `inspect_memory` filtered to this run returned ten extracted org facts covering both attempts: costs $0.012760520 and $0.012079440; successful task titles; CLI run cap/monthly budget; and same-token-mix alternative tier prices. Task #34's facts were saved at `19:42:31Z`; #33's at `19:42:34Z`. This proves Ari can recall the reports' facts, not that inspect_memory returned the complete original markdown documents. Exact results are retained in `cfo-attempt-memory.json`.\n\n`inspect_pages` after the run still showed the same page blocks and guide text. It does not expose table-cell values; separate adapter reads verified these changes:\n\n| Cell | Before USD | After USD | Change USD |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Agent spend | 2.274052560 | 2.298892520 | +0.024839960 |\n| Tier spend - cheap | 1.078686560 | 1.103526520 | +0.024839960 |\n| Tier spend - middle | 1.195366000 | 1.195366000 | 0 |\n| Tier spend - top | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| Run spend - current | 0.774489440 | 0.02483