nd - current | 0.774489440 | 0.024839960 | replaced with this run total |\n| Run spend - cumulative | 2.274052560 | 2.298892520 | +0.024839960 |\n\nMonthly budget remained $40. Remaining budget fell by the exact ledger cost to $37.701107480. Prior test excess or historical spend was not corrected.\n\n## Cleanup and scope\n\nScratch AO registration was removed after both workers were confirmed closed (`removedStorageDir: false`), retaining the run/worktrees as evidence. Dashboard stopped after completion. No new workers beyond the two approved tasks, no paid rerun, no PR merges, no code fixes or manual publication, and no default-branch change except the explicitly authorized automatic-linking commit.\n\nDurable run and raw read-back evidence: `final-021-sanity/run-20261012-194035Z/` beside this report.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791834684616,"completed_at_ms":1791834684616}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:51:24.772Z","ordinal":17144,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b7c4c663-1c19-4e0c-b2ac-77fbf9b964e9","process_id":"10513","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,110p' engine/harness.ts"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,110p' engine/harness.ts","name":"harness.ts","path":"engine/harness.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"import type { Tier } from '../schema/types.js';\nimport type { InitCommandRunner } from './init.js';\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\n\nexport type Harness = Tier['harness'];\nexport const AO_HARNESS_PERMISSIONS = { codex: 'auto', 'claude-code': 'default' } as const;\nexport type AoHarnessPermissionModes = Partial<Record<Harness, 'auto' | 'default'>>;\nexport interface HarnessStatus { harness: Harness; installed: boolean; signedIn: boolean; detail: string; fix: string }\n\n/** CLI-owned status only: never inspect credential files or invoke inference. */\nexport async function checkHarness(harness: Harness, command: InitCommandRunner, cwd?: string): Promise<HarnessStatus> {\n  const file = harness === 'claude-code' ? 'claude' : 'codex';\n  const fix = harness === 'claude-code' ? 'claude auth login' : 'codex login';\n  try { await command(file, ['--version'], { cwd }); }\n  catch { return { harness, installed: false, signedIn: false, detail: `${file} is not installed or could not run. Install it before using ${harness} tiers.`, fix: `Install ${harness === 'claude-code' ? 'Claude Code (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/setup)' : 'Codex CLI (https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli/)'} and then run ${fix}.` }; }\n  try {\n    const output = await command(file, harness === 'claude-code' ? ['auth', 'status'] : ['login', 'status'], { cwd });\n    const signedIn = harness === 'claude-code' ? JSON.parse(output.stdout).loggedIn === true\n      : /\\blogged in\\b/i.test(`${output.stdout}\\n${output.stderr}`) && !/\\bnot logged in\\b/i.test(`${output.stdout}\\n${output.stderr}`);\n    return { harness, installed: true, signedIn, detail: signedIn ? `${file} is installed and signed in. Model access was not probed.` : `${file} is signed out or its sign-in status could not be verified.`, fix };\n  } catch { return { harness, installed: true, signedIn: false, detail: `${file} is signed out or its sign-in status could not be verified`, fix }; }\n}\n\nexport function claudeAllowList(test: { command: string; setupCommand?: string }): string[] {\n  const commands = ['git add *', 'git commit *', 'git status', 'git status *', 'git diff', 'git diff *'];\n  return [...new Set(['Edit(./**)', 'Write(./**)', ...commands.map(value => `Bash(${value})`), ...claudeScripts(test).map(script => script.rule)])];\n}\n\nexport function claudeScripts(test: { command: string; setupCommand?: string }): Array<{ name: 'test' | 'setup'; contents: string; rule: string }> {\n  const commands = [test.command, ...(test.setupCommand ? [test.setupCommand] : [])];\n  if (commands.some(value => /[\\r\\n]/.test(value))) throw new Error('Claude allow-list needs single-line test and setup commands');\n  if (commands.some(value => value.includes('\\0'))) throw new Error('Claude script commands cannot contain NUL');\n  return commands.map((command, index) => {\n    const name = index === 0 ? 'test' as const : 'setup' as const;\n    const contents = `#!/bin/sh\\nset -e\\n${command}\\n`;\n    const hash = createHash('sha256').update(contents).digest('hex');\n    return { name, contents, rule: `Bash({{tally.${name}Script:${hash}}})` };\n  });\n}\n\nexport function requireClaudeScriptConsent(allow: string[] | undefined, test: { command: string; setupCommand?: string }): asserts allow is string[] {\n  const expected = claudeAllowList(test);\n  if (!allow?.length || allow.length !== expected.length || expected.some(rule => !allow.includes(rule))) {\n    throw new Error('Claude Code script consent is missing or outdated (old raw-command rules do not authorize scripts); re-run tally init to review and approve the current test/setup script contents.');\n  }\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"import type { Tier } from '../schema/types.js';\nimport type { InitCommandRunner } from './init.js';\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\n\nexport type Harness = Tier['harness'];\nexport const AO_HARNESS_PERMISSIONS = { codex: 'auto', 'claude-code': 'default' } as const;\nexport type AoHarnessPermissionModes = Partial<Record<Harness, 'auto' | 'default'>>;\nexport interface HarnessStatus { harness: Harness; installed: boolean; signedIn: boolean; detail: string; fix: string }\n\n/** CLI-owned status only: never inspect credential files or invoke inference. */\nexport async function checkHarness(harness: Harness, command: InitCommandRunner, cwd?: string): Promise<HarnessStatus> {\n  const file = harness === 'claude-code' ? 'claude' : 'codex';\n  const fix = harness === 'claude-code' ? 'claude auth login' : 'codex login';\n  try { await command(file, ['--version'], { cwd }); }\n  catch { return { harness, installed: false, signedIn: false, detail: `${file} is not installed or could not run. Install it before using ${harness} tiers.`, fix: `Install ${harness === 'claude-code' ? 'Claude Code (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/setup)' : 'Codex CLI (https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli/)'} and then run ${fix}.` }; }\n  try {\n    const output = await command(file, harness === 'claude-code' ? ['auth', 'status'] : ['login', 'status'], { cwd });\n    const signedIn = harness === 'claude-code' ? JSON.parse(output.stdout).loggedIn === true\n      : /\\blogged in\\b/i.test(`${output.stdout}\\n${output.stderr}`) && !/\\bnot logged in\\b/i.test(`${output.stdout}\\n${output.stderr}`);\n    return { harness, installed: true, signedIn, detail: signedIn ? `${file} is installed and signed in. Model access was not probed.` : `${file} is signed out or its sign-in status could not be verified.`, fix };\n  } catch { return { harness, installed: true, signedIn: false, detail: `${file} is signed out or its sign-in status could not be verified`, fix }; }\n}\n\nexport function claudeAllowList(test: { command: string; setupCommand?: string }): string[] {\n  const commands = ['git add *', 'git commit *', 'git status', 'git status *', 'git diff', 'git diff *'];\n  return [...new Set(['Edit(./**)', 'Write(./**)', ...commands.map(value => `Bash(${value})`), ...claudeScripts(test).map(script => script.rule)])];\n}\n\nexport function claudeScripts(test: { command: string; setupCommand?: string }): Array<{ name: 'test' | 'setup'; contents: string; rule: string }> {\n  const commands = [test.command, ...(test.setupCommand ? [test.setupCommand] : [])];\n  if (commands.some(value => /[\\r\\n]/.test(value))) throw new Error('Claude allow-list needs single-line test and setup commands');\n  if (commands.some(value => value.includes('\\0'))) throw new Error('Claude script commands cannot contain NUL');\n  return commands.map((command, index) => {\n    const name = index === 0 ? 'test' as const : 'setup' as const;\n    const contents = `#!/bin/sh\\nset -e\\n${command}\\n`;\n    const hash = createHash('sha256').update(contents).digest('hex');\n    return { name, contents, rule: `Bash({{tally.${name}Script:${hash}}})` };\n  });\n}\n\nexport function requireClaudeScriptConsent(allow: string[] | undefined, test: { command: string; setupCommand?: string }): asserts allow is string[] {\n  const expected = claudeAllowList(test);\n  if (!allow?.length || allow.length !== expected.length || expected.some(rule => !allow.includes(rule))) {\n    throw new Error('Claude Code script consent is missing or outdated (old raw-command rules do not authorize scripts); re-run tally init to review and approve the current test/setup script contents.');\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11875},"formatted_output":"import type { Tier } from '../schema/types.js';\nimport type { InitCommandRunner } from './init.js';\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\n\nexport type Harness = Tier['harness'];\nexport const AO_HARNESS_PERMISSIONS = { codex: 'auto', 'claude-code': 'default' } as const;\nexport type AoHarnessPermissionModes = Partial<Record<Harness, 'auto' | 'default'>>;\nexport interface HarnessStatus { harness: Harness; installed: boolean; signedIn: boolean; detail: string; fix: string }\n\n/** CLI-owned status only: never inspect credential files or invoke inference. */\nexport async function checkHarness(harness: Harness, command: InitCommandRunner, cwd?: string): Promise<HarnessStatus> {\n  const file = harness === 'claude-code' ? 'claude' : 'codex';\n  const fix = harness === 'claude-code' ? 'claude auth login' : 'codex login';\n  try { await command(file, ['--version'], { cwd }); }\n  catch { return { harness, installed: false, signedIn: false, detail: `${file} is not installed or could not run. Install it before using ${harness} tiers.`, fix: `Install ${harness === 'claude-code' ? 'Claude Code (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/setup)' : 'Codex CLI (https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli/)'} and then run ${fix}.` }; }\n  try {\n    const output = await command(file, harness === 'claude-code' ? ['auth', 'status'] : ['login', 'status'], { cwd });\n    const signedIn = harness === 'claude-code' ? JSON.parse(output.stdout).loggedIn === true\n      : /\\blogged in\\b/i.test(`${output.stdout}\\n${output.stderr}`) && !/\\bnot logged in\\b/i.test(`${output.stdout}\\n${output.stderr}`);\n    return { harness, installed: true, signedIn, detail: signedIn ? `${file} is installed and signed in. Model access was not probed.` : `${file} is signed out or its sign-in status could not be verified.`, fix };\n  } catch { return { harness, installed: true, signedIn: false, detail: `${file} is signed out or its sign-in status could not be verified`, fix }; }\n}\n\nexport function claudeAllowList(test: { command: string; setupCommand?: string }): string[] {\n  const commands = ['git add *', 'git commit *', 'git status', 'git status *', 'git diff', 'git diff *'];\n  return [...new Set(['Edit(./**)', 'Write(./**)', ...commands.map(value => `Bash(${value})`), ...claudeScripts(test).map(script => script.rule)])];\n}\n\nexport function claudeScripts(test: { command: string; setupCommand?: string }): Array<{ name: 'test' | 'setup'; contents: string; rule: string }> {\n  const commands = [test.command, ...(test.setupCommand ? [test.setupCommand] : [])];\n  if (commands.some(value => /[\\r\\n]/.test(value))) throw new Error('Claude allow-list needs single-line test and setup commands');\n  if (commands.some(value => value.includes('\\0'))) throw new Error('Claude script commands cannot contain NUL');\n  return commands.map((command, index) => {\n    const name = index === 0 ? 'test' as const : 'setup' as const;\n    const contents = `#!/bin/sh\\nset -e\\n${command}\\n`;\n    const hash = createHash('sha256').update(contents).digest('hex');\n    return { name, contents, rule: `Bash({{tally.${name}Script:${hash}}})` };\n  });\n}\n\nexport function requireClaudeScriptConsent(allow: string[] | undefined, test: { command: string; setupCommand?: string }): asserts allow is string[] {\n  const expected = claudeAllowList(test);\n  if (!allow?.length || allow.length !== expected.length || expected.some(rule => !allow.includes(rule))) {\n    throw new Error('Claude Code script consent is missing or outdated (old raw-command rules do not authorize scripts); re-run tally init to review and approve the current test/setup script contents.');\n  }\n}\n"},"started_at_ms":1791834684772,"completed_at_ms":1791834684772}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:51:24.917Z","ordinal":17145,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-06a9e477-8450-454c-b428-94de63bad2d1","process_id":"29095","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-2/ao-parallel-proof.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-2/ao-parallel-proof.md","name":"ao-parallel-proof.md","path":"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-2/ao-parallel-proof.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# AO Parallel Proof\n\nCompleted one authorized real run: `run-20261011-190131Z`, 3/3 passed, three open PRs, $0.041119320 of a $2 cap. Three AO Codex workers overlapped and cfo.ai reconciles exactly. Caveat: one decision trace is recorded but unavailable from neatlogs; all three worker traces are delivered. No second run was started.\n\n## Release And Setup\n\nFresh install into an empty temporary prefix/cache:\n\n```sh\nnpm install -g --prefix /private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/prefix --cache /private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/cache github:Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack#release\n```\n\nInstalled `release-source.json`: `2015d099888c94ceadb182e1e09251486d0ce645`. All Tally commands used that installed binary, not source checkout. Fresh clone: `/private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/chip-parallel-proof`. Target base: `6da539d6573cc6eb80190cd0e6025b358f85bc6f`, also recorded in run.json. Human checkout untouched.\n\nFiled exactly three new issues: #19 mux exploration guide, #20 memory exploration guide, #21 pipeline exploration guide. Each asks for one distinct new Markdown file and no existing-file edits. All have label `tally` plus dedicated `tally-parallel-proof-20261012`; init uses the latter to prevent selecting any old open task. No prior task was rerun.\n\nReal PTY init: AO, Codex-only luna/terra/sol in tui mode; explicitly opted into parallel workers, count 3. neatlogs and cfo.ai on, Entire off. Existing global hooks reused; optional SDK probe/read-connection/global hook install declined. No global harness settings changed. Init created only this scratch AO project. The sole manual config edit was the approved small base ceiling, 1.5 -> 0.75. `parallelWorkers: 3` is the explicit opt-in; legacy concurrency is not relied on. Doctor connected AO daemon, worker auto mode, Codex, gh, neatlogs key and cfo.ai.\n\nPlan listed only #21, #20, #19, each small/confidence 0.80, cheap `codex/gpt-5.6-luna`, ceiling $0.15. Related source sections were context, not edit targets. List prices came from installed init's pricing module and their source notes remain on the ledger. These costs are configured list-price accounting, not invoices.\n\nReservation arithmetic: each task reserves cheap $0.15 + potential middle $0.375 = $0.525; 3 x $0.525 = $1.575, leaving $0.425 under the $2 cap. Monthly remaining before run was $40 - $0.958404600 = $39.041595400. No ceiling, escalation or aggregate budget stop fired.\n\n## Command And Live Observation\n\n```sh\n/private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/prefix/bin/tally run --budget 2 --parallel 3 --dashboard --port 5203\n```\n\nRun output: `/private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/chip-parallel-proof/.tally/runs/run-20261011-190131Z`.\n\nDashboard address printed immediately: `http://127.0.0.1:5203/?data=%2Fruns%2Flatest%2F`; HTTP 200 before first spawn. latest held this run while tasks were still pending. Read-only dashboard JSON observations show all three tasks running at 19:04:01.705Z. Combined live spend increased through $0.003044440, $0.005410400, $0.006890880, $0.020295120 and $0.041119320. Each ledger row appeared as its attempt finished, before the other tasks were done; every observed JSON response parsed successfully.\n\nRun timestamps: 2026-10-11T19:01:31.886Z -> 19:06:27.554Z (12 Oct 00:31:31.886 -> 00:36:27.554 IST). Real routing-history reads delayed first spawn by about 139 seconds. No worker was consuming tokens during that wait; terminal printed the dashboard and budget first, then routing lines. Plan also took several minutes on history reads. This latency is a finding, not hidden as instant startup.\n\n## AO Overlap\n\nThese are actual AO daemon `createdAt` and terminated-session `updatedAt` (not identical engine attempt-start timestamps):\n\n| Task | AO session | Created (UTC) | Closed (UTC) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| #20 | chip-parallel-proof-1 | 19:03:51.112220 | 19:05:27.388608 |\n| #19 | chip-parallel-proof-2 | 19:03:53.840543 | 19:06:05.657242 |\n| #21 | chip-parallel-proof-3 | 19:03:56.759365 | 19:05:07.045772 |\n\nAll three session lifetimes overlapped from 19:03:56.759365 to 19:05:07.045772: 70.286407 seconds. This measures coexistence, not continuous simultaneous token generation. Independent task spends increased during that interval. Each session had mode tui, harness codex, model gpt-5.6-luna; each final daemon record had `isTerminated: true` and activity exited. Memory's transient needs_input cleared without intervention and produced a commit; Tally did not kill it prematurely.\n\n## Tasks And Publishing\n\n| Task | Tokens (uncached/cached/output/total) | Cost USD | PR | Commit |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| #21 | 25782 / 207360 / 2706 / 235848 | 0.012550800 | [#22](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/22) | 68bfc6980c6531888fe3477b1d84ee62dc9129c1 |\n| #20 | 31127 / 211200 / 2584 / 244911 | 0.013550200 | [#23](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/23) | 7a5dedc397fabca0e29a9dfdc2c6074cb298c9a2 |\n| #19 | 28220 / 240896 / 3797 / 272913 | 0.015018320 | [#24](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/24) | fec57fe50fdf2589357afa1ca4162dddf8fc0cac |\n\n753672 aggregate tokens. Each task stayed cheap, one attempt, passed Tally's independent configured JavaScript syntax command, resultReason null. Each PR has one commit and one new file only: docs/pipeline-exploration.md, docs/memory-exploration.md, docs/mux-exploration.md respectively. Branches are `ao/chip-parallel-proof-3/root`, `ao/chip-parallel-proof-1/root`, `ao/chip-parallel-proof-2/root`. Tally pushed and created all PRs; no manual verification/push/PR fallback. All PRs remain open, none merged; closingIssuesReferences verifies #22 closes #21, #23 closes #20, #24 closes #19. Nothing pushed to main. Syntax checks do not prove Markdown factual correctness; no stronger test coverage is claimed. Entire was intentionally off, so ledger checkpoint ids are null.\n\n## Accounting Read-Back\n\n| Cell | Before USD | After USD | Delta USD |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Agent spend | 0.958404600 | 0.999523920 | 0.041119320 |\n| Tier spend - cheap | 0.680313000 | 0.721432320 | 0.041119320 |\n| Tier spend - middle | 0.278091600 | 0.278091600 | 0 |\n| Tier spend - top | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n\nBefore read: 19:59:17 is NOT the timestamp; the actual saved snapshot is **2026-10-11T18:59:17.589Z**. After read: **2026-10-11T19:06:55.926Z**. Ledger sum 41119320 nanos = Agent spend delta = cheap delta, exact. Tier rows sum to Agent spend both before and after. Remaining run cap $1.958880680. cfo.ai write-back status ok. run.json: limitSource cli, systemOfRecord cfoai, monthly source cfoai/$40, cap $2, github-issues backlog with dedicated label, dryRun false. Accounting writes were handled by Tally, not these read-only observers.\n\n## Trace Read-Back\n\n| Task | Decision trace ID | Worker trace ID | Read-back |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| #21 | f2a8b6eb07efc12112bcce054c05e582 | 759a437ac0d326bba367b8275d5b742f | Both detail and spans 200; worker 23 spans |\n| #20 | 2165fb70bc65c97ec68dad595623e077 | f7b0ab5ee687be8444ad853a39529dff | Decision detail/spans 404; worker both 200, 24 spans |\n| #19 | 0a2551da02bbab47b42a047818274b0c | f5967797d277ad6441db62d9ede326a5 | Both detail and spans 200; worker 25 spans |\n\nEvery worker workflow starts `Tally run-20261011-190131Z #<issue> a1`, matching the correct task and attempt; native worker sessions differ from the run id. Delivered decision traces name the corresponding run/task/attempt. All three history outcome traces also delivered. #20 decision remained 404 before and after normal SDK shutdown; six recent trace pages contained the other two route traces but no #20 route trace. Delivery is therefore NOT established for that row, despite nonnull ledger ID and run neatlogs status ok. The cause is not established; this is not claimed to be fixed or merely eventual consistency. No ledger was hand-rewritten. This trace-delivery gap needs follow-up, not another paid run.\n\n## Terminal And Evidence\n\nVerbatim run terminal transcript: [ao-parallel-proof-terminal.log](ao-parallel-proof-terminal.log). Includes every routing, start, periodic spend, result and summary line, with original terminal carriage returns. Init, plan and doctor transcripts, JSON observations, original/post-shutdown trace reads, raw AO session/usage and PR evidence, before/after accounting snapshots are retained in the scratch root `/private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0`. Consolidated read-back JSON is attached beside this report as `ao-parallel-proof-evidence.json`.\n\nExact selected terminal lines (values not substituted with more precise ledger figures):\n\n```text\ndashboard http://127.0.0.1:5203/?data=%2Fruns%2Flatest%2F\ndata /runs/latest/\nmonthly budget: $40.00 from cfo.ai; run cap: $2.00 (CLI --budget)\n#20 attempt 1: worker chip-parallel-proof-1 started on cheap\n#19 attempt 1: worker chip-parallel-proof-2 started on cheap\n#21 attempt 1: worker chip-parallel-proof-3 started on cheap\n#20 attempt 1: spend $0.0030\n#19 attempt 1: spend $0.0024\n#21 attempt 1: spend $0.0026\n#21 attempt 1: passed $0.0126 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/22\n#20 attempt 1: passed $0.0136 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/23\n#19 attempt 1: passed $0.0150 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/24\nfinished run-20261011-190131Z: 3 tasks, 3 attempts\nsummary: 3 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; total $0.0411 against run cap $2.00\nmonthly budget: $40.00 from cfo.ai; run cap: $2.00 (CLI --budget)\nPR https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/22\nPR https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/23\nPR https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/24\n```\n\nDashboard kept serving through evidence collection, then normal Ctrl+C shutdown flushed the SDK. A saved-run viewing command is:\n\n```sh\ncd /private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/chip-parallel-proof\n/private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/prefix/bin/tally dashboard --port 5203\n# Open http://127.0.0.1:5203/?data=%2Fruns%2Frun-20261011-190131Z%2F\n```\n\nCleanup finding: installed `tally uninstall --yes` refused the intentionally changed ceiling config and printed a raw Node stack (`tally.yaml changed after init; preserve or remove it manually before uninstalling.`), exit 1. It made no removals. I then removed only the owned scratch AO project with `ao project rm chip-parallel-proof -y`, after all workers closed and evidence was saved. Run folder and proof config retained; issues/PRs left open. No target code/config was hand-edited except the explicitly approved local Tally ceiling. No further real run is needed to demonstrate overlap/accounting/publishing, and none was started.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# AO Parallel Proof\n\nCompleted one authorized real run: `run-20261011-190131Z`, 3/3 passed, three open PRs, $0.041119320 of a $2 cap. Three AO Codex workers overlapped and cfo.ai reconciles exactly. Caveat: one decision trace is recorded but unavailable from neatlogs; all three worker traces are delivered. N