d $0.0150 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/24\nfinished run-20261011-190131Z: 3 tasks, 3 attempts\nsummary: 3 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; total $0.0411 against run cap $2.00\nmonthly budget: $40.00 from cfo.ai; run cap: $2.00 (CLI --budget)\nPR https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/22\nPR https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/23\nPR https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/24\n```\n\nDashboard kept serving through evidence collection, then normal Ctrl+C shutdown flushed the SDK. A saved-run viewing command is:\n\n```sh\ncd /private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/chip-parallel-proof\n/private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/prefix/bin/tally dashboard --port 5203\n# Open http://127.0.0.1:5203/?data=%2Fruns%2Frun-20261011-190131Z%2F\n```\n\nCleanup finding: installed `tally uninstall --yes` refused the intentionally changed ceiling config and printed a raw Node stack (`tally.yaml changed after init; preserve or remove it manually before uninstalling.`), exit 1. It made no removals. I then removed only the owned scratch AO project with `ao project rm chip-parallel-proof -y`, after all workers closed and evidence was saved. Run folder and proof config retained; issues/PRs left open. No target code/config was hand-edited except the explicitly approved local Tally ceiling. No further real run is needed to demonstrate overlap/accounting/publishing, and none was started.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791834684917,"completed_at_ms":1791834684917}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:51:25.206Z","ordinal":17146,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9025feb5-5d7b-46c3-ba86-5dc133080a14","process_id":"10142","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","node bin/tally.js init --help"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"node bin/tally.js init --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"tally: a CFO for a fleet of coding agents\n\nUsage: tally <command> [options]\n\nCommands:\n  experiment Run baseline and Tally repeats with a shared safety budget\n  run      Run the backlog against the budget in tally.yaml\n  demo     Run the full loop with simulated workers on a sample backlog\n  dashboard Start the local dashboard server\n  init     Set up tally.yaml for the current repository\n  uninstall List and remove the recorded Tally installation\n  doctor   Check that each integration is connected\n  login    Connect an integration, e.g. tally login cfoai\n  market   Find and qualify likely pilot companies with CrustData\n  publish  Write a static dashboard bundle (does not deploy)\n  traces drain --run <id> Drain and read-back verify a finished run's worker traces\n  logo     Replay the Tally logo animation\n\nOptions:\n  --repeats <N>     Repeats per experiment mode (default: 2)\n  --config <path>   Path to tally.yaml (default: tally.yaml)\n  --dry-run         Simulate workers; spends nothing\n  --budget <usd>    Override the budget for this run\n  --only <task>     Run a single task\n  --parallel <N>    Opt into up to N AO workers (default: 1; direct is sequential)\n  --baseline        Send every task to the strongest tier\n  --dashboard       Serve the dashboard before run/demo; keep serving until Ctrl+C\n  --open            Also open the dashboard in the browser\n  --port <number>   Dashboard port (default: 5177; use 0 for any free port)\n  --plan            Size and route tasks, but do not spawn workers\n  --live            For demo: use live read-only integrations with fake workers\n  --yes             Approve init changes or explicitly budgeted paid experiments\n  --test-command <cmd> For init: verification shell command\n  --setup-command <cmd> For init: setup shell command (empty means none)\n  --issue-label <label> For init: GitHub issue label (default: tally)\n  --neatlogs <yes|no> --entire <yes|no> --cfoai <yes|no> Init product opt-ins\n  --verbose         For init: include the full proposed YAML\n  --runner <ao|direct> For init: AO workers or sequential direct workers\n  --harness <claude-code|codex|mixed> For init: coding agent choice (Codex is default)\n  --model-access-fallback-tier <name> For init: override the default cheap-tier fallback\n  --allow-claude     For init: explicitly consent to the printed repository allow-list\n  --output <dir>    Output directory for tally market (default: .tally/market/latest)\n  --limit <number>  Result limit for tally market (default: 10)\n  --keyword <text>  Optional exact description phrase for tally market\n  --max-credits <N> Market estimated credit cap (default: 10); refuses above cap\n  --replay <query.json> Replay cached market snapshot; no API calls\n  --review <json>   Apply human review labels to a cached market snapshot\n  --jobs            Search engineering job posts for explicit coding-tool evidence\n  --secondary <query.json> Include a cached firmographic table in the job report\n                    market --plan checks free account pricing, without a search\n  --out <dir>       New directory for tally publish (required)\n  --runs <ids>      Comma-separated run folder ids (default: all real runs)\n  --run <id>        Run id for traces drain; --output overrides its run directory\n  -h, --help        Show this help\n  -v, --version     Show the version\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"tally: a CFO for a fleet of coding agents\n\nUsage: tally <command> [options]\n\nCommands:\n  experiment Run baseline and Tally repeats with a shared safety budget\n  run      Run the backlog against the budget in tally.yaml\n  demo     Run the full loop with simulated workers on a sample backlog\n  dashboard Start the local dashboard server\n  init     Set up tally.yaml for the current repository\n  uninstall List and remove the recorded Tally installation\n  doctor   Check that each integration is connected\n  login    Connect an integration, e.g. tally login cfoai\n  market   Find and qualify likely pilot companies with CrustData\n  publish  Write a static dashboard bundle (does not deploy)\n  traces drain --run <id> Drain and read-back verify a finished run's worker traces\n  logo     Replay the Tally logo animation\n\nOptions:\n  --repeats <N>     Repeats per experiment mode (default: 2)\n  --config <path>   Path to tally.yaml (default: tally.yaml)\n  --dry-run         Simulate workers; spends nothing\n  --budget <usd>    Override the budget for this run\n  --only <task>     Run a single task\n  --parallel <N>    Opt into up to N AO workers (default: 1; direct is sequential)\n  --baseline        Send every task to the strongest tier\n  --dashboard       Serve the dashboard before run/demo; keep serving until Ctrl+C\n  --open            Also open the dashboard in the browser\n  --port <number>   Dashboard port (default: 5177; use 0 for any free port)\n  --plan            Size and route tasks, but do not spawn workers\n  --live            For demo: use live read-only integrations with fake workers\n  --yes             Approve init changes or explicitly budgeted paid experiments\n  --test-command <cmd> For init: verification shell command\n  --setup-command <cmd> For init: setup shell command (empty means none)\n  --issue-label <label> For init: GitHub issue label (default: tally)\n  --neatlogs <yes|no> --entire <yes|no> --cfoai <yes|no> Init product opt-ins\n  --verbose         For init: include the full proposed YAML\n  --runner <ao|direct> For init: AO workers or sequential direct workers\n  --harness <claude-code|codex|mixed> For init: coding agent choice (Codex is default)\n  --model-access-fallback-tier <name> For init: override the default cheap-tier fallback\n  --allow-claude     For init: explicitly consent to the printed repository allow-list\n  --output <dir>    Output directory for tally market (default: .tally/market/latest)\n  --limit <number>  Result limit for tally market (default: 10)\n  --keyword <text>  Optional exact description phrase for tally market\n  --max-credits <N> Market estimated credit cap (default: 10); refuses above cap\n  --replay <query.json> Replay cached market snapshot; no API calls\n  --review <json>   Apply human review labels to a cached market snapshot\n  --jobs            Search engineering job posts for explicit coding-tool evidence\n  --secondary <query.json> Include a cached firmographic table in the job report\n                    market --plan checks free account pricing, without a search\n  --out <dir>       New directory for tally publish (required)\n  --runs <ids>      Comma-separated run folder ids (default: all real runs)\n  --run <id>        Run id for traces drain; --output overrides its run directory\n  -h, --help        Show this help\n  -v, --version     Show the version\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":44246667},"formatted_output":"tally: a CFO for a fleet of coding agents\n\nUsage: tally <command> [options]\n\nCommands:\n  experiment Run baseline and Tally repeats with a shared safety budget\n  run      Run the backlog against the budget in tally.yaml\n  demo     Run the full loop with simulated workers on a sample backlog\n  dashboard Start the local dashboard server\n  init     Set up tally.yaml for the current repository\n  uninstall List and remove the recorded Tally installation\n  doctor   Check that each integration is connected\n  login    Connect an integration, e.g. tally login cfoai\n  market   Find and qualify likely pilot companies with CrustData\n  publish  Write a static dashboard bundle (does not deploy)\n  traces drain --run <id> Drain and read-back verify a finished run's worker traces\n  logo     Replay the Tally logo animation\n\nOptions:\n  --repeats <N>     Repeats per experiment mode (default: 2)\n  --config <path>   Path to tally.yaml (default: tally.yaml)\n  --dry-run         Simulate workers; spends nothing\n  --budget <usd>    Override the budget for this run\n  --only <task>     Run a single task\n  --parallel <N>    Opt into up to N AO workers (default: 1; direct is sequential)\n  --baseline        Send every task to the strongest tier\n  --dashboard       Serve the dashboard before run/demo; keep serving until Ctrl+C\n  --open            Also open the dashboard in the browser\n  --port <number>   Dashboard port (default: 5177; use 0 for any free port)\n  --plan            Size and route tasks, but do not spawn workers\n  --live            For demo: use live read-only integrations with fake workers\n  --yes             Approve init changes or explicitly budgeted paid experiments\n  --test-command <cmd> For init: verification shell command\n  --setup-command <cmd> For init: setup shell command (empty means none)\n  --issue-label <label> For init: GitHub issue label (default: tally)\n  --neatlogs <yes|no> --entire <yes|no> --cfoai <yes|no> Init product opt-ins\n  --verbose         For init: include the full proposed YAML\n  --runner <ao|direct> For init: AO workers or sequential direct workers\n  --harness <claude-code|codex|mixed> For init: coding agent choice (Codex is default)\n  --model-access-fallback-tier <name> For init: override the default cheap-tier fallback\n  --allow-claude     For init: explicitly consent to the printed repository allow-list\n  --output <dir>    Output directory for tally market (default: .tally/market/latest)\n  --limit <number>  Result limit for tally market (default: 10)\n  --keyword <text>  Optional exact description phrase for tally market\n  --max-credits <N> Market estimated credit cap (default: 10); refuses above cap\n  --replay <query.json> Replay cached market snapshot; no API calls\n  --review <json>   Apply human review labels to a cached market snapshot\n  --jobs            Search engineering job posts for explicit coding-tool evidence\n  --secondary <query.json> Include a cached firmographic table in the job report\n                    market --plan checks free account pricing, without a search\n  --out <dir>       New directory for tally publish (required)\n  --runs <ids>      Comma-separated run folder ids (default: all real runs)\n  --run <id>        Run id for traces drain; --output overrides its run directory\n  -h, --help        Show this help\n  -v, --version     Show the version\n"},"started_at_ms":1791834685162,"completed_at_ms":1791834685206}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:51:25.256Z","ordinal":17147,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a131ab-7f48-7e93-9779-97cfc6d22c9a","call_id":"call_d97b60113ef54ea9b13452abea62134a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"072886\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000006458,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2461,\"output\":\"# Tally 0.2.1 release sanity: passed\\n\\n## Candidate and isolation\\n\\n- Installed with `npm install -g --prefix /private/tmp/tally-021-sanity.l0XjHO/prefix --cache /private/tmp/tally-021-sanity.l0XjHO/npm-cache github:Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack#release` (fresh prefix and cache).\\n- Installed `tally --version`: `0.2.1`. Installed `release-source.json`: `ceddd6a23e7d57dd69f5ba240aa34218647a47c2`. Main was checked again immediately before starting and matched.\\n- Fresh clone: `/private/tmp/tally-021-sanity.l0XjHO/tally-021-sanity-chip`. Human checkout was not touched. Scratch AO project: `tally-021-sanity-chip`.\\n- Fresh issues: [#33](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/issues/33), [#34](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/issues/34), label `tally-sanity-021`. No old tasks were selected.\\n- Used the installed CLI for init, doctor, plan and run. No hand-edited tally.yaml, ceilings, tiers, worker output or PR body.\\n\\n## Init and the explicitly authorized settings commit\\n\\nPTY init used AO, Codex only, two parallel workers, verification `find js -name '*.js' -print0 | xargs -0 -n1 node --check`, no setup, and all three integrations requested. Default model prices and ceilings were retained. Monthly/fallback budget: $40, read from cfo.ai.\\n\\nThe first init asked to publish automatic Entire linking to the target default branch. I declined, reported the blocker, and started no worker. The human then authorized exactly that settings change. Before consenting I compared the existing settings with the installed init transformation; the sole proposed change was `commit_linking: always`. Re-init published the same exact change:\\n\\nCommit: `d5d93ba9cb23466585f9416cabf3bc98690da43c` (`chore: enable Entire capture for Tally workers`). Only `.entire/settings.json` changed. It is the only default-branch push in this proof, separately authorized by the human.\\n\\n```diff\\n@@ -4,5 +4,6 @@\\n     \\\"primary\\\": {\\n       \\\"type\\\": \\\"git-refs\\\"\\n     }\\n-  }\\n+  },\\n+  \\\"commit_linking\\\": \\\"always\\\"\\n }\\n```\\n\\nRe-init's config diff only changed Entire from false to true. It preserved the rest of the settings and install record. Doctor then reported AO ready, worker auto mode, signed-in Codex, GitHub, Entire CLI/graph/checkpoint recall/repository/mirror, neatlogs and cfo.ai connected. No mirror was created; existing mirrors were ready. Generated summaries remained off.\\n\\n## Run and results\\n\\nCommand: `tally run --budget 3 --parallel 2 --dashboard --port 0`.\\n\\n- Run: `run-20261012-194035Z`, from `2026-10-12T19:40:35.715Z` to `19:42:49.622Z` (13 October 01:10:35 to 01:12:49 IST).\\n- Repo base: `d5d93ba9cb23466585f9416cabf3bc98690da43c`, after the authorized settings commit.\\n- Dashboard: `http://127.0.0.1:61613/?data=%2Fruns%2Flatest%2F`; stopped after the final summary, not while workers were active.\\n- 2/2 tasks passed; two attempts total; no ceiling stop or escalation, as expected for this sanity run.\\n- Both tasks used `codex/gpt-5.6-luna`, AO tui, cheap tier, $0.30 attempt ceilings. Parallel reservations: 2 x ($0.30 + $0.75) = $2.10, within the $3 run cap and monthly remaining budget.\\n\\n| Issue | Tokens (uncached / cached / output / total) | Cost USD | PR | Commit |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| #33 | 39762 / 87552 / 1980 / 129294 | 0.012079440 | [#35](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/35) | 8d7c3b42ea35012c33432bf9f0e197153ce2463b |\\n| #34 | 29017 / 212736 / 2252 / 244005 | 0.012760520 | [#36](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/36) | e5ea198b2361f8c128afa8125350ebc757997fc3 |\\n\\nTotal: **$0.024839960 of $3.00**. Tally verified and published both PRs. GitHub `closingIssuesReferences` reports #33 and #34 respectively. Each PR adds exactly its requested docs file, no other changes. Both PRs remain open; neither was merged.\\n\\n## Parallelism and live UI\\n\\n- #33 AO session `tally-021-sanity-chip-1`: created `19:40:51.931043Z`, terminated/updated `19:41:51.306589Z`.\\n- #34 AO session `tally-021-sanity-chip-2`: created `19:40:56.271395Z`, terminated/updated `19:41:56.387101Z`.\\n- Both are `isTerminated: true`, activity `exited`. Their lifetimes overlapped for about 55 seconds.\\n- Dashboard run.json HTTP 200 at `19:40:40.776Z`, before either session existed. Latest pointed at this run from its initial record.\\n- 130 recorded live observations: pending/zero at `19:40:40.420Z`, both running with $0.003165120 live spend at `19:41:06.451Z`, then climbing to $0.024839960, then both passed with PR links.\\n- Terminal printed routing, worker starts, repeated spend, result/PR lines and final budget/integration summary. Exact output is retained in `terminal.log`.\\n- run.json records GitHub backlog source and label, CLI limit source, $3 cap, cfo.ai system of record and $40 monthly budget with the pre-run spend snapshot.\\n\\nActual terminal Entire line:\\n\\n```text\\nEntire       CONNECTED\\n  Graph sizing: ok (Graph search available; tasks without matching code symbols are sized by repository search.); checkpoint search available\\n```\\n\\nThis verifies #159 on real tasks with no matching code symbols: no setup-needed/fix advice was printed. Both task decisions retained the repository-search explanation.\\n\\n## Evidence links and trace delivery\\n\\nEach PR has five working evidence links: Entire session/checkpoint; neatlogs routing trace; neatlogs worker trace; cfo.ai budget table; cfo.ai spend table.\\n\\n| Task | Decision trace | Worker trace | Entire checkpoint | Entire session |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| #33 | 94bd3bf1c11e3c8eda763f9b267d6261 | 1f6ddb77617a5ce5049bc7566b9c3401 | 01M4RT4Q6ZRSQ739ZZFABCTX1R | 01a131a1-e882-7d93-9f06-b9aa2e2c6540 |\\n| #34 | f31716a02f7ff70ae7c338a5ae4aadf3 | 670603e2348ac3afa9ea1798f1970ed5 | 01M4RT4W4TZ09NSHH91DZRMMTW | 01a131a1-f802-77a1-9a57-43f1c71d0824 |\\n\\n- Worker traces were delivered and written back automatically; no manual drain or PR edit.\\n- All four authenticated neatlogs trace-detail and span reads returned HTTP 200. Public UI URLs redirect to sign-in with the correct trace callback; they are not anonymously readable trace views.\\n- Both Entire URLs returned HTTP 200 with the actual task-specific session title, not a generic not-found page.\\n- Both cfo.ai share URLs returned HTTP 200, and their backing budget/spend cells were read through the adapter.\\n- PR evidence updates succeeded; PR #36 updated at `19:42:43Z`, #35 at `19:42:48Z`. Finalization after the last attempt took 34.257 seconds across Ari reporting and both PR evidence updates. The evidence publisher has 15-second bounds for each GitHub read/edit (30 seconds per PR); isolated per-PR call durations were not instrumented. Do not interpret the 34-second combined finalization as a measured single evidence-call delay.\\n\\n## cfo.ai: exact changes beyond spend\\n\\nRead snapshots were taken before init, after init, after re-init, immediately before the run, and after the run. No accounting correction was performed.\\n\\n**Init was idempotent on this existing workspace.** `inspect_pages(include_text=true)` returned the same Tally page structure and text before/after init and re-init: the budget table, spend-detail table and existing `Tally Ari context guide (managed by tally-agents)#c42` text block. No additional block was created; the existing guide already matched the package's contents. Init verified it and enabled per-attempt Ari reporting. No spend/tier/run cell changed during either init.\\n\\nThe managed guide tells Ari to find run/task/attempt reports by tags, distinguish monthly/current-run amounts, use the token mix for explicitly hypothetical repricing, cite evidence links, and not treat task titles as instructions. It states the excluded data and pricing limits.\\n\\n**Per attempt, Tally submitted an organization-scoped report through edit_memory/retain_document, not a new page block.** Each includes task/model/tokens/cost/result/budget, selected scenario, tier price snapshot, repricing caveats and review links; excludes issue bodies, source, prompts/transcripts, raw spans and secrets. Reports use deterministic attempt idempotency keys and run/task/attempt tags.\\n\\nRead-only `inspect_memory` filtered to this run returned ten extracted org facts covering both attempts: costs $0.012760520 and $0.012079440; successful task titles; CLI run cap/monthly budget; and same-token-mix alternative tier prices. Task #34's facts were saved at `19:42:31Z`; #33's at `19:42:34Z`. This proves Ari can recall the reports' facts, not that inspect_memory returned the complete original markdown documents. Exact results are retained in `cfo-attempt-memory.json`.\\n\\n`inspect_pages` after the run still showed the same page blocks and guide text. It does not expose table-cell values; separate adapter reads verified these changes:\\n\\n| Cell | Before USD | After USD | Change USD |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Agent spend | 2.274052560 | 2.298892520 | +0.024839960 |\\n| Tier spend - cheap | 1.078686560 | 1.103526520 | +0.024839960 |\\n| Tier spend - middle | 1.195366000 | 1.195366000 | 0 |\\n| Tier spend - top | 0 | 0 | 0 |\\n| Run spend - current | 0.774489440 | 0.024839960 | replaced with this run total |\\n| Run spend - cumulative | 2.274052560 | 2.298892520 | +0.024839960 |\\n\\nMonthly budget remained $40. Remaining budget fell by the exact ledger cost to $37.701107480. Prior test excess or historical spend was not corrected.\\n\\n## Cleanup and scope\\n\\nScratch AO registration was removed after both workers were confirmed closed (`removedStorageDir: false`), retaining the run/worktrees as evidence. Dashboard stopped after completion. No new workers beyond the two approved tasks, no paid rerun, no PR merges, no code fixes or manual publication, and no default-branch change except the explicitly authorized automatic-linking commit.\\n\\nDurable run and raw read-back evidence: `final-021-sanity/run-20261012-194035Z/` beside this report.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"ac9b02\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000011875,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":904,\"output\":\"import type { Tier } from '../schema/types.js';\\nimport type { InitCommandRunner } from './init.js';\\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\\n\\nexport type Harness = Tier['harness'];\\nexport const AO_HARNESS_PERMISSIONS = { codex: 'auto', 'claude-code': 'default' } as const;\\nexport type AoHarnessPermissionModes = Partial<Record<Harness, 'auto' | 'default'>>;\\nexport interface HarnessStatus { harness: Harness; installed: boolean; signedIn: boolean; detail: string; fix: string }\\n\\n/** CLI-owned status only: never inspect credential files or invoke inference. */\\nexport async function checkHarness(harness: Harness, command: InitCommandRunner, cwd?: string): Promise<HarnessStatus> {\\n  const file = harness === 'claude-code' ? 'claude' : 'codex';\\n  const fix = harness === 'claude-code' ? 'claude auth login' : 'codex login';\\n  try { await command(file, ['--version'], { cwd }); }\\n  catch { return { harness, installed: false, signedIn: false, detail: `${file} is not installed or could not run. Install it before using ${harness} tiers.`, fix: `Install ${harness === 'claude-code' ? 'Claude Code (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/setup)' : 'Codex CLI (https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli/)'} and then run ${fix}.` }; }\\n  try {\\n    const output = await command(file, harness === 'claude-code' ? ['auth', 'status'] : ['login', 'status'], { cwd });\\n    const signedIn = harness === 'claude-code' ? JSON.parse(output.stdout).loggedIn === true\\n      : /\\\\blogged in\\\\b/i.test(`${output.stdout}\\\\n${output.stderr}`) && !/\\\\bnot logged in\\\\b/i.test(`${output.stdout}\\\\n${output.stderr}`);\\n    return { harness, installed: true, signedIn, detail: signedIn ? `${file} is installed and signed in. Model access was not probed.` : `${file} is signed out or its sign-in status could not be verified.`, fix };\\n  } catch { return { harness, installed: true, signedIn: false, detail: `${file} is signed out or its sign-in status could not be verified`, fix }; }\\n}\\n\\nexport function claudeAllowList(test: { command: string; setupCommand?: string }): string[] {\\n  const commands = ['git add *', 'git commit *', 'git status', 'git status *', 'git diff', 'git diff *'];\\n  return [...new Set(['Edit(./**)', 'Write(./**)', ...commands.map(value => `Bash(${value})`), ...claudeScripts(test).map(script => script.rule)])];\\n}\\n\\nexport function claudeScripts(test: { command: string; setupCommand?: string }): Array<{ name: 'test' | 'setup'; contents: string; rule: string }> {\\n  const commands = [test.command, ...(test.setupCommand ? [test.setupCommand] : [])];\\n  if (commands.some(value => /[\\\\r\\\\n]/.test(value))) throw new Error('Claude allow-list needs single-line test and setup commands');\\n  if (commands.some(value => value.includes('\\\\0'))) throw new Error('Claude script commands cannot contain NUL');\\n  return commands.map((command, index) => {\\n    const name = index === 0 ? 'test' as const : 'setup' as const;\\n    const contents = `#!/bin/sh\\\\nset -e\\\\n${command}\\\\n`;\\n    const hash = createHash('sha256').update(contents).digest('hex');\\n    return { name, contents, rule: `Bash({{tally.${name}Script:${hash}}})` };\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nexport function requireClaudeScriptConsent(allow: string[] | undefined, test: { command: string; setupCommand?: string }): asserts allow is string[] {\\n  const expected = claudeAllowList(test);\\n  if (!allow?.length || allow.length !== expected.length || expected.some(rule => !allow.includes(rule))) {\\n    throw new Error('Claude Code script consent is missing or outdated (old raw-command rules do not authorize scripts); re-run tally init to review and approve the current test/setup script contents.');\\n  }\\n}\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"b0328b\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000004875,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2688,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2688)\\nTotal output lines: 113\\n\\n# AO Parallel Proof\\n\\nCompleted one authorized real run: `run-20261011-190131Z`, 3/3 passed, three open PRs, $0.041119320 of a $2 cap. Three AO Codex workers overlapped and cfo.ai reconciles exactly. Caveat: one decision trace is recorded but unavailable from neatlogs; all three worker traces are delivered. No second run was started.\\n\\n## Release And Setup\\n\\nFresh install into an empty temporary prefix/cache:\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm install -g --prefix /private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/prefix --cache /private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/cache github:Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack#release\\n```\\n\\nInstalled `release-source.json`: `2015d099888c94ceadb182e1e09251486d0ce645`. All Tally commands used that installed binary, not source checkout. Fresh clone: `/private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/chip-parallel-proof`. Target base: `6da539d6573cc6eb80190cd0e6025b358f85bc6f`, also recorded in run.json. Human checkout untouched.\\n\\nFiled exactly three new issues: #19 mux exploration guide, #20 memory exploration guide, #21 pipeline exploration guide. Each asks for one distinct new Markdown file and no existing-file edits. All have label `tally` plus dedicated `tally-parallel-proof-20261012`; init uses the latter to prevent selecting any old open task. No prior task was rerun.\\n\\nReal PTY init: AO, Codex-only luna/terra/sol in tui mode; explicitly opted into parallel workers, count 3. neatlogs and cfo.ai on, Entire off. Existing global hooks reused; optional SDK probe/read-connection/global hook install declined. No global harness settings changed. Init created only this scratch AO project. The sole manual config edit was the approved small base ceiling, 1.5 -> 0.75. `parallelWorkers: 3` is the explicit opt-in; legacy concurrency is not relied on. Doctor connected AO daemon, worker auto mode, Codex, gh, neatlogs key and cfo.ai.\\n\\nPlan listed only #21, #20, #19, each small/confidence 0.80, cheap `codex/gpt-5.6-luna`, ceiling $0.15. Related source sections were context, not edit targets. List prices came from installed init's pricing module and their source notes remain on the ledger. These costs are configured list-price accounting, not invoices.\\n\\nReservation arithmetic: each task reserves cheap $0.15 + potential middle $0.375 = $0.525; 3 x $0.525 = $1.575, leaving $0.425 under the $2 cap. Monthly remaining before run was $40 - $0.958404600 = $39.041595400. No ceiling, escalation or aggregate budget stop fired.\\n\\n## Command And Live Observation\\n\\n```sh\\n/private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/prefix/bin/tally run --budget 2 --parallel 3 --dashboard --port 5203\\n```\\n\\nRun output: `/private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/chip-parallel-proof/.tally/runs/run-20261011-190131Z`.\\n\\nDashboard address printed immediately: `http://127.0.0.1:5203/?data=%2Fruns%2Flatest%2F`; HTTP 200 before first spawn. latest held this run while tasks were still pending. Read-only dashboard JSON observations show all three tasks running at 19:04:01.705Z. Combined live spend increased through $0.003044440, $0.005410400, $0.006890880, $0.020295120 and $0.041119320. Each ledger row appeared as its attempt finished, before the other tasks were done; every observed JSON response parsed successfully.\\n\\nRun timestamps: 2026-10-11T19:01:31.886Z -> 19:06:27.554Z (12 Oct 00:31:31.886 -> 00:36:27.554 IST). Real routing-history reads delayed first spawn by about 139 seconds. No worker was consuming tokens during that wait; terminal printed the dashboard and budget first, then routing lines. Plan also took several minutes on history reads. This latency is a finding, not hidden as instant startup.\\n\\n## AO Overlap\\n\\nThese are actual AO daemon `createdAt` and terminated-session `updatedAt` (not identical engine attempt-start timestamps):\\n\\n| Task | AO session | Created (UTC) | Closed (UTC) |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| #20 | chip-parallel-proof-1 | 19:03:51.112220 | 19:05:27.388608 |\\n| #19 | chip-parallel-proof-2 | 19:03:53.840543 | 19:06:05.657242 |\\n| #21 | chip-parallel-proof-3 | 19:03:56.759365 | 19:05:07.045772 |\\n\\nAll three session lifetimes overlapped from 19:03:56.759365 to 19:05:07.045772: 70.286407 seconds. This measures coexistence, not continuous simultaneous token generation. Independent task spends increased during that interval. Each session had mode tui, harness codex, model gpt-5.6-luna; each final daemon record had `isTerminated: true` and activity exited. Memory's transient needs_input cleared without intervention and produced a commit; Tally did not kill it prematurely.\\n\\n## Tasks And Publishing\\n\\n| Task | Tokens (uncached/cached/output/total) | Cost USD | PR | Commit |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| #21 | 25782 / 207360 / 2706 / 235848 | 0.012550800 | [#22](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/22) | 68bfc6980c6531888fe3477b1d84…288 tokens truncated…-Back\\n\\n| Cell | Before USD | After USD | Delta USD |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Agent spend | 0.958404600 | 0.999523920 | 0.041119320 |\\n| Tier spend - cheap | 0.680313000 | 0.721432320 | 0.041119320 |\\n| Tier spend - middle | 0.278091600 | 0.278091600 | 0 |\\n| Tier spend - top | 0 | 0 | 0 |\\n\\nBefore read: 19:59:17 is NOT the timestamp; the actual saved snapshot is **2026-10-11T18:59:17.589Z**. After read: **2026-10-11T19:06:55.926Z**. Ledger sum 41119320 nanos = Agent spend delta = cheap delta, exact. Tier rows sum to Agent spend both before and after. Remaining run cap $1.958880680. cfo.ai write-back status ok. run.json: limitSource cli, systemOfRecord cfoai, monthly source cfoai/$40, cap $2, github-issues backlog with dedicated label, dryRun false. Accounting writes were handled by Tally, not these read-only observers.\\n\\n## Trace Read-Back\\n\\n| Task | Decision trace ID | Worker trace ID | Read-back |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| #21 | f2a8b6eb07efc12112bcce054c05e582 | 759a437ac0d326bba367b8275d5b742f | Both detail and spans 200; worker 23 spans |\\n| #20 | 2165fb70bc65c97ec68dad595623e077 | f7b0ab5ee687be8444ad853a39529dff | Decision detail/spans 404; worker both 200, 24 spans |\\n| #19 | 0a2551da02bbab47b42a047818274b0c | f5967797d277ad6441db62d9ede326a5 | Both detail and spans 200; worker 25 spans |\\n\\nEvery worker workflow starts `Tally run-20261011-190131Z #<issue> a1`, matching the correct task and attempt; native worker sessions differ from the run id. Delivered decision traces name the corresponding run/task/attempt. All three history outcome traces also delivered. #20 decision remained 404 before and after normal SDK shutdown; six recent trace pages contained the other two route traces but no #20 route trace. Delivery is therefore NOT established for that row, despite nonnull ledger ID and run neatlogs status ok. The cause is not established; this is not claimed to be fixed or merely eventual consistency. No ledger was hand-rewritten. This trace-delivery gap needs follow-up, not another paid run.\\n\\n## Terminal And Evidence\\n\\nVerbatim run terminal transcript: [ao-parallel-proof-terminal.log](ao-parallel-proof-terminal.log). Includes every routing, start, periodic spend, result and summary line, with original terminal carriage returns. Init, plan and doctor transcripts, JSON observations, original/post-shutdown trace reads, raw AO session/usage and PR evidence, before/after accounting snapshots are retained in the scratch root `/private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0`. Consolidated read-back JSON is attached beside this report as `ao-parallel-proof-evidence.json`.\\n\\nExact selected terminal lines (values not substituted with more precise ledger figures):\\n\\n```text\\ndashboard http://127.0.0.1:5203/?data=%2Fruns%2Flatest%2F\\ndata /runs/latest/\\nmonthly budget: $40.00 from cfo.ai; run cap: $2.00 (CLI --budget)\\n#20 attempt 1: worker chip-parallel-proof-1 started on cheap\\n#19 attempt 1: worker chip-parallel-proof-2 started on cheap\\n#21 attempt 1: worker chip-parallel-proof-3 started on cheap\\n#20 attempt 1: spend $0.0030\\n#19 attempt 1: spend $0.0024\\n#21 attempt 1: spend $0.0026\\n#21 attempt 1: passed $0.0126 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/22\\n#20 attempt 1: passed $0.0136 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/23\\n#19 attempt 1: passed $0.0150 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/24\\nfinished run-20261011-190131Z: 3 tasks, 3 attempts\\nsummary: 3 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; total $0.0411 against run cap $2.00\\nmonthly budget: $40.00 from cfo.ai; run cap: $2.00 (CLI --budget)\\nPR https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/22\\nPR https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/23\\nPR https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/24\\n```\\n\\nDashboard kept serving through evidence collection, then normal Ctrl+C shutdown flushed the SDK. A saved-run viewing command is:\\n\\n```sh\\ncd /private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/chip-parallel-proof\\n/private/tmp/tally-ao-parallel-proof.GTgYq0/prefix/bin/tally dashboard --port 5203\\n# Open http://127.0.0.1:5203/?data=%2Fruns%2Frun-20261011-190131Z%2F\\n```\\n\\nCleanup finding: installed `tally uninstall --yes` refused the intentionally changed ceiling config and printed a raw Node stack (`tally.yaml changed after init; preserve or remove it manually before uninstalling.`), exit 1. It made no removals. I then removed only the owned scratch AO project with `ao project rm chip-parallel-proof -y`, after all workers closed and evidence was saved. Run folder and proof config retained; issues/PRs left open. No target code/config was hand-edited except the explicitly approved local Tally ceiling. No further real run is needed to demonstrate overlap/accounting/publishing, and none was started.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"90b75f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.044269375,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":835,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 835)\\nTotal output lines: 55\\n\\ntally: a CFO for a fleet of coding agents\\n\\nUsage: tally <command> [options]\\n\\nCommands:\\n  experiment Run baseline and Tally repeats with a shared safety budget\\n  run      Run the backlog against the budget in tally.yaml\\n  demo     Run the full loop with simulated workers on a sample backlog\\n  dashboard Start the local dashboard server\\n  init     Set up tally.yaml for the current repository\\n  uninstall List and remove the recorded Tally installation\\n  doctor   Check that each integration is connected\\n  login    Connect an integration, e.g. tally login cfoai\\n  market   Find and qualify likely pil…535 tokens truncated…<json>   Apply human review labels to a cached market snapshot\\n  --jobs            Search engineering job posts for explicit coding-tool evidence\\n  --secondary <query.json> Include a cached firmographic table in the job report\\n                    market --plan checks free account pricing, without a search\\n  --out <dir>       New directory for tally publish (required)\\n  --runs <ids>      Comma-separated run folder ids (default: all real runs)\\n  --run <id>        Run id for traces drain; --output overrides its run directory\\n  -h, --help        Show this help\\n  -v, --version     Show the version\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","create_time":1791834685.256208}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
