{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:55:30.281Z","ordinal":17189,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_072dfc8f7183a0b2016acd3a8416b481918f6088d22a170d20","status":"completed","call_id":"call_92615b6c5611457887a31e5f559ea3c3","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Delete File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/README.md\\n*** Add File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/README.md\\n+![Meet Tally, the CFO for your agent fleet: pixel tally mark on a dark background](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/main/docs/assets/tally-banner.png)\\n+\\n+Tally is a CFO for coding agents: give it GitHub issues and a budget, and it routes, caps and verifies the work before opening pull requests.\\n+\\n+## Install\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+npm install -g tally-agents\\n+```\\n+\\n+Published version: **0.2.1**, checked on npm on 13 October 2026.\\n+Requires Node 20+; real work also needs Git, signed-in GitHub CLI and at least\\n+one signed-in coding agent. Optional integrations are not required.\\n+\\n+## 60-Second Quick Start\\n+\\n+From the root of your repository, with open issues carrying your chosen label:\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+tally init\\n+tally run --plan\\n+tally run --budget 3 --dashboard\\n+```\\n+\\n+Init asks for your runner, agents, verification command, budget and integrations.\\n+Review the plan's task list, tiers and ceilings before the last command:\\n+**the last command starts paid workers and may push task branches/open PRs**.\\n+Replace `3` with your approved run budget in USD. Account connection or setup\\n+can take longer than a minute. The dashboard keeps serving until Ctrl+C.\\n+\\n+Excerpt from a real three-worker AO run (not the simulated demo):\\n+\\n+```text\\n+#21 attempt 1: passed $0.0126 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/22\\n+#20 attempt 1: passed $0.0136 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/23\\n+#19 attempt 1: passed $0.0150 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/24\\n+finished run-20261011-190131Z: 3 tasks, 3 attempts\\n+summary: 3 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; total $0.0411 against run cap $2.00\\n+```\\n+\\n+Try it without accounts or paid workers: `tally demo --dashboard --port 0`.\\n+Its seven tasks and token usage are scripted, not evidence of real savings.\\n+\\n+## What Tally Does\\n+\\n+1. **Route:** size each task and choose a configured model tier using cost,\\n+   confidence and past outcomes when available.\\n+2. **Cap:** reserve the budget and meter each worker against its attempt ceiling.\\n+3. **Escalate:** stop capped/failed work and, when appropriate and affordable,\\n+   hand the branch and available checkpoint metadata to a stronger tier.\\n+4. **Verify:** run your repository's configured checks independently.\\n+5. **Open a pull request:** Tally commits/publishes verified work and records\\n+   the decision, cost and evidence. **Tally never merges its task PRs.**\\n+\\n+The run cap and remaining monthly budget both apply. Metering/polling can\\n+overshoot a ceiling: this is not a provider-side hard billing limit.\\n+\\n+## Runners and Agents\\n+\\n+| Runner | Execution | Agents |\\n+| --- | --- | --- |\\n+| Agent Orchestrator (`ao`) | AO manages worker sessions; opt into parallel workers during init or with `--parallel N` | Claude Code, Codex or configured mixed tiers |\\n+| Direct (`direct`) | Tally launches workers itself, one task at a time; no AO daemon needed | Claude Code or Codex, selected per tier |\\n+\\n+Both coding CLIs must be installed and signed in if both are configured. Tally\\n+does not silently replace a missing harness. Sign-in does not prove entitlement\\n+to every configured model. Claude uses a scoped consented allow-list; no runner\\n+uses bypass-permissions. [Runner details and proof](docs/EVIDENCE.md).\\n+\\n+## Optional Integrations\\n+\\n+| Product | Adds | When Off or Unavailable |\\n+| --- | --- | --- |\\n+| neatlogs | CFO decision/worker traces, read-back evidence, historical cost/pass rates by size and actual model, and history-derived caps when enough successful samples exist | No Tally decision export when off; use local price history, then explicit priors/configured caps when insufficient. Global hooks already installed are separate and may still trace sessions. |\\n+| Entire | Code-graph sizing, checkpoint/session evidence, past-failure recall and metadata-only handoff | Repository code search sizes tasks; no Entire checkpoint/hosted recall promised. No graph matches falls back to code search without calling a working graph disconnected. |\\n+| cfo.ai | Read monthly budget, reconcile real spend to tables, and optional workspace-shared per-attempt Ari reports | Use the local configured budget and ledger. Failed real writes retain `cfoai-spend-fallback.csv`; review/reconcile it before rerunning. |\\n+\\n+Accounts and credentials stay with their own login tools or in `~/.tally/`, not\\n+the repository. A trace ID alone is not proof that the trace was delivered.\\n+\\n+## Evidence, Not Promises\\n+\\n+| Matched Three-Task Pass | Estimated Cost | Final Tasks Passing |\\n+| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n+| Every task on the top tier | $1.22 | 3/3 |\\n+| Tally v1, built-in priors | $0.31 | 3/3 |\\n+| Tally v2, history enabled | $0.43 | 3/3 |\\n+\\n+These are **three tasks, one run each per pass**, at the same starting commit,\\n+using token/list-price estimates, not invoices: about 75% and 65% cheaper than\\n+the top-tier pass on this sample. Each pass also had three separately reported\\n+startup retries. Only C's large task used observed neatlogs statistics; no\\n+tier or cap changed. C cost more than B, so this does **not** prove that history\\n+improved on prior-only routing, or guarantee savings on your workload.\\n+\\n+- **Cap and escalation:** [fly-doom-jev PR #17](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/fly-doom-jev/pull/17),\\n+  run `run-20261012-100856Z`: cheap stopped at a $0.018 cap (metered $0.01956),\\n+  middle passed at $0.16958; the ceiling diagnosis was ledger-derived.\\n+- **Parallel AO:** three overlapping workers produced PRs #22-24 above at\\n+  $0.04111932 total. The later 0.2.1 sanity run produced\\n+  [PR #35](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/35) and\\n+  [PR #36](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/36),\\n+  2/2 passing at $0.02483996, with matching cfo.ai spend and read-back traces.\\n+- **History-derived ceiling:** the tested rule uses successful cost P90 x 1.5,\\n+  capped by config, after five successful samples for that size/tier/model.\\n+  The comparison and cited sanity runs had too few successful samples and used\\n+  configured caps; they are not live learned-cap proof.\\n+- **Four paths:** individual real PRs exist for Claude Code and Codex through\\n+  AO and directly. [Full evidence, limits and operational notes](docs/EVIDENCE.md).\\n+\\n+## Consent and Data Sharing\\n+\\n+Read what init proposes; selecting an integration can change external systems\\n+before the final config write. [Approval details](docs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md).\\n+\\n+- **Claude allow-list:** review file edits, git add/commit/status/diff and exact\\n+  test/setup scripts. Missing or stale script consent blocks launch; never\\n+  replace it with broad Bash or bypass permissions.\\n+- **Entire repository settings:** capture modifies listed settings/local hooks.\\n+  Publishing those settings to the default branch is a separate confirmation.\\n+  Review/trust agent hooks yourself. A hosted repository mirror is another\\n+  choice; generated summaries are off by default.\\n+- **neatlogs:** key verification exports a synthetic probe. Enabled tracing\\n+  sends decisions; optional global hooks can trace agent sessions outside Tally.\\n+- **cfo.ai:** fresh init asks for budget, spend and Ari context. Real attempts\\n+  update spend and, when enabled, send organization-memory reports containing\\n+  task/title/IDs, model/token/cost/decision/outcome, budgets and evidence links.\\n+  They exclude issue bodies, code/diffs, prompts/transcripts and raw spans.\\n+  Re-init currently uses a generic cfo.ai enable question: review the printed\\n+  reporting disclosure and `publishRunContext` proposal carefully.\\n+- **PR evidence:** Tally appends available Entire/neatlogs/cfo.ai links to task\\n+  PR bodies. There is currently **no separate init question for finance-URL\\n+  sharing**. Links do not grant account access, but their addresses become\\n+  visible to PR readers; do not enable this flow without accepting that.\\n+\\n+Never paste credentials into YAML, issues, PRs or diagnostic reports. Free-text\\n+task labels and result notes still need care; sanitization is not a complete\\n+privacy guarantee. Dry runs never write simulated spend/Ari reports, but can\\n+send decision traces if neatlogs is enabled.\\n+\\n+## Known Limits\\n+\\n+- Early product; verification is only as strong as your chosen test command.\\n+- Do not run two Tally processes against the same cfo.ai page: spend updates\\n+  are not atomic cross-process increments and can overwrite one another.\\n+- Mixed AO permission switching is locked within one Tally process only.\\n+  Direct-runner escalation and no-account onboarding need more live validation.\\n+- Direct processes cannot be reattached after Tally exits. Codex metering uses\\n+  an internal rollout format; missing metering stops the worker.\\n+- Model access, trace delivery and hosted checkpoint recall are independent\\n+  checks. Integration connectivity does not establish every evidence feature.\\n+- Old 0.1.0 configs load unchanged/sequentially; newer config fields do not work\\n+  on 0.1.0. Source tests need a Vitest-supported Node (22.12+ on Node 22),\\n+  although the built runtime is tested on Node 20.\\n+\\n+## For AI Agents\\n+\\n+Read [the self-contained agent guide](docs/AGENT_GUIDE.md) before using Tally\\n+on a person's repository. It names the decisions you must leave to the human,\\n+safe checks, command flags, ledger interpretation and failure responses.\\n+[llms.txt](llms.txt) provides discovery links. The guide ships with npm.\\n+\\n+## More\\n+\\n+- [Getting started and troubleshooting](docs/GETTING_STARTED.md)\\n+- [Business plan and labelled assumptions](docs/BUSINESS_PLAN.md)\\n+- [Detailed evidence and reference](docs/EVIDENCE.md)\\n+- [Project website](https://tally-agents-pi.vercel.app/)\\n+- [npm package](https://www.npmjs.com/package/tally-agents)\\n+\\n+GitHub installation alternative:\\n+`npm install -g github:Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack#release`.\\n+The release branch is prebuilt; main is source-only.\\n+\\n+## Licence\\n+\\n+[MIT](LICENSE).\\n*** Add File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/docs/AGENT_GUIDE.md\\n+# Tally Agent Guide\\n+\\n+Instructions for an AI coding agent asked to \\\"use Tally on this repo\\\".\\n+Self-contained for tally-agents 0.2.1. Work from the target repository root.\\n+Do not infer permission to spend money or publish from that request alone.\\n+\\n+## 1. Hard Rules\\n+\\n+- Never merge Tally's pull requests. The human reviews and merges.\\n+- Never push to a default branch. If Entire setup offers a settings commit\\n+  and default-branch push, stop and hand that step to the human; do not approve\\n+  it on their behalf. Normal Tally task publication targets worker branches.\\n+- Never pass bypass-permissions, danger/full-access flags or loosen a sandbox.\\n+- Never edit tally.yaml or an installation record to skip consent. Ask the\\n+  human to rerun init and review the proposed rules/changes.\\n+- Never run two Tally runs against one cfo.ai page at once. Cross-process spend\\n+  writes are not atomic; coordinate with other operators before starting.\\n+- Never paste keys/tokens into commands, config, logs or reports. Do not read\\n+  another tool's stored tokens. Tally secrets belong in ~/.tally/, managed by\\n+  its onboarding, not in the repository.\\n+- Never invent a test command, price, model entitlement or savings claim.\\n+  Verification and cost are only as reliable as their recorded inputs.\\n+- Do not start paid work, create issues, install global hooks or change an\\n+  external workspace without the relevant human approval.\\n+\\n+## 2. Preconditions: Read-Only Checks\\n+\\n+Run these without exposing credential values. Summarize status, not account\\n+details or raw authentication output. Missing optional binaries are expected.\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+pwd\\n+git status --short\\n+git rev-parse --show-toplevel\\n+node --version\\n+npm --version\\n+git --version\\n+gh --version\\n+gh auth status\\n+tally --version\\n+tally init --help\\n+tally run --help\\n+```\\n+\\n+Node must be 20+. The published version was checked as 0.2.1 on 13 October\\n+2026; do not assume source main and an installed package match. If missing,\\n+ask before installing with `npm install -g tally-agents`.\\n+\\n+Check the agents the human wants, not by invoking inference:\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+claude --version\\n+claude auth status\\n+codex --version\\n+codex login status\\n+```\\n+\\n+Claude status must report loggedIn true; Codex must report logged in. Missing\\n+or signed-out agents block those tiers; do not substitute another harness.\\n+For login, hand control to the human. No login command is a paid model probe.\\n+Ask separately about model entitlement: sign-in is not proof of access.\\n+\\n+If AO is installed and the human wants AO:\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+ao version\\n+ao status --json\\n+```\\n+\\n+Require a ready/healthy daemon; direct does not need AO. Tally resolves AO from\\n+PATH, TALLY_AO_BIN, repo.aoBin or the macOS AO app bundle. An absent `ao` on\\n+PATH alone does not establish that Tally cannot find it. Do not change daemon\\n+or project settings just to make a check pass.\\n+\\n+For enabled Entire, read its state before approving changes:\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+entire --version\\n+entire auth status --json\\n+entire plugin list\\n+entire status --json\\n+```\\n+\\n+## 3. Named Human Decisions\\n+\\n+Put these choices to the human explicitly and retain their answers:\\n+\\n+| Decision | What the Human Must Choose |\\n+| --- | --- |\\n+| Budget and caps | Monthly/local fallback budget, approved USD run cap, per-size/tier ceilings, how much to reserve for escalation; estimated cost can overshoot |\\n+| Runner | AO for opt-in parallel workers, or direct for one at a time; parallel count if AO |\\n+| Agents and tiers | Claude Code, Codex or mixed; model IDs, prices and access; no automatic harness substitution |\\n+| Tasks and verification | Exact issue label/task set, meaningful test command, setup command (which executes repo code/installs dependencies) |\\n+| neatlogs | Decision exports, history-read project/access and optional machine-wide hooks, including sessions outside Tally |\\n+| Entire | Login/plugin, capture, explicit human-owned default-branch settings publication, hook trust, optional hosted mirror |\\n+| cfo.ai budget/spend | Workspace/scenario/tables, budget reads and real spend write-back; missing tables require separate creation approval |\\n+| Claude allow-list | Scoped file writes, git add/commit/status/diff and content-bound external test/setup scripts; no broad Bash rule |\\n+| cfo.ai reports | Managed guide and organization-shared operational reports with task/title/IDs, model/token/pricing/cost/result/decision, budget snapshots and evidence links |\\n+| PR evidence links | Available Entire/neatlogs/cfo.ai URLs are appended to task PRs; currently no dedicated init prompt for finance-link sharing, so ask the human yourself |\\n+| Publishing/spending | Final approval for this concrete task set, budget, worker branch pushes and PR creation; not permission to merge |\\n+\\n+Fresh init's cfo.ai question names Ari context. Re-init uses a generic enable\\n+question and can add reporting to an existing installation. Explain that gap\\n+before re-init. Reports exclude issue bodies, source/diffs, worker prompts/\\n+transcripts and raw trace spans, but free-text titles/result notes are still\\n+shared metadata and sanitization cannot guarantee all sensitive text is removed.\\n+Declining integration onboarding leaves it off; do not force-enable it in YAML.\\n+\\n+## 4. Init: Preview Before Applying\\n+\\n+Interactive `tally init` is the preferred account-connection/consent flow.\\n+Piped input is rejected. Give the human the terminal for prompts and browser\\n+OAuth; do not fake answers. Existing config is preserved by the re-init path.\\n+\\n+Explicit preview example, with all integrations off:\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+tally init --dry-run --yes --runner direct --harness codex \\\\\\n+  --budget 5 --issue-label tally --test-command 'npm test' \\\\\\n+  --setup-command '' --neatlogs no --entire no --cfoai no --verbose\\n+```\\n+\\n+Replace the example budget, label and commands with approved repository values.\\n+`npm test` is not correct for every repository. Empty setup means none.\\n+`--dry-run` previews; `--yes` must not be used as blanket external consent.\\n+\\n+After specific approval, the non-interactive config-apply form is the same\\n+command **without `--dry-run`**. Use `--config PATH` if not tally.yaml.\\n+`--runner ao` selects AO; `--parallel N` opts into its worker count;\\n+`--harness claude-code` or `mixed` selects the requested harness set.\\n+`--allow-claude` explicitly approves the printed allow-list, so use it only\\n+after the human reviews those exact test/setup contents. The CLI also accepts\\n+`--model-access-fallback-tier NAME` for one budget-checked access-denial retry.\\n+Never choose that fallback without the human's agreement.\\n+\\n+`--neatlogs yes`, `--entire yes` and `--cfoai yes` are integration opt-ins,\\n+not evidence that onboarding can finish unattended: OAuth, secret input,\\n+workspace choice, table creation and hook trust may need the human. Selecting\\n+cfo.ai includes Ari reporting when supported. Global neatlogs hooks can affect\\n+all matching agent sessions. If any requested decision is missing, stop.\\n+\\n+After init, run:\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+tally doctor --config tally.yaml\\n+gh issue list --label tally --state open\\n+tally run --plan --config tally.yaml --budget 5\\n+```\\n+\\n+Use the chosen label/budget, not these literals blindly. Do not create/label\\n+issues without approval. A plan with zero tasks starts no worker; inspect the\\n+label and open PR exclusions. Doctor checks connections, not model entitlement\\n+or successful delivery of every trace/checkpoint feature.\\n+\\n+## 5. Explain the Plan Before Spending\\n+\\n+Plan starts no worker and does not write spend or PRs; it can read GitHub,\\n+repository/Entire signals, neatlogs history and cfo.ai budget. It is not offline.\\n+\\n+Report task count/IDs, selected harness/model/tier, size/confidence, per-attempt\\n+ceiling, routing explanation and history source. Distinguish observed samples\\n+from priors, and a configured cap from a P90-derived cap. History is keyed by\\n+size, tier and actual model; five successful samples are needed for learned\\n+caps. The run cap and remaining monthly budget both apply. Parallel tasks may\\n+reserve first-attempt plus escalation costs; unused reservations are not spend.\\n+\\n+Tell the human which integrations are off/missing, what falls back locally,\\n+and that approved real work can edit code, execute setup/tests and publish PRs.\\n+If the effective budget, task set or permissions changed since approval,\\n+ask again. Do not silently increase a cap because a reservation did not fit.\\n+\\n+Optional safe simulation after reviewing the selected configuration:\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+tally run --dry-run --plan --config tally.yaml --budget 5\\n+tally run --dry-run --config tally.yaml --budget 5\\n+```\\n+\\n+Dry runs use simulated workers; they do not test model access or real task\\n+quality. Enabled neatlogs can export simulated decision traces. For a fully\\n+offline-style demo, use `tally demo` with its bundled integrations-off config;\\n+do not alter a person's config to hide declined consent.\\n+\\n+## 6. Start Only the Approved Run\\n+\\n+Once the human approves the plan, run-cap and task publication:\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+tally run --config tally.yaml --budget 5 --dashboard --port 0\\n+```\\n+\\n+Optional `--only TASK_ID` limits selection; use an ID exactly as shown by plan.\\n+AO only: `--parallel N` requests the approved concurrency; direct stays\\n+sequential. `--open` opens the dashboard in a browser. `--baseline` uses the\\n+strongest tier without task ceilings: do not use it unless explicitly approved.\\n+There is no required `--yes` for ordinary run; executing it is the spend/\\n+publication action. Do not add experiment modes or paid retries opportunistically.\\n+\\n+Record the printed run ID, output directory and dashboard URL immediately.\\n+The dashboard keeps serving after completion until Ctrl+C. A direct process\\n+cannot be reattached after Tally exits. If interrupted, inspect saved evidence\\n+and existing PRs before restarting; restarting can spend again.\\n+\\n+## 7. Read State and Ledger\\n+\\n+By default, local output is `.tally/runs/RUN_ID/run.json` and `ledger.json`,\\n+relative to the current working directory; trust the paths printed by the CLI.\\n+`latest/` mirrors the latest run. Ledger is an array of attempt rows; run.json\\n+contains tasks, budget and integrations. Read with a structured JSON parser:\\n+\\n+```sh\\n+node -e 'const fs=require(\\\"node:fs\\\");const r=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\\\".tally/runs/latest/run.json\\\",\\\"utf8\\\"));const l=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\\\".tally/runs/latest/ledger.json\\\",\\\"utf8\\\"));console.log(JSON.stringify({runId:r.runId,status:r.status,dryRun:r.dryRun,budget:r.budget,integrations:r.integrations,tasks:r.tasks.map(t=>({id:t.taskId,status:t.status,reason:t.statusReason,usd:t.spentNanos/1e9,pr:t.prUrl})),attempts:l.map(a=>({id:a.attemptId,tier:a.tier,model:a.model,usd:a.estimatedCostNanos/1e9,result:a.result,reason:a.resultReason,failureAssessment:a.failureAssessment,pr:a.prUrl}))},null,2));'\\n+```\\n+\\n+Money fields are integer USD nanos; divide by 1e9. run.status is running,\\n+finished or interrupted; **finished does not mean every task passed**.\\n+Task status includes pending/running/passed/failed/skipped. Live spend can\\n+appear in run.json before the ended attempt appears in ledger.json. Read all\\n+attempts, including stopped/errors/escalations; never count only passing spend.\\n+Costs are list-price estimates, not invoices. Inspect price/priceNote/costSource,\\n+scopeWarnings, permissionWarnings and integration detail when relevant.\\n+\\n+failureAssessment, if present, records kind, source (neatlogs or ledger),\\n+evidence and retryable. A ledger-derived ceiling reason is not trace-derived.\\n+traceId is the CFO decision; workerTraceId is separate. Null/unverified evidence\\n+is not proof of delivery. checkpointId and entireSessionId differ from AO's\\n+sessionId. Do not publish raw traces/transcripts or financial snapshots in your\\n+human report without consent.\\n+\\n+## 8. Failure Responses\\n+\\n+| Symptom | Correct Response |\\n+| --- | --- |\\n+| Reservation/next ceiling does not fit | Report skipped/failed task and remaining budget; ask about task order or a new cap, never raise it yourself |\\n+| AO project not found/not ready | Check doctor and the displayed project diagnostic; ask the human to re-init/repair AO or choose direct, never silently switch |\\n+| Harness missing/signed out | Report selected agent and login fix; hand login to the human, then rerun doctor/plan |\\n+| Model unavailable | Check recorded access denial; only the configured budget-checked access fallback may retry; do not invent an accessible model |\\n+| Missing/stale Claude consent | Stop; human must rerun init and approve exact script rules, not hand-edit/bypass them |\\n+| Ceiling stop | Inspect actual spend, stopped branch/checkpoint and assessment; allow Tally's approved affordable escalation, never same-tier rerun yourself |\\n+| Verification failed | Report configured command/verdict and retained branch; do not weaken tests or merge; escalate only within the approved plan |\\n+| Tool/permission/environment failure | Inspect source and evidence; stronger models cannot fix missing credentials or a shared permission wall; ask for repair rather than paid retries |\\n+| neatlogs read/export/drain error | Preserve pending batches and ledger; report local fallback versus unverified worker trace. Do not claim connected means all traces delivered |\\n+| Entire no symbols/recall unavailable | Code-search sizing can be valid; missing hosted recall is not local capture failure. Do not enable a mirror without consent |\\n+| cfo.ai read/write/report error | Report local budget source/CSV fallback and sanitized detail; avoid concurrent writers, preserve evidence and reconcile before rerunning |\\n+| PR push/evidence-update failure | Inspect existing branch/PR before retrying. Publishing does one automatic transient push retry; never force-push or default-branch push |\\n+\\n+For a finished run's approved trace recovery (network export/read-back, not\\n+worker inference), `tally traces drain --run RUN_ID` is available. Ask before\\n+exporting and restrict recovery to this run. Do not delete unrelated spool data.\\n+\\n+## 9. Report to the Human\\n+\\n+Report run ID and finished/interrupted state; task counts and individual PR\\n+links; total cost including failures/retries versus the approved cap; verification\\n+results; failure classes/evidence/source; off/broken integrations and fallbacks;\\n+unverified trace/checkpoint links; and whether spend/report write-back succeeded.\\n+Name what remains unproven. Distinguish simulations from real work. Leave PRs\\n+open for review and state that nothing was merged by you.\\n*** Add File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/llms.txt\\n+# Tally\\n+\\n+> A CFO for coding agents: route, cap, escalate, verify and open PRs. Never merge.\\n+\\n+## Instructions\\n+\\n+- [Agent guide](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/main/docs/AGENT_GUIDE.md): Self-contained commands, human decisions, safety rules and failure handling. Read first when asked to use Tally on a repository.\\n+- [Getting started](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/main/docs/GETTING_STARTED.md): Human onboarding and troubleshooting.\\n+- [Evidence](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/main/docs/EVIDENCE.md): Recorded proofs and limits.\\n+- [Business plan](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/main/docs/BUSINESS_PLAN.md): Measured results and labelled commercial assumptions.\\n*** Update File: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/package.json\\n@@\\n     \\\"docs/\\\",\\n+    \\\"docs/AGENT_GUIDE.md\\\",\\n+    \\\"llms.txt\\\",\\n@@\\n     \\\"!dist/**/testing/**\\\",\\n+    \\\"!docs/assets/**\\\",\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","create_time":1791834756.1111012}}}
