{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:59:15.827Z","ordinal":17223,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-83ffeea8-3deb-457f-bb01-8f191bcf8167","process_id":"17474","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -C 2 'An Entire opt|docs/|summary|publishing writes' docs/EVIDENCE.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -C 2 'An Entire opt|docs/|summary|publishing writes' docs/EVIDENCE.md","query":"An Entire opt|docs/|summary|publishing writes","path":"EVIDENCE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"88-ends with a ledger tying spend to each attempt, its test result and any opened PR.\n89-\n90:**Start here: [Getting Started](docs/GETTING_STARTED.md)** covers the no-account demo, every init question, your first real run, troubleshooting and uninstall.\n91-\n92-Status: early build. Published npm version checked 13 October 2026 is 0.2.1.\n--\n176-the agent starts and is recorded separately as `setupDurationMs`.\n177-\n178:The live meter reads [Claude's partial stream events](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/streaming-output)\n179-and deduplicates API message ids; final JSON usage settles the same session,\n180-not an additional charge. Usage arrives at message boundaries, so a ceiling\n181-can overshoot during a long generation or between watcher polls. Prompt-cache\n182:writes use [Anthropic's 5-minute / 1-hour multipliers](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-caching)\n183-of 1.25x / 2x the configured input price. Existing ledger costs are unchanged.\n184-Subagents and MCP tools are disabled so their unmetered work cannot escape the\n--\n302-   no tasks to work on.\n303-2. **`tally init`** asks for a budget and the issue label, shows the\n304:   short configuration summary and the AO changes it would make, and applies\n305-   nothing until you confirm. Type the label exactly as it is on GitHub.\n306-3. **`tally doctor`** prints one line per integration: connected, missing or\n--\n331-the selected agents' global settings; those hooks trace matching sessions on\n332-this computer, including sessions outside Tally.\n333:The final summary shows the permission policy for this AO project's workers.\n334-Uninstall restores owned project settings; it never enables bypass-permissions.\n335-\n--\n369-\n370-Doctor and real runs use the same resolver. Init checks AO, git, GitHub auth\n371:and requested integrations before applying changes. An Entire opt-in requires\n372-Entire to be enabled in the target repo; init prints `entire enable` and stops\n373-if it is not, rather than installing capture hooks without consent.\n--\n436-continues after the run for inspection, until Ctrl+C. Terminal output includes\n437-routes, worker session IDs, spend updates at most every ten seconds, attempt\n438:results, PR URLs and a final summary. `--budget` is a cap for this run, not a\n439-replacement for the monthly budget: Tally applies the lower of the run cap and\n440-the remaining monthly budget, including for the direct sequential runner. Plan\n441:and summary show both, including the amount available now and monthly source.\n442-When cfo.ai supplies the monthly budget, init asks only for a local fallback\n443-after connecting it. Worker trace IDs require correlated trace read-back;\n444-unverified delivery is shown as missing rather than success. See\n445:[Human approval points](docs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md) for operations that still\n446-require explicit user consent or review.\n447-\n--\n498-## Routing Evidence\n499-\n500:See the [Tally business plan](docs/BUSINESS_PLAN.md) for share-of-savings pricing,\n501-the measured three-task comparison, explicitly labelled unit-economics and\n502-pilot-funnel assumptions, cfo.ai usage and the remaining commercial risks.\n--\n546-\n54