{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:01:48.029Z","ordinal":17252,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-0b4240b1-1534-4329-b933-6ce6bd09bc0e","changes":{"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5/docs/EVIDENCE.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -89,3 +89,3 @@\n \n-**Start here: [Getting Started](docs/GETTING_STARTED.md)** covers the no-account demo, every init question, your first real run, troubleshooting and uninstall.\n+**Start here: [Getting Started](GETTING_STARTED.md)** covers the no-account demo, every init question, your first real run, troubleshooting and uninstall.\n \n@@ -304,3 +304,5 @@\n    short configuration summary and the AO changes it would make, and applies\n-   nothing until you confirm. Type the label exactly as it is on GitHub.\n+   configuration/AO changes after confirmation. Integration onboarding has its\n+   own earlier consent steps and can connect external services before that\n+   final confirmation. Type the label exactly as it is on GitHub.\n 3. **`tally doctor`** prints one line per integration: connected, missing or\n@@ -370,5 +372,6 @@\n Doctor and real runs use the same resolver. Init checks AO, git, GitHub auth\n-and requested integrations before applying changes. An Entire opt-in requires\n-Entire to be enabled in the target repo; init prints `entire enable` and stops\n-if it is not, rather than installing capture hooks without consent.\n+and requested integrations. Entire onboarding checks this repository's capture\n+settings and offers enabling them with explicit consent; settings publication\n+to the default branch has its own approval, and Codex hook trust remains a\n+human step. Declining keeps the integration off.\n \n@@ -444,3 +447,3 @@\n unverified delivery is shown as missing rather than success. See\n-[Human approval points](docs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md) for operations that still\n+[Human approval points](HUMAN_APPROVALS.md) for operations that still\n require explicit user consent or review.\n@@ -499,3 +502,3 @@\n \n-See the [Tally business plan](docs/BUSINESS_PLAN.md) for share-of-savings pricing,\n+See the [Tally business plan](BUSINESS_PLAN.md) for share-of-savings pricing,\n the measured three-task comparison, explicitly labelled unit-economics and\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM docs/EVIDENCE.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1791835307997,"completed_at_ms":1791835308029}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:01:48.374Z","ordinal":17253,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2872c6de-1f62-4e00-b0d7-c4f7a0b3ccd9","process_id":"20526","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,90p' README.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,90p' README.md","name":"README.md","path":"README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"![Meet Tally, the CFO for your agent fleet: pixel tally mark on a dark background](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/main/docs/assets/tally-banner.png)\n\nTally is a CFO for coding agents: give it GitHub issues and a budget, and it routes, caps and verifies the work before opening pull requests.\n\n## Install\n\n```sh\nnpm install -g tally-agents\n```\n\nPublished version: **0.2.1**, checked on npm on 13 October 2026.\nRequires Node 20+; real work also needs Git, signed-in GitHub CLI and at least\none signed-in coding agent. Optional integrations are not required.\n\n## 60-Second Quick Start\n\nFrom your repository root, with open issues carrying your chosen label:\n\n```sh\ntally init\ntally run --plan\ntally run --budget 3 --dashboard\n```\n\nInit asks about runner, agents, verification, budget and integrations. Review\nthe plan before the last command: **it starts paid workers and may push task\nbranches/open PRs**. Replace `3` with your approved USD run budget. Connection\nand setup can take longer than a minute; the dashboard serves until Ctrl+C.\n\nExcerpt from a real AO run, not the simulated demo:\n\n```text\n#21 attempt 1: passed $0.0126 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/22\n#20 attempt 1: passed $0.0136 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/23\n#19 attempt 1: passed $0.0150 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/24\nfinished run-20261011-190131Z: 3 tasks, 3 attempts\nsummary: 3 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; total $0.0411 against run cap $2.00\n```\n\nTry it without accounts or paid workers: `tally demo --dashboard --port 0`.\nThe seven demo tasks and token usage are scripted, not real savings evidence.\n\n## What Tally Does\n\n1. **Route:** size tasks and choose configured tiers using confidence, cost\n   and past outcomes when available.\n2. **Cap:** reserve budget and meter workers against their attempt ceilings.\n3. **Escalate:** stop capped/failed work and, when appropriate and affordable,\n   pass its branch and available checkpoint metadata to a stronger tier.\n4. **Verify:** independently run your configured repository checks.\n5. **Open a pull request:** publish verified work with a cost/evidence ledger.\n   **Tally never merges its task PRs.**\n\nBoth the run cap and remaining monthly budget apply. Polling/metering can\novershoot a ceiling; this is not a provider-side hard billing limit.\n\n## Runners and Agents\n\n| Runner | Execution | Agents |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Agent Orchestrator (`ao`) | AO manages sessions; opt into parallel workers at init or with `--parallel N` | Claude Code, Codex or configured mixed tiers |\n| Direct (`direct`) | Tally launches workers itself, one task at a time; no AO daemon needed | Claude Code or Codex, selected per tier |\n\nInstall/sign in to every configured harness. Tally never silently substitutes\none for a missing agent. Login does not prove model entitlement. Claude uses\na scoped consented allow-list; no runner uses bypass-permissions.\n[Runner details and proofs](docs/EVIDENCE.md).\n\n## Optional Integrations\n\n| Product | Adds | When Off or Unavailable |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| neatlogs | Decision/worker traces, read-back evidence, cost/pass-rate history and learned caps keyed by size and actual model | No Tally decision export when off; local history, then explicit priors/config caps. Previously installed global hooks may still trace sessions. |\n| Entire | Graph sizing, checkpoints, past-failure recall and metadata-only handoff | Repository search sizes tasks; no Entire checkpoints/hosted recall promised. No symbol matches falls back without calling a working graph disconnected. |\n| cfo.ai | Monthly budget read, reconciled real spend and workspace-shared per-attempt Ari reports when enabled | Local budget/ledger; failed writes retain `cfoai-spend-fallback.csv` for reconciliation. |\n\nCredentials stay in their login tools or `~/.tally/`, not the repository.\nA stored trace ID does not itself prove delivery.\n\n## Evidence, Not Promises\n\n| Matched Three-Task Pass | Estimated Cost | Final Tasks Passing |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Every task on the top tier | $1.22 | 3/3 |\n| Tally v1, built-in priors | $0.31 | 3/3 |\n| Tally v2, history enabled | $0.43 | 3/3 |\n\n**Three tasks, one run each per pass**, same initial commit, list-price token\nestimates rather than invoices: about 75% and 65% cheaper on that sample. Each\npass also had three separately recorded startup retries. Only C's large task\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"![Meet Tally, the CFO for your agent fleet: pixel tally mark on a dark background](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/main/docs/assets/tally-banner.png)\n\nTally is a CFO for coding agents: give it GitHub issues and a budget, and it routes, caps and verifies the work before opening pull requests.\n\n## Install\n\n```sh\nnpm install -g tally-agents\n```\n\nPublished version: **0.2.1**, checked on npm on 13 October 2026.\nRequires Node 20+; real work also needs Git, signed-in GitHub CLI and at least\none signed-in coding agent. Optional integrations are not required.\n\n## 60-Second Quick Start\n\nFrom your repository root, with open issues carrying your chosen label:\n\n```sh\ntally init\ntally run --plan\ntally run --budget 3 --dashboard\n```\n\nInit asks about runner, agents, verification, budget and integrations. Review\nthe plan before the last command: **it starts paid workers and may push task\nbranches/open PRs**. Replace `3` with your approved USD run budget. Connection\nand setup can take longer than a minute; the dashboard serves until Ctrl+C.\n\nExcerpt from a real AO run, not the simulated demo:\n\n```text\n#21 attempt 1: passed $0.0126 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/22\n#20 attempt 1: passed $0.0136 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/23\n#19 attempt 1: passed $0.0150 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/24\nfinished run-20261011-190131Z: 3 tasks, 3 attempts\nsummary: 3 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; total $0.0411 against run cap $2.00\n```\n\nTry it without accounts or paid workers: `tally demo --dashboard --port 0`.\nThe seven demo tasks and token usage are scripted, not real savings evidence.\n\n## What Tally Does\n\n1. **Route:** size tasks and choose configured tiers using confidence, cost\n   and past outcomes when available.\n2. **Cap:** reserve budget and meter workers against their attempt ceilings.\n3. **Escalate:** stop capped/failed work and, when appropriate and affordable,\n   pass its branch and available checkpoint metadata to a stronger tier.\n4. **Verify:** independently run your configured repository checks.\n5. **Open a pull request:** publish verified work with a cost/evidence ledger.\n   **Tally never merges its task PRs.**\n\nBoth the run cap and remaining monthly budget apply. Polling/metering can\novershoot a ceiling; this is not a provider-side hard billing limit.\n\n## Runners and Agents\n\n| Runner | Execution | Agents |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Agent Orchestrator (`ao`) | AO manages sessions; opt into parallel workers at init or with `--parallel N` | Claude Code, Codex or configured mixed tiers |\n| Direct (`direct`) | Tally launches workers itself, one task at a time; no AO daemon needed | Claude Code or Codex, selected per tier |\n\nInstall/sign in to every configured harness. Tally never silently substitutes\none for a missing agent. Login does not prove model entitlement. Claude uses\na scoped consented allow-list; no runner uses bypass-permissions.\n[Runner details and proofs](docs/EVIDENCE.md).\n\n## Optional Integrations\n\n| Product | Adds | When Off or Unavailable |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| neatlogs | Decision/worker traces, read-back evidence, cost/pass-rate history and learned caps keyed by size and actual model | No Tally decision export when off; local history, then explicit priors/config caps. Previously installed global hooks may still trace sessions. |\n| Entire | Graph sizing, checkpoints, past-failure recall and metadata-only handoff | Repository search sizes tasks; no Entire checkpoints/hosted recall promised. No symbol matches falls back without calling a working graph disconnected. |\n| cfo.ai | Monthly budget read, reconciled real spend and workspace-shared per-attempt Ari reports when enabled | Local budget/ledger; failed writes retain `cfoai-spend-fallback.csv` for reconciliation. |\n\nCredentials stay in their login tools or `~/.tally/`, not the repository.\nA stored trace ID does not itself prove delivery.\n\n## Evidence, Not Promises\n\n| Matched Three-Task Pass | Estimated Cost | Final Tasks Passing |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Every task on the top tier | $1.22 | 3/3 |\n| Tally v1, built-in priors | $0.31 | 3/3 |\n| Tally v2, history enabled | $0.43 | 3/3 |\n\n**Three tasks, one run each per pass**, same initial commit, list-price token\nestimates rather than invoices: about 75% and 65% cheaper on that sample. Each\npass also had three separately recorded startup retries. Only C's large task\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":9792},"formatted_output":"![Meet Tally, the CFO for your agent fleet: pixel tally mark on a dark background](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/main/docs/assets/tally-banner.png)\n\nTally is a CFO for coding agents: give it GitHub issues and a budget, and it routes, caps and verifies the work before opening pull requests.\n\n## Install\n\n```sh\nnpm install -g tally-agents\n```\n\nPublished version: **0.2.1**, checked on npm on 13 October 2026.\nRequires Node 20+; real work also needs Git, signed-in GitHub CLI and at least\none signed-in coding agent. Optional integrations are not required.\n\n## 60-Second Quick Start\n\nFrom your repository root, with open issues carrying your chosen label:\n\n```sh\ntally init\ntally run --plan\ntally run --budget 3 --dashboard\n```\n\nInit asks about runner, agents, verification, budget and integrations. Review\nthe plan before the last command: **it starts paid workers and may push task\nbranches/open PRs**. Replace `3` with your approved USD run budget. Connection\nand setup can take longer than a minute; the dashboard serves until Ctrl+C.\n\nExcerpt from a real AO run, not the simulated demo:\n\n```text\n#21 attempt 1: passed $0.0126 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/22\n#20 attempt 1: passed $0.0136 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/23\n#19 attempt 1: passed $0.0150 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/24\nfinished run-20261011-190131Z: 3 tasks, 3 attempts\nsummary: 3 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; total $0.0411 against run cap $2.00\n```\n\nTry it without accounts or paid workers: `tally demo --dashboard --port 0`.\nThe seven demo tasks and token usage are scripted, not real savings evidence.\n\n## What Tally Does\n\n1. **Route:** size tasks and choose configured tiers using confidence, cost\n   and past outcomes when available.\n2. **Cap:** reserve budget and meter workers against their attempt ceilings.\n3. **Escalate:** stop capped/failed work and, when appropriate and affordable,\n   pass its branch and available checkpoint metadata to a stronger tier.\n4. **Verify:** independently run your configured repository checks.\n5. **Open a pull request:** publish verified work with a cost/evidence ledger.\n   **Tally never merges its task PRs.**\n\nBoth the run cap and remaining monthly budget apply. Polling/metering can\novershoot a ceiling; this is not a provider-side hard billing limit.\n\n## Runners and Agents\n\n| Runner | Execution | Agents |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Agent Orchestrator (`ao`) | AO manages sessions; opt into parallel workers at init or with `--parallel N` | Claude Code, Codex or configured mixed tiers |\n| Direct (`direct`) | Tally launches workers itself, one task at a time; no AO daemon needed | Claude Code or Codex, selected per tier |\n\nInstall/sign in to every configured harness. Tally never silently substitutes\none for a missing agent. Login does not prove model entitlement. Claude uses\na scoped consented allow-list; no runner uses bypass-permissions.\n[Runner details and proofs](docs/EVIDENCE.md).\n\n## Optional Integrations\n\n| Product | Adds | When Off or Unavailable |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| neatlogs | Decision/worker traces, read-back evidence, cost/pass-rate history and learned caps keyed by size and actual model | No Tally decision export when off; local history, then explicit priors/config caps. Previously installed global hooks may still trace sessions. |\n| Entire | Graph sizing, checkpoints, past-failure recall and metadata-only handoff | Repository search sizes tasks; no Entire checkpoints/hosted recall promised. No symbol matches falls back without calling a working graph disconnected. |\n| cfo.ai | Monthly budget read, reconciled real spend and workspace-shared per-attempt Ari reports when enabled | Local budget/ledger; failed writes retain `cfoai-spend-fallback.csv` for reconciliation. |\n\nCredentials stay in their login tools or `~/.tally/`, not the repository.\nA stored trace ID does not itself prove delivery.\n\n## Evidence, Not Promises\n\n| Matched Three-Task Pass | Estimated Cost | Final Tasks Passing |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Every task on the top tier | $1.22 | 3/3 |\n| Tally v1, built-in priors | $0.31 | 3/3 |\n| Tally v2, history enabled | $0.43 | 3/3 |\n\n**Three tasks, one run each per pass**, same initial commit, list-price token\nestimates rather than invoices: about 75% and 65% cheaper on that sample. Each\npass also had three separately recorded startup retries. Only C's large task\n"},"started_at_ms":1791835308374,"completed_at_ms":1791835308374}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:01:48.615Z","ordinal":17254,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ca9b1637-58ad-44c6-8576-c28c9c731a03","process_id":"20218","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/skills/using-ao/commands/report.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/skills/using-ao/commands/report.md","name":"report.md","path":"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/skills/using-ao/commands/report.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# ao report\n\nPersist a meaningful worker report for durable delivery to the active project\norchestrator.\n\n## Syntax\n\n```text\nao report <free-form-text>\nao report --checkpoint --note <text> [output flags]\nao report --needs-input --note <text> [output flags]\nao report --stuck --note <text> [output flags]\nao report --done --note <text> [output flags]\n```\n\nOutput flags are repeatable:\n\n```text\n--artifact <opaque-reference>\n--pr-created <pr-or-mr-url>\n--pr-reviewed <pr-or-mr-url>\n```\n\nUse reports for meaningful transitions, decisions, blockers, required input,\noutputs, and terminal judgment. Do not narrate routine commands. Outputs do not\nimply completion, and `--done` does not terminate the session.\n\nAttach a reviewable deliverable as soon as it is ready, not only at `--done`:\nuse `--artifact <reference>` on the report for the milestone that produced it.\nExamples include a requested document, a rendered dashboard, or another output\nthe orchestrator or human needs to open directly. `--artifact` takes any opaque\nreference string; it is not validated as a URL.\nIn a chat session, an HTML file from the artifact directory that you attach\nwith `--artifact` also shows in the thread.\n\nRoutine test logs, command output, scratch notes, and intermediate diagnostics\nare working material, not deliverables. Do not attach them unless requested or\nneeded to explain an actionable failure. Summarize validation in the report note;\nwhen a separate deliverable is useful, prefer one consolidated report over\nindividual logs. Ordinary progress updates and concise final answers do not\nneed separate artifact files.\n\nSaving a local artifact or attaching its reference to an AO report is not\nexternal publishing authorization. Publish externally only within the\nuser-authorized scope.\n\n`--pr-created` and `--pr-reviewed` accept complete GitHub PR or GitLab MR URLs.\n\n`--needs-input` requests immediate non-interrupting delivery. `--stuck`\nrequests immediate delivery plus a rate-limited interrupt. Informational work\nbatches for up to one hour, while the first done report opens a fixed five\nminute settlement window.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```bash\nao report \"The focused tests pass; I am checking the generated diff.\"\nao report --done --note \"Ready for review.\" \\\n  --pr-created https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/88\n```\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# ao report\n\nPersist a meaningful worker report for durable delivery to the active project\norchestrator.\n\n## Syntax\n\n```text\nao report <free-form-text>\nao report --checkpoint --note <text> [output flags]\nao report --needs-input --note <text> [output flags]\nao report --stuck --note <text> [output flags]\nao report --done --note <text> [output flags]\n```\n\nOutput flags are repeatable:\n\n```text\n--artifact <opaque-reference>\n--pr-created <pr-or-mr-url>\n--pr-reviewed <pr-or-mr-url>\n```\n\nUse reports for meaningful transitions, decisions, blockers, required input,\noutputs, and terminal judgment. Do not narrate routine commands. Outputs do not\nimply completion, and `--done` does not terminate the session.\n\nAttach a reviewable deliverable as soon as it is ready, not only at `--done`:\nuse `--artifact <reference>` on the report for the milestone that produced it.\nExamples include a requested document, a rendered dashboard, or another output\nthe orchestrator or human needs to open directly. `--artifact` takes any opaque\nreference string; it is not validated as a URL.\nIn a chat session, an HTML file from the artifact directory that you attach\nwith `--artifact` also shows in the thread.\n\nRoutine test logs, command output, scratch notes, and intermediate diagnostics\nare working material, not deliverables. Do not attach them unless requested or\nneeded to explain an actionable failure. Summarize validation in the report note;\nwhen a separate deliverable is useful, prefer one consolidated report over\nindividual logs. Ordinary progress updates and concise final answers do not\nneed separate artifact files.\n\nSaving a local artifact or attaching its reference to an AO report is not\nexternal publishing authorization. Publish externally only within the\nuser-authorized scope.\n\n`--pr-created` and `--pr-reviewed` accept complete GitHub PR or GitLab MR URLs.\n\n`--needs-input` requests immediate non-interrupting delivery. `--stuck`\nrequests immediate delivery plus a rate-limited interrupt. Informational work\nbatches for up to one hour, while the first done report opens a fixed five\nminute settlement window.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```bash\nao report \"The focused tests pass; I am checking the generated diff.\"\nao report --done --note \"Ready for review.\" \\\n  --pr-created https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/88\n```\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":12459},"formatted_output":"# ao report\n\nPersist a meaningful worker report for durable delivery to the active project\norchestrator.\n\n## Syntax\n\n```text\nao report <free-form-text>\nao report --checkpoint --note <text> [output flags]\nao report --needs-input --note <text> [output flags]\nao report --stuck --note <text> [output flags]\nao report --done --note <text> [output flags]\n```\n\nOutput flags are repeatable:\n\n```text\n--artifact <opaque-reference>\n--pr-created <pr-or-mr-url>\n--pr-reviewed <pr-or-mr-url>\n```\n\nUse reports for meaningful transitions, decisions, blockers, required input,\noutputs, and terminal judgment. Do not narrate routine commands. Outputs do not\nimply completion, and `--done` does not terminate the session.\n\nAttach a reviewable deliverable as soon as it is ready, not only at `--done`:\nuse `--artifact <reference>` on the report for the milestone that produced it.\nExamples include a requested document, a rendered dashboard, or another output\nthe orchestrator or human needs to open directly. `--artifact` takes any opaque\nreference string; it is not validated as a URL.\nIn a chat session, an HTML file from the artifact directory that you attach\nwith `--artifact` also shows in the thread.\n\nRoutine test logs, command output, scratch notes, and intermediate diagnostics\nare working material, not deliverables. Do not attach them unless requested or\nneeded to explain an actionable failure. Summarize validation in the report note;\nwhen a separate deliverable is useful, prefer one consolidated report over\nindividual logs. Ordinary progress updates and concise final answers do not\nneed separate artifact files.\n\nSaving a local artifact or attaching its reference to an AO report is not\nexternal publishing authorization. Publish externally only within the\nuser-authorized scope.\n\n`--pr-created` and `--pr-reviewed` accept complete GitHub PR or GitLab MR URLs.\n\n`--needs-input` requests immediate non-interrupting delivery. `--stuck`\nrequests immediate delivery plus a rate-limited interrupt. Informational work\nbatches for up to one hour, while the first done report opens a fixed five\nminute settlement window.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```bash\nao report \"The focused tests pass; I am checking the generated diff.\"\nao report --done --note \"Ready for review.\" \\\n  --pr-created https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/88\n```\n"},"started_at_ms":1791835308615,"completed_at_ms":1791835308615}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:01:48.709Z","ordinal":17255,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a131b5-02a5-7ee1-845f-45125eaeed86","call_id":"call_8c4f453eb619480a91efee81e8d0520c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"024992\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000009792,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1115,\"output\":\"![Meet Tally, the CFO for your agent fleet: pixel tally mark on a dark background](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/main/docs/assets/tally-banner.png)\\n\\nTally is a CFO for coding agents: give it GitHub issues and a budget, and it routes, caps and verifies the work before opening pull requests.\\n\\n## Install\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm install -g tally-agents\\n```\\n\\nPublished version: **0.2.1**, checked on npm on 13 October 2026.\\nRequires Node 20+; real work also needs Git, signed-in GitHub CLI and at least\\none signed-in coding agent. Optional integrations are not required.\\n\\n## 60-Second Quick Start\\n\\nFrom your repository root, with open issues carrying your chosen label:\\n\\n```sh\\ntally init\\ntally run --plan\\ntally run --budget 3 --dashboard\\n```\\n\\nInit asks about runner, agents, verification, budget and integrations. Review\\nthe plan before the last command: **it starts paid workers and may push task\\nbranches/open PRs**. Replace `3` with your approved USD run budget. Connection\\nand setup can take longer than a minute; the dashboard serves until Ctrl+C.\\n\\nExcerpt from a real AO run, not the simulated demo:\\n\\n```text\\n#21 attempt 1: passed $0.0126 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/22\\n#20 attempt 1: passed $0.0136 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/23\\n#19 attempt 1: passed $0.0150 https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/24\\nfinished run-20261011-190131Z: 3 tasks, 3 attempts\\nsummary: 3 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; total $0.0411 against run cap $2.00\\n```\\n\\nTry it without accounts or paid workers: `tally demo --dashboard --port 0`.\\nThe seven demo tasks and token usage are scripted, not real savings evidence.\\n\\n## What Tally Does\\n\\n1. **Route:** size tasks and choose configured tiers using confidence, cost\\n   and past outcomes when available.\\n2. **Cap:** reserve budget and meter workers against their attempt ceilings.\\n3. **Escalate:** stop capped/failed work and, when appropriate and affordable,\\n   pass its branch and available checkpoint metadata to a stronger tier.\\n4. **Verify:** independently run your configured repository checks.\\n5. **Open a pull request:** publish verified work with a cost/evidence ledger.\\n   **Tally never merges its task PRs.**\\n\\nBoth the run cap and remaining monthly budget apply. Polling/metering can\\novershoot a ceiling; this is not a provider-side hard billing limit.\\n\\n## Runners and Agents\\n\\n| Runner | Execution | Agents |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Agent Orchestrator (`ao`) | AO manages sessions; opt into parallel workers at init or with `--parallel N` | Claude Code, Codex or configured mixed tiers |\\n| Direct (`direct`) | Tally launches workers itself, one task at a time; no AO daemon needed | Claude Code or Codex, selected per tier |\\n\\nInstall/sign in to every configured harness. Tally never silently substitutes\\none for a missing agent. Login does not prove model entitlement. Claude uses\\na scoped consented allow-list; no runner uses bypass-permissions.\\n[Runner details and proofs](docs/EVIDENCE.md).\\n\\n## Optional Integrations\\n\\n| Product | Adds | When Off or Unavailable |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| neatlogs | Decision/worker traces, read-back evidence, cost/pass-rate history and learned caps keyed by size and actual model | No Tally decision export when off; local history, then explicit priors/config caps. Previously installed global hooks may still trace sessions. |\\n| Entire | Graph sizing, checkpoints, past-failure recall and metadata-only handoff | Repository search sizes tasks; no Entire checkpoints/hosted recall promised. No symbol matches falls back without calling a working graph disconnected. |\\n| cfo.ai | Monthly budget read, reconciled real spend and workspace-shared per-attempt Ari reports when enabled | Local budget/ledger; failed writes retain `cfoai-spend-fallback.csv` for reconciliation. |\\n\\nCredentials stay in their login tools or `~/.tally/`, not the repository.\\nA stored trace ID does not itself prove delivery.\\n\\n## Evidence, Not Promises\\n\\n| Matched Three-Task Pass | Estimated Cost | Final Tasks Passing |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| Every task on the top tier | $1.22 | 3/3 |\\n| Tally v1, built-in priors | $0.31 | 3/3 |\\n| Tally v2, history enabled | $0.43 | 3/3 |\\n\\n**Three tasks, one run each per pass**, same initial commit, list-price token\\nestimates rather than invoices: about 75% and 65% cheaper on that sample. Each\\npass also had three separately recorded startup retries. Only C's large task\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"225d03\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000012459,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":578,\"output\":\"# ao report\\n\\nPersist a meaningful worker report for durable delivery to the active project\\norchestrator.\\n\\n## Syntax\\n\\n```text\\nao report <free-form-text>\\nao report --checkpoint --note <text> [output flags]\\nao report --needs-input --note <text> [output flags]\\nao report --stuck --note <text> [output flags]\\nao report --done --note <text> [output flags]\\n```\\n\\nOutput flags are repeatable:\\n\\n```text\\n--artifact <opaque-reference>\\n--pr-created <pr-or-mr-url>\\n--pr-reviewed <pr-or-mr-url>\\n```\\n\\nUse reports for meaningful transitions, decisions, blockers, required input,\\noutputs, and terminal judgment. Do not narrate routine commands. Outputs do not\\nimply completion, and `--done` does not terminate the session.\\n\\nAttach a reviewable deliverable as soon as it is ready, not only at `--done`:\\nuse `--artifact <reference>` on the report for the milestone that produced it.\\nExamples include a requested document, a rendered dashboard, or another output\\nthe orchestrator or human needs to open directly. `--artifact` takes any opaque\\nreference string; it is not validated as a URL.\\nIn a chat session, an HTML file from the artifact directory that you attach\\nwith `--artifact` also shows in the thread.\\n\\nRoutine test logs, command output, scratch notes, and intermediate diagnostics\\nare working material, not deliverables. Do not attach them unless requested or\\nneeded to explain an actionable failure. Summarize validation in the report note;\\nwhen a separate deliverable is useful, prefer one consolidated report over\\nindividual logs. Ordinary progress updates and concise final answers do not\\nneed separate artifact files.\\n\\nSaving a local artifact or attaching its reference to an AO report is not\\nexternal publishing authorization. Publish externally only within the\\nuser-authorized scope.\\n\\n`--pr-created` and `--pr-reviewed` accept complete GitHub PR or GitLab MR URLs.\\n\\n`--needs-input` requests immediate non-interrupting delivery. `--stuck`\\nrequests immediate delivery plus a rate-limited interrupt. Informational work\\nbatches for up to one hour, while the first done report opens a fixed five\\nminute settlement window.\\n\\n**Examples:**\\n\\n```bash\\nao report \\\"The focused tests pass; I am checking the generated diff.\\\"\\nao report --done --note \\\"Ready for review.\\\" \\\\\\n  --pr-created https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/88\\n```\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","create_time":1791835308.709786}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
