yes|no> Init product opt-ins\n  --verbose         For init: include the full proposed YAML\n  --runner <ao|direct> For init: AO workers or sequential direct workers\n  --harness <claude-code|codex|mixed> For init: coding agent choice (Codex is default)\n  --model-access-fallback-tier <name> For init: override the default cheap-tier fallback\n  --allow-claude     For init: explicitly consent to the printed repository allow-list\n  --output <dir>    Output directory for tally market (default: .tally/market/latest)\n  --limit <number>  Result limit for tally market (default: 10)\n  --keyword <text>  Optional exact description phrase for tally market\n  --max-credits <N> Market estimated credit cap (default: 10); refuses above cap\n  --replay <query.json> Replay cached market snapshot; no API calls\n  --review <json>   Apply human review labels to a cached market snapshot\n  --jobs            Search engineering job posts for explicit coding-tool evidence\n  --secondary <query.json> Include a cached firmographic table in the job report\n                    market --plan checks free account pricing, without a search\n  --out <dir>       New directory for tally publish (required)\n  --runs <ids>      Comma-separated run folder ids (default: all real runs)\n  --run <id>        Run id for traces drain; --output overrides its run directory\n  -h, --help        Show this help\n  -v, --version     Show the version\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":4,"nanos":771134500},"formatted_output":"tally: a CFO for a fleet of coding agents\n\nUsage: tally <command> [options]\n\nCommands:\n  experiment Run baseline and Tally repeats with a shared safety budget\n  run      Run the backlog against the budget in tally.yaml\n  demo     Run the full loop with simulated workers on a sample backlog\n  dashboard Start the local dashboard server\n  init     Set up tally.yaml for the current repository\n  uninstall List and remove the recorded Tally installation\n  doctor   Check that each integration is connected\n  login    Connect an integration, e.g. tally login cfoai\n  market   Find and qualify likely pilot companies with CrustData\n  publish  Write a static dashboard bundle (does not deploy)\n  traces drain --run <id> Drain and read-back verify a finished run's worker traces\n  logo     Replay the Tally logo animation\n\nOptions:\n  --repeats <N>     Repeats per experiment mode (default: 2)\n  --config <path>   Path to tally.yaml (default: tally.yaml)\n  --dry-run         Simulate workers; spends nothing\n  --budget <usd>    Override the budget for this run\n  --only <task>     Run a single task\n  --parallel <N>    Opt into up to N AO workers (default: 1; direct is sequential)\n  --baseline        Send every task to the strongest tier\n  --dashboard       Serve the dashboard before run/demo; keep serving until Ctrl+C\n  --open            Also open the dashboard in the browser\n  --port <number>   Dashboard port (default: 5177; use 0 for any free port)\n  --plan            Size and route tasks, but do not spawn workers\n  --live            For demo: use live read-only integrations with fake workers\n  --yes             Approve init changes or explicitly budgeted paid experiments\n  --test-command <cmd> For init: verification shell command\n  --setup-command <cmd> For init: setup shell command (empty means none)\n  --issue-label <label> For init: GitHub issue label (default: tally)\n  --neatlogs <yes|no> --entire <yes|no> --cfoai <yes|no> Init product opt-ins\n  --verbose         For init: include the full proposed YAML\n  --runner <ao|direct> For init: AO workers or sequential direct workers\n  --harness <claude-code|codex|mixed> For init: coding agent choice (Codex is default)\n  --model-access-fallback-tier <name> For init: override the default cheap-tier fallback\n  --allow-claude     For init: explicitly consent to the printed repository allow-list\n  --output <dir>    Output directory for tally market (default: .tally/market/latest)\n  --limit <number>  Result limit for tally market (default: 10)\n  --keyword <text>  Optional exact description phrase for tally market\n  --max-credits <N> Market estimated credit cap (default: 10); refuses above cap\n  --replay <query.json> Replay cached market snapshot; no API calls\n  --review <json>   Apply human review labels to a cached market snapshot\n  --jobs            Search engineering job posts for explicit coding-tool evidence\n  --secondary <query.json> Include a cached firmographic table in the job report\n                    market --plan checks free account pricing, without a search\n  --out <dir>       New directory for tally publish (required)\n  --runs <ids>      Comma-separated run folder ids (default: all real runs)\n  --run <id>        Run id for traces drain; --output overrides its run directory\n  -h, --help        Show this help\n  -v, --version     Show the version\n"},"started_at_ms":1791835438654,"completed_at_ms":1791835443427}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:04:08.197Z","ordinal":17317,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-42aa5960-b962-4df5-8b88-11c97a735005","process_id":"41504","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","ao report --checkpoint --note 'README, guide and evidence draft ready; verified user learned caps and ledger-source caveats. First suite 881/882 passed, existing init-terminal 4s child timeout failed; rerunning. Typecheck and npm pack audit pass: guide/llms ship, banner excluded. No paid runs.' --artifact docs/AGENT_GUIDE.md --artifact docs/EVIDENCE.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"ao report --checkpoint --note 'README, guide and evidence draft ready; verified user learned caps and ledger-source caveats. First suite 881/882 passed, existing init-terminal 4s child timeout failed; rerunning. Typecheck and npm pack audit pass: guide/llms ship, banner excluded. No paid runs.' --artifact docs/AGENT_GUIDE.md --artifact docs/EVIDENCE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":475115667},"formatted_output":""},"started_at_ms":1791835447720,"completed_at_ms":1791835448195}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:04:08.705Z","ordinal":17318,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a131b7-2580-78d1-91a6-ec7f2dd3e6e4","call_id":"call_cf71c08990c9455da65f1f9ec0adb819","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 24.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"697b24\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.335252292,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1307,\"output\":\"# Tally Evidence and Operational Reference\\n\\nDetailed reference preserved from the former README, updated with the following\\nevidence. Costs are recorded list-price estimates, not invoices. Historical\\ncommands and rates describe their original conditions, not new approvals.\\n\\n## Matched Comparison\\n\\nThree identical tasks at base `565e6ccd757ff794ead643dac7359efe67ec9db2`,\\none run per task/pass, source `9f18111e948a0a7c7e09c99dc86f854ca595e1a8`:\\n\\n| Pass / Run | Estimated USD | Final Verified Tasks |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| All top / run-20261012T104159Z-comparison-A | 1.21693600 | 3/3 |\\n| Priors / run-20261012T105538Z-comparison-B | 0.30932564 | 3/3 |\\n| History enabled / run-20261012T111142Z-comparison-C | 0.42632384 | 3/3 |\\n\\nB/C were 74.58%/64.97% cheaper than A on this sample. Each pass had three\\nzero-token startup retries, separately recorded, not model failures. Two other\\nplanned tasks were not run. C used observed statistics only for the large task\\n(top expectation $1.50 -> about $0.303 from two samples); no tier or cap changed.\\nC cost more than B: no history-driven improvement over priors established.\\nShared history/caching/model variability and one sample per mode prevent\\ncausal/repeatable/general savings claims. cfo.ai was off in these passes.\\nGraph size showed no clear linear cost signal; nine repeated task/pass points\\nare not nine independent task types.\\n\\n## Live Learned Ceilings and Same-Branch Escalation\\n\\nSaved published-0.2.0 user ledgers were read directly on 13 October 2026.\\nThis is ledger evidence, not a new live trace-readback or paid replication.\\n\\n`run-20261012-153240Z`, Othello #4: six successful small/cheap/luna observations\\nfrom neatlogs, 100% recorded pass rate and $0.0111 average cost. P90 x 1.5 set\\ncap **$0.02284986**, below configured $0.30; passed at **$0.01816744** on\\n`ao/Othello-2/root`:\\n[Othello PR #5](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/Othello/pull/5).\\n\\n`run-20261012-162757Z`, self-host #155/#157: six successful small/luna\\nobservations, average $0.0116; learned cap **$0.02725116**, maximum $0.30.\\n\\n| Task | Cheap Cost / Result | Middle Cost / Result | Same Branch | PR |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| #155 | $0.02817828 / stopped | $0.19549280 / passed | ao/tally-selfhost-2/root | [#163](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/163) |\\n| #157 | $0.02770580 / stopped | $0.38153360 / passed | ao/tally-selfhost-1/root | [#162](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/162) |\\n\\nMiddle/terra used configured $0.75 caps, not learned caps. escalatedFrom points\\nto each stopped row; branches match and base commits change to the earlier\\nwork-in-progress commit. Both stopped assessments record kind `ceiling`, source\\n`ledger`, traceId null, no spans and retryable true. Their exact evidence is\\n\\\"Ledger fallback: worker trace could not be read; attempt result stopped\\nclassifies as ceiling.\\\" Both stopped rows contain checkpoint IDs; escalations\\nrecord `entire-handoff`. These files do not establish trace-derived causes or\\nhandoff-context quality. Metering overshoot remains recorded, not clipped.\\nOther self-host tasks #158/#154/#153 passed cheap at $0.06608376/$0.04795676/\\n$0.02753844 with configured medium caps; five PRs #161-165 resulted in total.\\n\\nSeparate configured-cap proof: `run-20261012-100856Z`,\\n[fly-doom-jev PR #17](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/fly-doom-jev/pull/17):\\ncheap cap $0.018, stopped $0.01956044, middle passed $0.16957640; classification\\nalso ledger-derived. A forced configured cap is not a learned cap.\\n\\n## Parallel and Release Sanity\\n\\n`run-20261011-190131Z`: three AO Codex workers overlapped for 70.286 seconds;\\n3/3 passed, $0.04111932 under $2 cap; PRs\\n[22](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/22),\\n[23](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/23),\\n[24](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/24).\\nAll three worker traces read back; one decision trace remained unavailable.\\nOverlap is not continuous simultaneous token generation or a throughput study.\\n\\n0.2.1 `run-20261012-194035Z`, source ceddd6a: two overlapping AO Codex workers,\\n2/2 passed, $0.02483996, PRs\\n[35](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/35) and\\n[36](https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/chip-design-groundup/pull/36).\\nWorker/decision traces read back; cfo.ai spend delta matched the ledger. Entire\\nURLs showed task-specific sessions; neatlogs UI required sign-in. cfo.ai memory\\nreturned extracted facts for both reports, not necessarily complete Markdown.\\nThis sanity used configured caps. Its Entire default-branch linking-settings\\ncommit was separately human-approved.\\n\\n## Preserved Reference\\n\\nA CFO for a fleet of coding agents. Give it a backlog and a budget. It sizes\\neach task, sends it to the cheapest model likely to finish it, stops any task\\nthat overruns its spend ceiling, hands failed work to a stronger model, and\\nends with a ledger tying spend to each attempt, its test result and any opened PR.\\n\\n**Start here: [Getting Started](GETTING_STARTED.md)** covers the no-account demo, every init question, your first real run, troubleshooting and uninstall.\\n\\nStatus: early build. Published npm version checked 13 October 2026 is 0.2.1.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"c5b53d\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.720273334,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"da4727\",\"wall_time_seconds\":5.514814291,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2,\"output\":\"0.2.1\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"db3046\",\"wall_time_seconds\":4.772210458,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":835,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 835)\\nTotal output lines: 55\\n\\ntally: a CFO for a fleet of coding agents\\n\\nUsage: tally <command> [options]\\n\\nCommands:\\n  experiment Run baseline and Tally repeats with a shared safety budget\\n  run      Run the backlog against the budget in tally.yaml\\n  demo     Run the full loop with simulated workers on a sample backlog\\n  dashboard Start the local dashboard server\\n  init     Set up tally.yaml for the current repository\\n  uninstall List and remove the recorded Tally installation\\n  doctor   Check that each integration is connected\\n  login    Connect an integration, e.g. tally login cfoai\\n  market   Find and qualify likely pilot companies with CrustData\\n  publish  Write a static dashboard bundle (does not deploy)\\n  traces drain --run <id> Drain and read-back verify a finished run's worker traces\\n  logo     Replay the Tally logo animation\\n\\nOptions:\\n  --repeats <N>     Repeats per experiment mode (default: 2)\\n  --config <path>   Path to tally.yaml (default: tally.yaml)\\n  --dry-run         Simulate workers; spends nothing…335 tokens truncated…ository allow-list\\n  --output <dir>    Output directory for tally market (default: .tally/market/latest)\\n  --limit <number>  Result limit for tally market (default: 10)\\n  --keyword <text>  Optional exact description phrase for tally market\\n  --max-credits <N> Market estimated credit cap (default: 10); refuses above cap\\n  --replay <query.json> Replay cached market snapshot; no API calls\\n  --review <json>   Apply human review labels to a cached market snapshot\\n  --jobs            Search engineering job posts for explicit coding-tool evidence\\n  --secondary <query.json> Include a cached firmographic table in the job report\\n                    market --plan checks free account pricing, without a search\\n  --out <dir>       New directory for tally publish (required)\\n  --runs <ids>      Comma-separated run folder ids (default: all real runs)\\n  --run <id>        Run id for traces drain; --output overrides its run directory\\n  -h, --help        Show this help\\n  -v, --version     Show the version\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"0758b8\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.47494225,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","create_time":1791835448.704873}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
