{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:04:20.398Z","ordinal":17326,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a131aa-8bd4-7dc0-9e91-8071b2de8f12","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-66d9d5ef-92c1-4227-bd0b-67ad752bcb8a","process_id":"76689","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '595,610p' docs/EVIDENCE.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '595,610p' docs/EVIDENCE.md","name":"EVIDENCE.md","path":"docs/EVIDENCE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"Entire checkpoint records live in separate Git refs, not on the task branch.\nTally keeps the checkpoint ID and native session ID, and attaches a clickable\nEntire session link only when the Entire CLI confirms that the GitHub repo has\na ready mirror. The link opens the session that contains the checkpoint; a\nreviewer still needs access to that repo in Entire. Without a ready mirror,\nTally keeps the checkpoint ID available in the local ledger rather than adding\na link that may not open.\n\nAfter each run has completed its Neatlogs read-back, Tally adds an evidence\nsection to the generated PR body when links are available: Entire session and\ncheckpoint, Neatlogs routing and worker traces, and the configured cfo.ai\nbudget and spend tables. Worker trace links are added only after Tally verifies\ntheir read-back. These dashboard links use the viewer's existing account\naccess; Tally does not publish public trace shares.\n\nTally assumes nothing about the repository it works on. The repository, test\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Entire checkpoint records live in separate Git refs, not on the task branch.\nTally keeps the checkpoint ID and native session ID, and attaches a clickable\nEntire session link only when the Entire CLI confirms that the GitHub repo has\na ready mirror. The link opens the session that contains the checkpoint; a\nreviewer still needs access to that repo in Entire. Without a ready mirror,\nTally keeps the checkpoint ID available in the local ledger rather than adding\na link that may not open.\n\nAfter each run has completed its Neatlogs read-back, Tally adds an evidence\nsection to the generated PR body when links are available: Entire session and\ncheckpoint, Neatlogs routing and worker traces, and the configured cfo.ai\nbudget and spend tables. Worker trace links are added only after Tally verifies\ntheir read-back. These dashboard links use the viewer's existing account\naccess; Tally does not publish public trace shares.\n\nTally assumes nothing about the repository it works on. The repository, test\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":13917},"formatted_output":"Entire checkpoint records live in separate Git refs, not on the task branch.\nTally keeps the checkpoint ID and native session ID, and attaches a clickable\nEntire session link only when the Entire CLI confirms that the GitHub repo has\na ready mirror. The link opens the session that contains the checkpoint; a\nreviewer still needs access to that repo in Entire. Without a ready mirror,\nTally keeps the checkpoint ID available in the local ledger rather than adding\na link that may not open.\n\nAfter each run has completed its Neatlogs read-back, Tally adds an evidence\nsection to the generated PR body when links are available: Entire session and\ncheckpoint, Neatlogs routing and worker traces, and the configured cfo.ai\nbudget and spend tables. Worker trace links are added only after Tally verifies\ntheir read-back. These dashboard links use the viewer's existing account\naccess; Tally does not publish public trace shares.\n\nTally assumes nothing about the repository it works on. The repository, test\n"},"started_at_ms":1791835460398,"completed_at_ms":1791835460398}}
